URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/sunday-workshops-with-serpentina-n
 orth/
SUMMARY:Sunday Workshops with Serpentina North!
DESCRIPTION:The Thrill of Zills\n1-2pmJoin musician\, producer\, and multi-
 decade international dancer instructor/performer Jim Boz/JMBZ for an inten
 sely\, rhythmically\, and noisy opinion-filled intensive in the joys\, fru
 strations\, teks\, &amp\; clangs of working with finger cymbals both as a 
 musical instrument and an integral part of the western expression of raks 
 sharki\, belly dance\, and related dance styles.We will begin with basic t
 echniques including tonality\, and some basic drills to get us moving befo
 re launching into performance techniques\, applications (when to cymbal\, 
 when to shut the hell up)\, and advanced tonal techniques. Knowledge of ba
 sic Middle Eastern rhythms is not required\, but is essential to success.Y
 ou will be required to bring your own quality set of finger cymbals with p
 roperly fitted elastic. You will receive mp3 tracks created by Jim Boz for
  practice\, including tracks with a slowly increasing tempo to build speed
  and muscle memory. These tracks will be emailed to you\, or please bring 
 a USB memory stick (PC formatted).Funky Combos for Duets\n2-3pmThis one ho
 ur workshop with troupe director\, Orkideh\, is designed for dynamic duet 
 combinations to integrate into your dance repertoire. Geared towards inter
 mediate dancers\, we will have a yoga-based warmup\, talk about technique 
 and tribal posture while pairing up to dance together.Tribal experience is
  helpful but not necessary.$25 per workshop\, $45 for both\nWant to join t
 hese with a friend?\n$40 for both of you (per workshop) or $80 for both.ht
 tp://www.serpentinatribal.com Sunday Workshops with Serpentina North!
