URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/advanced-dunham-workshop/
SUMMARY:Advanced Dunham Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Ballet Creole Presents...Advanced Dance Workshops with\nCanada'
 s ONLY certified Dunham Instructor!Join Ballet Creole's Artistic Director 
 Patrick Parson (M.A\; BFA) for a monthly workshop exploring the technique 
 of dance pioneer\, Katherine (Katherine the Great) Dunham\, the "matriarch
  and queen mother of black dance".Ms. Dunham’s anthropological studies i
 n Africa and the Caribbean yielded a dance technique that draws from class
 ical ballet as well as traditional African/Caribbean movement\, forging a 
 cultural link between Africa and North America. Her technique has inspired
  many Black choreographers and dance artists throughout the world includin
 g Alvin Ailey\, Talley Beatty\, Lavinia Williams\, and our very own Artist
 ic Director\, Patrick Parson. Mr. Parson has been recognized for using thi
 s technique to train technically strong\, versatile dancers through the Ba
 llet Creole Company and PTP (now PTAP).Advanced and Professional Dancers a
 re invited to join us to learn this dynamic technique which is little know
 n and practiced in Canada.Fee: $25/class or pre-register at www.balletcreo
 le.org and save.Location: 101 Portland Street\, Etobicoke ON - South of Th
 e Queensway\, off Royal York RoadFall Workshop Schedule:\nNovember - Tuesd
 ay November 17th\, 7 - 8:30pm\nDecember - Tuesday December 15th\, 7 - 8:30
 pm Advanced Dunham Workshop
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2015/12/ESS_IMG_12540_iNOcyb.jpg
