URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/intermediate-kizomba/
SUMMARY:Intermediate Kizomba
DESCRIPTION:Don’t let the party stop!!!Back by demand and your support\, 
 we are bringing a continuation of our popular kizomba course with David Es
 pinosa &amp\; Tania Wong!David &amp\; Tania are dedicated to help grow the
  kizomba scene in Toronto and spread our love of the dance at its roots by
  strengthening your foundation in kizomba while adding some tricks to your
  dancing.Kizomba comes from Angola\, means “party”\, and have been tak
 ing the world by storm in the last few years as a romantic music that catc
 hes the ear and as a sensual dance that captivates the soul. Kizomba\, whi
 ch was derived from Semba\, has taken on many influences and allows each d
 ancer to develop their own style based on their own dance backgrounds and 
 preferences. Also\, other styles can be incorporated into your dance and a
 dd to your musicality.Content includes but not limited to:\nIntricate patt
 erns/tricks and musicality\, Introduction to SembaTime: Thurs 8:45pm-10:15
 pm\nFees: $135+hst (total 9 hrs over 6 weeks)\nDROP IN WELCOMED but basics
  of kizomba recommended! :DAbout David Espinosa:\n************************
 ***\nA passionate and versatile dancer from Peru. He started his Kizomba &
 amp\; Semba training with local artists Pedro Moreira Goncalves\, Nico Kru
 mp and Marc Brewer. From there\, he further polished his style by travelli
 ng to France\, Spain\, England and the Netherlands and trained with world 
 reknown artists such as Isabel &amp\; Felicien\, Albir &amp\; Sara\, Mr. T
 ecas &amp\; Miss Jo\, Fabricio &amp\; Sabrina\, Eddy Vents &amp\; Lucia\, 
 etc. just to name a few here.Since 2013\, David is the only male semba tea
 cher in Ontario trained in Europe and\, he is one of the pioneers of Kizom
 ba in Toronto\, first as part of the GoDanz Taxi Dancer Team and recently 
 as the founder of “Amigos do Semba”. Intermediate Kizomba
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2016/01/ESS_IMG_12739_mSvdx0.jpg
