 -fringe-festival/
SUMMARY:Exterminating Angel at the Toronto Fringe Festival
DESCRIPTION:$12 CASH ONLY AT THE DOOR | $14 IN ADVANCE |\n(ON SALE ONLINE/B
 Y PHONE AS OF JUNE 9TH)\nwww.fringetoronto.com/exterminating-angel\n\nAN A
 THLETIC AND EMOTIONAL PIECE OF DANCE THEATRE – explores high stakes\, an
 imal instinct and humanity stripped of all social pretence as part of Toro
 nto Fringe 2016.\n\nInspired by Luis Buñuel’s surrealist film of the sa
 me name\, EXTERMINATING ANGEL is an intensely physical and theatrical cont
 emporary dance work. When a group of dinner guests find themselves psychol
 ogically trapped\, the pomp and formality of their social event dissolves 
 into hostility and hysteria.\n\nWith choreography by Alysa Pires and an or
 iginal score by Adam Sakiyama\, "Exterminating Angel" features some of Tor
 onto’s most exciting dance artists including Dora Nominee Ryan Lee\, Kel
 ly Shaw\, Colleen Snell\, James-Thomas Papandreos\, Andrea Gregorio\, Dami
 an Norman\, Matthew Vautour\, Sierra Chin Sawdy\, and Michaela Reichenbach
 .\n\n&nbsp\; Exterminating Angel at the Toronto Fringe Festival
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2016/06/ESS_IMG_13546_m7L7BZ.jpg
