SUMMARY:Dusk Dances 2016
DESCRIPTION:In its 22nd season\, Dusk Dances is an enchanting outdoor dance
  festival that brings high quality urban\, contemporary and traditional da
 nce to Withrow Park. Audiences are invited to enjoy works by top Canadian 
 choreographers and participate in free nia dance classes. An event for all
  ages! Bring your chairs and blankets\, and get ready for a breathtaking e
 vening of live performances!When: Aug 1 - Aug 7\, 2016Nightly Performances
 : Monday\, August 1st to Sunday\, August 7th\n-Opening band and nia class 
 at 7:00 pm\n-Dance performances at 7:30 pmDaytime Performances: Thursday\,
  August 4th and Sunday\, August 7th:\n-Opening band and nia class at 2:00p
 m\n-Dance performances at 2:30 pm\n**Thursday and Sunday will have both da
 ytime and evening performancesPrice: Pay-What-You-Can (suggested contribut
 ion $10.00)Schedule:\nFree nia class by master teacher Martha Randall\nOpe
 ning band – DoubleTooth\nHosted by Allegra CharlestonPerformances:\nPas 
 à trois by Myriam Allard (La Otra Orilla)\nThis Is How We Love by Susie B
 urpee\nHeyKloro by Apolonia Velsquez and Ofilio Sinbadinho (Gadfly Dance C
 ompany)\nWaves by Michael CaldwellSpecial 30 minute performance:\nAuto-Fic
 tion by Milan Gervais (Human Playground)More info: www.duskdances.ca or fe
 el free to email info@duskdances.ca and check out us on facebook! Dusk Dan
 ces 2016
