URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/sara-does-a-solo/
SUMMARY:Sara does a Solo
DESCRIPTION:A vibrant interplay of fact and fantasy\, contemporary dance an
 d comedy\, Sara does a Solo blends storytelling\, singing\, dance\, poetry
 \, puppetry\, video\, costume and character into a poignant and passionate
  account of life as an artist and a parent. Prompted by a chance encounter
  (and performance) with renowned singer Mary Margaret O’Hara\, Sara pres
 ents a fearless account of what we all face – an aging body and a reflec
 tive mind.\n\nCelebrated for her “daring imagination” (Toronto Star) a
 nd being “wickedly funny” (Dance International)\, Sara Porter is back 
 onstage with Sara does a Solo. Fresh from appearances in Montreal\, New Yo
 rk City\, and San Francisco International Arts Festival\, Sara does a Solo
  is unlike anything else. Part memoir\, part stand-up comedy\, part dance 
 performance\, her stories blend intimacy and pathos\, hilarity and beauty.
  A bold and beautiful account of mid-life.\n\n“Refreshingly candid… em
 otionally mesmerizing and deliciously fun!” Niegel Smith\, Director\, Fl
 ea Theatre\, NYC.\n\n&nbsp\;\n\n&nbsp\; Sara does a Solo
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2016/06/ESS_IMG_13643_PU1cEr.jpg
