SUMMARY:African Dance Workshops with guest Fara Tolno
DESCRIPTION:African Dance and drum like you've never experienced it before!
 \n\nFARA TOLNO will share traditional African drum and dance from Guinea\,
  West Africa.\n\nSUN OCT 2:\n12-2pm | Drum class - All levels\ndjembes or 
 dunduns available upon email request\n\ncash only: $25\n\nEcole de Djembe\
 n243 Gerrard St E.Toronto.ON\nSAT OCT 8:\n2 30-4pm | Dance - Beginner leve
 l\n4 15-5 45pm | Dance - Int &amp\; Adv Levels\n\ncash only:\n$20 | 1 Danc
 e class\n$36 | 2 Dance classes\n\n-Bring comfortable clothes.\n\n918 Bathu
 rst\, The Great Hall\n918 Bathurst St E.Toronto.ON\n\ninfo | private class
  | drum request: shayenneproductions@gmail.com\nsite: luashayenne.com\n\nF
 ARA TOLNO was born in Guinea\, West Africa. He's now based in Colorado\, U
 S. He spent nine years as the lead drummer for Les Merveilles de Guinea (T
 he Wonders of Guinea) under the tutelage of West Africa’s most influenti
 al director and choreographer\, Kemoko Sano. Fara is the founder\, directo
 r\, and choreographer for Kissidugu\, his percussion and dance theatre ens
 emble &amp\; Project Drum\,. Fara has performed with Mamady Keita\, Burnin
 g Spear\, Neil Young\, Sekouba Bambino\, Otis Taylor\, Joe Cocker\, Yousso
 u N’Dour\, Salif Keita Habibe Koite\, B.B. King\, Oumou Sangare\, &amp\;
  many more… African Dance Workshops with guest Fara Tolno
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2016/09/website-FaraWorkshop-OCT2016_Oct28.jpg
CATEGORIES:African
LOCATION:Ecole de Djembe\, 243 Gerrard St E.Toronto.ON \, Toronto\, Ontario
 \, M6C 2M2\, Toronto\, Canada
