URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/musical-theatre-workshop/
SUMMARY:Musical Theatre Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Join us as we welcome Broadway dancer and rehearsal director Mi
 chael Jablonski\, in this special 3-part Musical Theatre workshop. Michael
  will be bringing his extensive Broadway experience to the studio as he wi
 ll teach you original Broadway choreography over the course of the worksho
 p. Q&amp\;A and Audition tips will also be included.\n\nThis is a one time
  chance to learn from and industry professional!\n\nSundays\nNovember 13 -
  27\n10:30am - 12pm\n\n$30 +hst Single Class\n$75 +hst Full 3 Week Worksho
 p\n\nThis is a registered class for adults only. Space is limited and stud
 ents must pre register to confirm a spot in the class. Registration is bas
 ed on a first come\, first serve basis. Your spot may be lost if you do no
 t attend the first class. Please be aware of our refund\, registration and
  general studio policies before registering for your class.\n\nMichael Jab
 lonski - Musical Theatre Dance\n\nMichael has been a successful musical th
 eatre dancer for over 20 years. He has taken his experience on the stage a
 nd transitioned it into the classroom where he has taught master classes f
 or many universities and dance centers across the globe.\n\nMichael is cur
 rently residing as the Dance Captain of the Toronto and National Touring c
 ompany of the hit Broadway show Matilda. He was part of the original cast 
 of the Original Broadway production of Cry-Baby. Michael understudied and 
 performed the role of Riff in the most recent Broadway revival of West Sid
 e Story. He was part of the Broadway cast of The Book of Mormon and went o
 n to perform in both national touring companies. Michael toured the world 
 with 8 different National Tours including Matilda\, The Book of Mormon\, W
 est Side Story (50th Anniversary world tour)\, Saturday Night Fever\, Doct
 or Dolittle\, The Best Little Whorehouse in Texas starring Ann-Margret\, V
 ictor/Victoria\, and Brigadoon. Michael performed 4 years with the Radio C
 ity Rockette’s in the Christmas Spectacular at Radio City Music Hall. On
  film\, he can be seen as a featured dancer in the movie version of The Pr
 oducers starring Matthew Broderick and Nathan Lane.\n\nMichael has perform
 ed at many prestigious theatre’s across the United States including Good
 speed Opera House\, Pioneer Theatre Company\, LaJolla Playhouse\, Pittsbur
 gh Civic Light Opera\, Seattle’s 5th Avenue Theatre\, Kansas City Starli
 ght\, Stages St. Louis\, Sacramento Music Circus\, Houston Theatre Under T
 he Stars\, Flatrock Playhouse\, Riverside Theatre\, North Shore Music Thea
 tre\, Forestburgh Playhouse\, Atlanta Theatre of The Stars\, Theatre by Th
 e Sea\, and Austin Musical Theatre.\n\nMichael has a Bachelor of Arts from
  SUNY at Buffalo and has been a Guest Lecturer and Master Instructor of da
 nce &amp\; Musical Theatre audition technique at many Universities and aca
 demic programs across the U.S and Canada. He has taught at Shenandoah Univ
 ersity\, University at Buffalo\, University of Texas\, University of Utah\
 , Sacramento Music Circus Summer Intensive program\, and Stages St. Louis 
 Young artists program.\n\nOn the creative side Michael has assisted David 
 Marquez in the Pre-Broadway Workshop of The Adventures of Tom Sawyer that 
 opened at The Minskoff Theater on Broadway. He also created additional cho
 reography for the National Tour of The Best Little Whorehouse in Texas sta
 rring Ann-Margret. Michael recently assisted Karen Azenberg for her musica
 l staging of Les Miserables at Pioneer Theatre Company in Salt Lake City. 
 He has also supervised 4 national tours and multiple regional productions 
 as their Dance Captain.\n\nMichael is a member of Canadian Actors Equity A
 ssociation\, American Actors Equity Association\, American Guild of Variet
 y Artists\, and the Screen Actor’s Guild. Musical Theatre Workshop
