SUMMARY:Twelfth Night Historical Supper and Dance
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, January 7\n\nTwelfth Night Traditions: Supper and Da
 nce Party at Historic Montgomery's Inn\n\nOn the twelfth day of Christmas.
 ..\n\nStep into the atmosphere of times gone by. Partake in the Yuletide c
 ustoms of Old England — dance by the fire to live music\, eat a deliciou
 s historical supper with wassail and other seasonal treats\, play traditio
 nal games and enjoy the historic Inn by candlelight\, in all its festive d
 ecorations.\n\nAll dances will be taught and led. No dance experience or p
 artner are needed (and there is no lead or follow)\, but the dance worksho
 p is required for people newer to English Country Dancing and will help ev
 eryone enjoy the evening to the fullest.\n\n3.30 - 5 – Dance workshop (r
 equired for people newer to English Country Dancing)\n5 – 6.30 – Dress
 ing\, carol-singing &amp\; games\n6.30 – 8 – Supper\n8 - 10.30 – Dan
 cing to live music\, with light refreshments served during the break\n\nDr
 ess: historical and festive modern clothing all most welcome.\n\nTickets a
 re 60\, 50 for youth\, students and seniors. Space is limited\, and must b
 e booked by January 5. The registration form and other details can be foun
 d on www.JaneAustenDancing.ca\, or you can phone (416) 578-1031. Twelfth N
 ight Historical Supper and Dance
