 /
SUMMARY:Noisy at Winchester Street Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Dance Theatre presents NOISY\,\na new work by Ame Hende
 rson with Robin Dann &amp\; Matt Smith for TDT\n\nAme Henderson returns to
  TDT in a continuation of the experimental trajectory that drove her Dora-
 nominated work Henderson / Castle: voyager. Noisy questions the silent pre
 sence of the dancer. How does the dance change when the dancer is responsi
 ble for creating both movement and song in an always-emerging counterpoint
 ? Noisy resists a predetermined arc\, insisting\, rather\, on a radical ne
 gotiation of time\, movement and melody in a dance of un-muted bodies.\n\n
 Created in partnership with musicians Matt Smith and Robin Dann\, lighting
  designer Simon Rossiter\, costume designer Claudia Fancello and performer
 s Valerie Calam\, Alana Elmer\, Yuichiro Inoue\, Justin de Luna\, Pulga Mu
 chochoma\, James Phillips and Christianne Ullmark.\n\nJan 26 – 29 + Feb 
 1 – 4\nat the Winchester Street Theatre\,\n80 Winchester St\, Toronto\n\
 nTICKETS: Adult $25 | Student/Senior $20\nBOX OFFICE: 416-967-1365 or http
 ://www.tdt.org/buy-tickets/ Noisy at Winchester Street Theatre
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2017/01/TDT-2017-NOISY-poster-500-lores.jpg
CATEGORIES:Other
LOCATION:Winchester Street Theatre\, 80 Winchester Street\, Toronto\, Ontar
 io\, M4X 1B2\, GTA\, Canada
GEO:43.666302;-79.367203
