URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/urbancommercial-pre-professional-t
 raining-program-school-of-groove/
SUMMARY:School of Groove Urban/Commercial Pre-Professional Training Program
DESCRIPTION:Applications are open now! www.schoolofgroove.ca/apply\n\n*We a
 re happy to answer any and all questions you may have! Fill out the "More 
 Info" form.\n\nWhat is SOG?\n\nSchool Of Groove is a dance training and me
 ntorship program dedicated to nurturing strong and confident young female 
 dancers. We act as a bridge – connecting dancers to like minded peers\, 
 mentors and the larger dance community. Our mission lies in giving emergin
 g talent a holistic approach to the learning experience and the tools they
  need in order to refine their practice and find success on their personal
  dance journey.\n\nOur 3 month long program uses urban and commercial danc
 e techniques as a means to provide you with the skills and mindset to help
  you accomplish your personal dance goals\, all while keeping the female v
 oice in mind. Our school-of-thought focuses on an in-depth understanding a
 nd application of the SOG pillars: music\, movement\, style\, empowerment.
 \n\n 	Limited class sizes &amp\; personalized attention\n 	structured curr
 iculum\n 	technical and artistic enrichment\n 	guest workshops\n 	professi
 onal development\n 	and more...\n\nWho can apply?\n\n 	ages 15-30 years ol
 d\n 	identify as female\n 	previous dance training an asset (formal or inf
 ormal)\n 	able to commit to full 3 month program (Sundays 3-6pm\, Sept 10-
 Dec 3rd)\n 	must have strong work ethic\, team mentality and desire to gro
 w\n\n----------------------------------------\nMore info: www.schoolofgroo
 ve.ca\nApply now: www.schoolofgroove.ca/application\n\nUnder direction of 
 Queenie Seguban and Kelly Gammie of @deucendip dance crew.\n\nDeadline: Ju
 ly 15\, 2016 (11:59pm) School of Groove Urban/Commercial Pre-Professional 
 Training Program
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2017/04/SOGLogo.jpg
