URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/canadian-contemporary-dance-theatr
 e-presents-serious-games/
SUMMARY:Canadian Contemporary Dance Theatre Presents Serious Games
DESCRIPTION:Highlights include a premiere by NYC’s Jennifer Archibald\, D
 avid Earle’s classic Serious Games\, August by José Limón Dance Compan
 y Artistic Director Colin Connor and Deborah Lundmark’s Rain Horse\, fea
 turing live performance by harmonica maestro Carlos del Junco and The Blue
 s Mongrels trio.\n\nLaunched in 1980\, Canadian Contemporary Dance Theatre
  performs one of Canada’s most diverse repertoires by leading internatio
 nal choreographers and has staged more than one thousand performances from
  Barrie to Beijing.\n\nThe company performed at New York City’s storied 
 Joyce Theater for the International Dance Festival celebrating the José L
 imón Company’s 70th Anniversary and represented Canada at the Commonwea
 lth Youth Dance Festival in Glasgow\, Scotland.\n\nOther highlights includ
 e appearances at Toronto’s Princess of Wales and Royal Alexandra Theatre
 s\, tours to Singapore\, Malaysia and China\, and five invitations to the 
 Canada Dance Festival.\n\n&nbsp\;\nAbout Choreographer Jennifer Archibald\
 nJennifer is a Unionville High School Alumnus and the New Resident Canadi
 an Choreographer of the Cincinnati Ballet  .  A graduate of the Alvin A
 iley School and the Maggie Flanigan Acting Conservatory where she speciali
 zed in the Meisner technique\, she brings a variety of experience and styl
 es to Cincinnati Ballet.\n\nIn addition to choreographic work for Cincinna
 ti Ballet\, she has also been commissioned by Atlanta Ballet\, Ballet Memp
 his\, Ailey II\, Kansas City Ballet\, Tulsa Ballet\, and has worked commer
 cially for brands such as Tommy Hilfiger\, Nike and MAC Cosmetics\, as wel
 l as chart-listed singers and actors.\n\nJennifer says of her commission\,
  “We live in a world of noise. At what point are we free enough to allow
  our thoughts to go below surface level. Our body is constantly communicat
 ing with us\; silently but powerfully. Do we listen to it? It takes great 
 patience and insight to understand the language of the world and how to li
 sten to our hearts. It is we alone who determine whether we find our perso
 nal treasure and fulfill whatever our destiny is.”\n\n“The evening’s
  most driving\, well executed movement came from New York’s Jennifer Arc
 hibald and her Arch Dance Company.” Washington Post\n\nMore about Jennif
 er WWW.JENNIFERARCHIBALD.COM\n\n&nbsp\; Canadian Contemporary Dance Theatr
 e Presents Serious Games
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2017/05/SeriousGamesFBheader.jpg
CATEGORIES:Contemporary
LOCATION:Fleck Dance Theatre\, Harbourfront Centre\, 207 Queens Quay West\,
  Toronto\, Ontario\, M5J1A7\, GTA\, Canada
GEO:43.639301;-79.380898
