URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/sharing-dance-day/
SUMMARY:Sharing Dance Day at Dundas Square
DESCRIPTION:Canada's National Ballet School and partners invite you to join
  the nation’s biggest dance party to celebrate Canada’s 150th with …
  Sharing Dance Canada 2017!\nSharing Dance Day Schedule:\n\n 	12-2pm: As a
  field trip destination\, Sharing Dance Day for children and youth will ho
 st free\, open dance workshops and performances by both professional and s
 tudent dance groups. It’s a can’t-miss event for schools!\n 	2-4pm: Ta
 ke part with the young-at-heart as they get their groove on! Join free\, o
 pen dance workshops for all\, and watch performances by some of Toronto's 
 most active seniors’ groups.\n 	4-6pm: Witness a community come together
  to perform the Sharing Dance Canada 2017 choreography. The evening wouldn
 't be complete without spectacular workshops and performances. Stay tuned 
 for a full list of performers!\n\nThis exciting event will include:\n\n 	C
 ommunity performance presentations of the 2017 choreography\n 	Community p
 articipants and partner organizations will perform the choreography in fro
 nt of a large public crowd multiple times over the course of the event\; h
 undreds of dancers expected at each Signature Official Event\n 	Free open 
 dance classes reflecting various dance forms\n 	Professional dance perform
 ances\n 	Partner activity booths\n 	Activities will engage the whole famil
 y\n 	An MC and other special guests\n 	Social media activation\n 	 Videog
 rapher to capture the event\n\nThis year\, four Canadian choreographers ha
 ve collaborated to give voice and movement to a unique work that embodies 
 and celebrates Canada’s diversity and artistic identity. Choreographers 
 include Kimberley Cooper (Calgary)\, Eugene Baffoe (Winnipeg)\, Tracee Smi
 th (Toronto) and Roger Sinha (Montreal).\n\nLearn more at sharingdance.ca 
 about how to join FREE dance rehearsals leading up to our June 2nd event a
 t Yonge and Dundas Square. Bring your friends\, family\, and neighbors and
  DANCE! Sharing Dance Day at Dundas Square
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2017/05/instagram-1080x1080px-English.jpg
