SUMMARY:Breakin' Convention Toronto Masterclass: Soweto Skeleton Movers
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Breakin' Convention for a Masterclass with Soweto Sk
 eleton Movers (South Africa)!\nInstructors: Jabulani\, Junior\, Topollo\, 
 Molefi\, Lerato\nStyle: Pantsula\nClass Description: In Soweto in the 1950
 s\, commuters developed a dance style known as isparapara inspired by thei
 r jumping on and off of moving trains. This was mixed with tap dance and l
 ater became known as Pantsula. More than a dance\, Pantsula is a lifestyle
 . Influences can be seen in jazz\, breaking\, popping\, house and bone bre
 aking.\nThe first half will focus on footwork and body movement and the se
 cond half will focus on the spoti (similar to the bucket hat) and a range 
 of tricks and movements using the hat. A rare opportunity to learn Pantsul
 a from some of South Africa’s leading practitioners in their first ever 
 Canadian workshop.\nThis class is open to all levels of dancers. Breakin&#
 039\; Convention Toronto Masterclass: Soweto Skeleton Movers
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2017/06/https-2F2Fcdn.evbuc_.com2Fimages2F319856502F1732362290352F12Forigi
 nal.jpg
