SUMMARY:Porch View Dances
DESCRIPTION:PORCH VIEW DANCES\nReal people dancing in real spaces\nConceive
 d by Karen Kaeja and further developed with Allen Kaeja\n\nPorch View Danc
 es: Real People Dancing In Real Spaces (PVD) is an award-winning community
  dance event that engages everyday people as creators\, storytellers and p
 erformers – many of whom have never danced before. Audience members trav
 el from house to house to see new dance works created with professional ch
 oreographers and performed by local families on the porches and front yard
 s of their own homes.\n\nLed by a tour guide through the winding streets o
 f Seaton Village\, audiences watch as the stories of the neighborhood unfo
 ld through music and dance. The event ends in Vermont Square Park where th
 e audience members are invited to participate in a gentle group dance know
 n as a Flock Landing\, welcoming to all ages\, skill levels and abilities!
 \n\nPrice: pay-what-you-can\n\nChoreographers:\nAllison Cummings\, Yvonne 
 NG Peck Wan\, Karen Kaeja\, Allen Kaeja\, Lua Shayenne\n\nCommunity Hosts:
 \nBasecamp Climbing\, Karma Food Co-op\, Park People\, Toronto Public Libr
 ary\, St. Alban's Boys &amp\; Girls Club\n\nFunders:\nTD Bank Group\, Cana
 da Council for the Arts\, Ontario Arts Council\, Ontario Trillium Foundati
 on\, Toronto Arts Council\, Arts In The Parks\, Bulmash-Seigel Fund\, Metc
 alf Foundation\n\nSpecial thank you to the Toronto Police Services for ens
 uring our audiences and participants are safe throughout the run of the ev
 ent! Porch View Dances
