URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/butoh-dance/
SUMMARY:Butoh Dance Workshop with Yesenia Fuentes
DESCRIPTION:“Dance is ‘a realization of one’s dream through the body
 ’. [It is]\n‘a work of making the mental imagination into a concrete p
 icture through the body’. We must be able to draw various pictures with 
 our bodies.”\n– Masaki Iwana\n\nWe are delighted to welcome Yesenia Fu
 entes\, a Montreal based Butoh dance artist and teacher\, join us in Toron
 to to instruct a two day Butoh workshop. Yesenia is a choreographer\, an i
 nterpreter\, and a performing artist whose practice mainly draws from the 
 techniques and fundamentals of Butoh. Yesenia has studied with Masaki Iwan
 a\, and Moeno Wakatmasu\, bringing their influence to her numerous solo pe
 rformances and students.\n\nThis workshop will be held on Saturday and Sun
 day\, August 19-20 at 12-4 pm each day. It will be followed by an evening 
 of performance on Sunday\, August 20th. The cost for both days is $80\, wh
 ich includes free entry to the performance night venue. It will fill up fa
 st\; you are invited! Registration open June 15.\n\nButoh is a form of Ja
 panese dance theatre that encompasses a diverse range of activities\, tech
 niques and motivations for dance\, performance\, or movement.\n\nSaturday\
 , August 19 12-4pm\nSunday\, August 20 12-4pm Butoh Dance Workshop with Ye
 senia Fuentes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2017/06/butoh-dance-workshop.jpg
CATEGORIES:Asian,Butoh,Other
LOCATION:Arraymusic\, 155 Walnut Ave\, TORONTO\, CA-ON\, CA-ON\, Canada
GEO:43.6442425;-79.40994339999997
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=155 Walnut Ave\, TORONTO\, 
 CA-ON\, CA-ON\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Arraymusic:geo:43.644242
 5,-79.40994339999997
END:VEVENT
