BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Toronto Dance
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/
UID:1919@torontodance.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20170820T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20170820T210000
DTSTAMP:20190112T203132Z
URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/sonic-fabulations/
SUMMARY:Sonic Fabulations
DESCRIPTION:An evening of dance and music performances.\ntimes:\n\n 	7:00-7
 :30 Free and Improvised\n 	7:40-8:00 Yesenia Fuentes "körper"\n 	8:10-8:4
 0 Fleshtone Aura with dancer Alana Elmer\n 	8:50-9:00 bodiesofwonder  "wa
 ter walk" (to be confirmed)\n\n**scheduled times are approximations\n\n$10
  at door\n\n+++Free and Improvised is a Toronto grown collaboration of exp
 erimental Jazz musicians\, consisting of Daria Morgacheva keys\, synths\, 
 Janine Wright on vocals\, Tal Davidson bass\, Stuart Mein on drums &amp\; 
 Stefan Haynes flute\, sax.\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/freeandimprovised/\
 n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vvQYb7-0NJo\n\n+++Yesenia Fuentes is pe
 rforming "körper." A woman subjected by its environment\, a spasmodic and
  almost agonizing struggle of a body that gradually seeks to reshape itsel
 f\, a moment of contained intensity… Körper is tension and strength but
  it is also exposure.\n\nYesenia is a choreographer\, interpreter\, and pe
 rforming artist whose practice mainly draws from the techniques and fundam
 entals of Butoh. Yesenia seeks to question the absurdity and hollowness of
  certain dynamics of the contemporary world while reflecting more broadly 
 on existence and the human condition.\n\nhttps://www.yeseniafuentes.com/\n
 \nhttps://vimeo.com/147385000\n\n+++Alana Elmer grew up on a farm just nor
 th of Toronto. She graduated from STDT in 2002 and has been a member of To
 ronto Dance Theatre since 2005. Independent from the company she has worke
 d with Paul Andre Fortier\, Deborah Hay and has appeared in numerous film 
 and television shows. Alana also works as a costume designer and is the Co
 -owner of the vintage booth Arsenic and Old Lace located in lovely Lesliev
 ille.\n\nFleshtone Aura is the solo sound-collage alias of Andrew Zukerman
 . Using new &amp\; antiquated technologies he weaves a sonic tapestry that
 's equal parts high &amp\; low-brow\, wet &amp\; dry\, dumb &amp\; dumber.
  Fleshtone Aura rose from the ashes of Gastric Female Reflex\, an equally 
 untethered sound collage duo that lasted a long time. As a solo artist he 
 has released perhaps too many albums and played too many shows to talk abo
 ut.\n\nThis performance evening is an extension of BUTOH workshop with Mon
 treal artist Yesenia Fuentes.\nImage by Jen Bolt Sonic Fabulations
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2017/08/20728762_10154739790537109_6060474348974129522_o.jpg
CATEGORIES:Asian,Butoh
LOCATION:Arraymusic\, 155 Walnut Ave\, TORONTO\, CA-ON\, CA-ON\, Canada
GEO:43.6442425;-79.40994339999997
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=155 Walnut Ave\, TORONTO\, 
 CA-ON\, CA-ON\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Arraymusic:geo:43.644242
 5,-79.40994339999997
END:VEVENT
