SUMMARY:Dancing on the Pier with Shelley Saxena
DESCRIPTION:This is Dancing on the Pier's last event of the summer.\n\nShel
 ley Saxena has danced\, studied and competed in West Coast Swing for 18 y
 ears and is now competing at Rising Star level. Currently she teaches gr
 oup classes and private lessons in West Coast Swing across the GTA.\n\n
 [caption id="attachment_18485" align="aligncenter" width="708"] Shelley Sa
 xena with Steven James.[/caption]\n\nOriginally branching off from the tra
 ditional swing dance Lindy Hop\, West Coast Swing is an an urban\, smooth\
 , and modern style of swing. It has been featured on popular dance progra
 ms such as So You Think You Can Dance and Dancing With The Stars. In fact\
 , the winner of the 2nd season of SYTYCD is a champion West Coast Swing da
 ncer\, Benji Schwimmer.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/rHXk2JBbm7Y\n\n&nbsp\; Dancing
  on the Pier with Shelley Saxena
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2017/07/dancing-on-the-pier-2.jpg
CATEGORIES:Swing,West Coast Swing
LOCATION:Harbourfront Centre\, 235 Queens Quay West\, Toronto\, Ontario\, G
 TA\, Canada
GEO:43.638847;-79.382996
