URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/the-apology-project/
SUMMARY:The Apology Project
DESCRIPTION:lbs/sq” ‘s Artistic Director Gerry Trentham returns to the 
 Harbourfront stage with The Apology Project.\nA collaboration with America
 n Visual Artist Kaersten Colvin- Woodruff\nPresented in association with H
 arbourfront Centre\nSeptember 21 – 23\, 2017\n\nChoreographer Gerry Tren
 tham returns to the Harbourfront stage with the world premiere of The Apol
 ogy Project September 21 – 23\, 2017 at 8:00pm\, at the Harbourfront Cen
 tre Theatre\, 231 Queens Quay West. Performed together with dancer Kevin O
 rmsby and set in a landscape of art works by visual artist Kaersten Colvin
 -Woodruff (USA)\, projections by Toronto filmmaker Valerie Buhagiar\, and 
 lighting design by Simon Rossiter\, The Apology Project interrogates the f
 alling body from triumph\, the shame of the oppressed\, and the oppressor 
 searching for the apology that can release a body’s endless legacy of vi
 olence.\n\nGerry Trentham\, whose Dora winning performances have been desc
 ribed as “remarkably lyrical” (Anna Kisselgoff\, New York Times)\, and
  “powerful\, outstanding” (Clive Barnes\, New York Post)\, and KM Hunt
 er Dance Award Nominee &amp\; Canada Council Victor Martyn Lynch–Staunto
 n Award recipient Kevin Ormsby join forces on stage for the first time. Th
 ese two Canadian dance powers come together in work that pushes boundaries
  and illuminates what is possible when one commits a life to dance. They p
 lay well together in a very dangerous playground that celebrates and unear
 ths both joyous and foul nature.\n\nFounded in 1995 and led by Artistic Di
 rector\, Gerry Trentham\, pounds per square inch performance (lbs/sq”) f
 osters contemporary creation and performance that reflects a trans-discipl
 inary\, cultural/environmental consciousness. lbs/sq” projects are desig
 ned to connect artists through mutual interest in the transformative human
  body/mind as a primary source for artistic development and artistic excel
