URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/advanced-beginner-feel-ur-body-bal
 let-contemporary-dance/
SUMMARY:Advanced Beginner: Feel Ur Body Ballet &amp\; Contemporary Dance
DESCRIPTION:Advanced Beginner: Feel Ur Body Ballet &amp\; Contemporary Danc
 e (6 weeks)\nTaught by Sze-Yang Ade-Lam\n\nSep 21\, 28 &amp\; Oct 5\, 12\,
  19\, 26\nThursdays at 7:30-9:30pm\n\nA great class for folks who feel com
 fortable with their plies\, tondues etc. and want to work on increasing th
 eir dance vocabulary with more challenging barre exercises\, short movemen
 t combinations across the floor\, short choreographies and/or to begin lea
 rning jumps and turns.\n\nTaught by Sze-Yang Ade-Lam\, a founding member o
 f ILL NANA/DiverseCity Dance Company\, Sze-Yang works to create a judgemen
 t free space where everybody is valued and positive energy and affirmation
  are encouraged\, so that people feel more comfortable exploring dance and
  movement while connecting with their bodies.\n\nSze-Yang Ade-Lam is a que
 er asian dancer\, martial artist\, storyteller &amp\; community developer\
 , who has taught\, choreographed\, and performed internationally. Sze-Yang
  shares stories through movement for self love\, empowerment\, and liberat
 ion as an independent artist and as part of ILL NANA/DiverseCity Dance Com
 pany. Sze-Yang is committed to creating more accessible dance education an
 d performance opportunities for people underrepresented in the arts. A gra
 duate of the School of Toronto Dance Theatre\, Sze-Yang continues to study
  Ballet with Xing Bang Fu\, Simon Lalonde\, and Christine Wright\, Wing Ch
 un with Ryan Kennedy\, Hip Hop and Street Styles.\n\nRate: $150\, $120 or 
 $90 for the 6-week series plus HST* (i.e. $169.50\, $135.60\, or $101.70)\
 n(i.e. $25\, $20\, or $15 for every 2-hour class)\n*When 10 people sign up
 \, we can have 5 PWYC spots for BIPOC folks.\n\nLet us know which rate you
  can afford to pay. We will respond with payment instruction as soon as po
 ssible. Advanced Beginner: Feel Ur Body Ballet &amp\; Contemporary Dance
