SUMMARY:Backbone
DESCRIPTION:BACKBONE is a cutting-edge new dance show inspired by the ‘sp
 ine’ of the Americas\, charting the vast and rocky terrain of our human 
 landscape. Through contemporary Indigenous dance and raw athleticism\, eig
 ht dancers bring to life the electricity and impulses of our rocky mountai
 nous backbone.  \n \nThe concept and direction of BACKBONE is by Red Sky's
  Executive and Artistic Director Sandra Laronde\, with collaborative chore
 ography by Jera Wolfe and Thomas Fonua. Backbone will be performed by danc
 ers Ageer\, Eddie Elliott\, Lonii Garnons-Williams\, Phillipe Larouche\, J
 ulie Pham\, Joshua St. John\, and Jera Wolfe. Video and ighting design of 
 Backbone is by Andy Moro and Michel Charbonneau\, with Costume design by J
 eff Chief.\n\nBackbone • Toronto\nNovember 2 - 12\, 2017\nMedia Night: F
 riday\, November 3 – 8pm\nThursdays\, Saturday\, Tuesday at 8pm\nFridays
  at 7pm\, Sunday and Wednesday at 1pm\nCanadian Stage\, Berkeley Street Th
 eatre\, 26 Berkeley Street\, Toronto\nTickets from $35 and can be purchase
 d online\, by phone at 416.368.3110\nor in person at the Berkeley Street T
 heatre Box Office (26 Berkeley Street)\nSee "More Info" tab for website in
 fo.\n Backbone
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2017/10/Backbone.jpg
CATEGORIES:Indigenous
