SUMMARY:Royal Winnipeg Ballet Professional Division’s 2017/18 Audition To
 ur in Oakville
DESCRIPTION:Each year Canada’s Royal Winnipeg Ballet School travels the c
 ountry in search of talented dancers to join one of three Professional Pro
 grams: Ballet Academic (Ages 10+)\, Aspirant (Post-Secondary)\, and Teache
 r Training Program (Post-Secondary).\n\nAuditions take place in cities acr
 oss Canada and into the United States and include a Q &amp\; A portion for
  parents and students\, as well as master class in some cities. Students u
 nable to attend an audition may send in a Video Application\, which are ac
 cepted until May 1\, 2018.\n\nStudents who are identified with potential a
 re invited to attend the second audition phase. The second audition happen
 s in Summer Session throughout the month of July in Winnipeg. Students exp
 erience life in residence\, the daily schedule\, connect with artistic fac
 ulty and build on their potential.\n\nAfter a month of intense training\, 
 students who are accepted to one of the Professional Programs will begin t
 heir journey as young artists in September 2018.\n\nVisit rwb.org/audition
  to register online or download the application form. For additional infor
 mation please do not hesitate to contact us. Royal Winnipeg Ballet Profess
 ional Division’s 2017/18 Audition Tour in Oakville
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2016/08/RWB-ballet.png
