SUMMARY:West Coast Swing For Beginners
DESCRIPTION:*** West Coast Swing Dance Lessons for Beginners ***\n\nIf you 
 have ever wanted to try West Coast Swing\, now is your chance with this fu
 n class especially for people with little or no experience with West Coast
  Swing\, or dancing in general.\n\nYou will learn the basic steps and patt
 erns of West Coast Swing in a fun and friendly class environment.\n\n- No 
 previous dance experience needed\n- No partner needed\n- Taught by Shelley
  Saxena - one of Toronto's top rated West Coast Swing instructors\n- Comfo
 rtable air-conditioned dance studio\n- Fun and friendly class environment\
 n- Free social dance included after class for practice and fun!\n\nLEVEL: 
 Beginner\n\nDANCE STYLE: West Coast Swing\n\nWHEN: Every Sunday from 4 to 
 5pm - 5 Week Series Starting Nov. 12\, 2017\n\nWHERE: Rhythm and Motion Da
 nce Studio\, 3352 Dundas Street West\, Toronto (corner of Runnymede and Du
 ndas)\n\nFor more information or to pre-register\, contact Shelley at her 
 website www.shelleydance.com or click on "Send Email to Organizer" down be
 low.\n\n*** FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS ***\n\nQ. Do I need any previous da
 nce experience?\n\nAbsolutely not! You can learn West Coast Swing in three
  easy steps\, even if you have never danced before and have two left feet.
 \n\nQ. Do I need to come with a partner?\n\nNo\, you do NOT need a partner
  for the class. If you have someone you would like to learn with\, that is
  fantastic. But you do NOT need a partner to take the class. The class is 
 structured so you rotate with different partners throughout the class. It'
 s a great way to meet new people and you also get to dance with a variety 
 of leads and follows.\n\nQ. What type of shoes should I wear?\n\nIf you al
 ready have dance shoes\, then bring those. If you don't have dance shoes\,
  then something with a leather or suede sole is best. If not\, then just w
 ear your most comfortable pair of shoes.\n\nQ. What type of clothes should
  I wear to class?\n\nWear whatever you will feel most comfortable in. West
  Coast Swing is a very casual dance so wear your favorite jeans and t-shir
 t if you want.\n\nQ. Who is the instructor?\n\nYour instructor is Shelley 
 Saxena. Shelley has been dancing\, studying and competing in West Coast Sw
 ing for 18 years. With an extensive background in Jazz\, Ballet and Modern
  dance\, Shelley now specializes in West Coast Swing.\n\nQ. Where can I pr
 actice what I've learned?\n\nThere is a social dance after the class from 
 7pm to 9pm. The dance is FREE for people in the beginner class.\n\nQ. I st
 ill have a question about the class or West Coast Swing. Can you help?\n\n
 Of course! If you have any other questions\, please don't hesitate to cont
 act Shelley at her website www.shelleydance.com or click on "Send Email to
  Organizer" down below. West Coast Swing For Beginners
