SUMMARY:West Coast Swing Sundays - Classes + Social Dance &amp\; Practice
DESCRIPTION:*** West Coast Swing Sundays - 3 Levels of Dance Classes + Soci
 al Dance/Practice ***\n\nEnd the week with a fun\, friendly and intimate e
 vening of West Coast Swing. New five week series starting Sunday Nov. 12 t
 o Dec . 17. Three levels of group classes to choose from.\n\nBEGINNER SERI
 ES (Level 1 Beginner) 4pm-5pm: A solid introduction to the basics of West 
 Coast swing. $80+tax. (No partner needed)\n\nBASICS PLUS SERIES (Level 2 B
 eginner) 5pm-6pm: For those who already have the basics steps of West Coas
 t swing. $80+tax. (No partner needed)\n\nINTERMEDIATE 6p-7pm: $18 drop-in.
  (Intermediate class requires minimum two years West Coast Swing experienc
 e\, or prior completion of both the Beginners and Basics Plus series.)\n\n
 All classes include free admission to the two hour social dance/practice f
 rom 7pm-9pm.\n\nSOCIAL DANCE: 7pm-9pm\, $5 for the dance only\n\n 	All cla
 sses taught by Shelley Saxena – one of Toronto’s top rated West Coast 
 Swing instructors\n 	Comfortable air-conditioned dance studio\n 	Fun and f
 riendly class environment\n 	Free social dance included after class for pr
 actice and fun!\n\nFor more information or to pre-register\, contact Shell
 ey at her website www.shelleydance.com or click on “Send Email to Organi
 zer” down below.\n\n*** FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS ***\n\nQ. Do I need a
 ny previous dance experience?\n\nAbsolutely not! You can learn West Coast 
 Swing in three easy steps\, even if you have never danced before and have 
 two left feet.\n\nQ. Do I need to come with a partner?\n\nNo\, you do NOT 
 need a partner for the classes. If you have someone you would like to lear
 n with\, that is fantastic. But you do NOT need a partner to take the clas
 s. The class is structured so you rotate with different partners throughou
 t the class. It’s a great way to meet new people and you also get to dan
 ce with a variety of leads and follows.\n\nQ. What type of shoes should I 
 wear?\n\nIf you already have dance shoes\, then bring those. If you don’
 t have dance shoes\, then something with a leather or suede sole is best. 
 If not\, then just wear your most comfortable pair of shoes.\n\nQ. What ty
 pe of clothes should I wear to class?\n\nWear whatever you will feel most 
 comfortable in. West Coast Swing is a very casual dance so wear your favor
 ite jeans and t-shirt if you want.\n\nQ. Who is the instructor?\n\nYour in
 structor is Shelley Saxena. Shelley has been dancing\, studying and compet
 ing in West Coast Swing for 18 years. With an extensive background in Jazz
 \, Ballet and Modern dance\, Shelley now specializes in West Coast Swing.\
 n\nQ. Where can I practice what I’ve learned?\n\nThere is a social dance
  after the class from 7pm to 9pm. The dance is FREE for people in any of t
 he classes.\n\nQ. I still have a question about the class or West Coast Sw
 ing. Can you help?\n\nOf course! If you have any other questions\, please 
 don’t hesitate to contact Shelley at her website www.shelleydance.com or
  click on “Send Email to Organizer” down below. West Coast Swing Sunda
 ys - Classes + Social Dance &amp\; Practice
