URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/west-coast-swing-dance-for-beginne
 rs/
SUMMARY:West Coast Swing Dance For Beginners
DESCRIPTION:*** West Coast Swing Dance For Beginners ***\n\nIf you have eve
 r wanted to try West Coast Swing\, now is your chance with this fun class 
 especially for people with little or no experience with West Coast Swing\,
  or dancing in general.\n\nYou will learn the basic steps and patterns of 
 West Coast Swing in a fun and friendly class environment.\n\n- No previous
  dance experience needed\n- No partner needed\n- Taught by Shelley Saxena 
 - one of Toronto's top rated West Coast Swing instructors\n- Comfortable a
 ir-conditioned dance studio\n- Fun and friendly class environment\n- FREE 
 social dance included after class for practice and fun!\n\nLEVEL: Beginner
 \n\nDANCE STYLE: West Coast Swing\n\nWHEN: Sunday Dec. 3\, 10 and 17\, 201
 7\n\nWHERE: Rhythm &amp\; Motion Dance Studio\, 3352 Dundas Street West\, 
 Toronto (corner of Runnymede and Dundas)\n\nFor more information or to pre
 -register\, click the "More Info" tab at the top of this listing\, or visi
 t www.ShelleyDance.com\n\n*** FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS ***\n\nQ. Do I ne
 ed any previous dance experience?\n\nAbsolutely not! You can learn West Co
 ast Swing in three easy steps\, even if you have never danced before and h
 ave two left feet.\n\nQ. Do I need to come with a partner?\n\nNo\, you do 
 not need a partner for the class. If you have someone you would like to le
 arn with\, that is fantastic. But you do NOT need a partner to take the cl
 ass. The class is structured so you rotate with different partners through
 out the class. It's a great way to meet new people and you also get to dan
 ce with a variety of leads and follows.\n\nQ. What type of shoes should I 
 wear?\n\nIf you already have dance shoes\, then bring those. If you don't 
 have dance shoes\, then something with a leather or suede sole is best. If
  not\, then just wear your most comfortable pair of shoes.\n\nQ. What type
  of clothes should I wear to class?\n\nWear whatever you will feel most co
 mfortable in. West Coast Swing is a very casual dance so wear your favorit
 e jeans and t-shirt if you want.\n\nQ. Who is the instructor?\n\nYour inst
 ructor is Shelley Saxena. Shelley has been dancing\, studying and competin
 g in West Coast Swing for 18 years. With an extensive background in Jazz\,
  Ballet and Modern dance\, Shelley now specializes in West Coast Swing. Yo
 u can contact Shelley at www.ShelleyDance.com\n\nQ. Where can I practice w
 hat I've learned?\n\nThere is a social dance after the class from 7pm to 9
 pm. The dance is FREE for people in the beginner class.\n\nQ. I still have
  a question about the class or West Coast Swing. Can you help?\n\nOf cours
 e! If you have any other questions\, please don't hesitate to contact Shel
 ley by clicking the "More Info" tab at the top of this listing\, or visiti
 ng her website www.ShelleyDance.com. She will be very happy to help you an
 y way she can.\n\nQ. I'm excited to get started! What's my next step?\n\nS
 imply click the "More Info" tab at the top of this listing to let Shelley 
 know you'd like to register\, or contact her at her website www.ShelleyDan
 ce.com (class size is limited so it's important to make sure you reserve y
 our spot). West Coast Swing Dance For Beginners
