SUMMARY:West Coast Swing - Classes + Social Dance
DESCRIPTION:*** West Coast Swing Classes + Social Dance ***\n\nThree differ
 ent classes available to suit your level - from total beginner to intermed
 iate.\n\n- No previous dance experience needed (for beginner class)\n- No 
 partner needed\n- Taught by Shelley Saxena - one of Toronto's top rated We
 st Coast Swing instructors\n- Comfortable air-conditioned dance studio\n- 
 Fun and friendly class environment\n- FREE social dance included after cla
 ss for practice and fun!\n- Wide variety of great music ranging from Blues
  to Top 40\n\nWHEN: Sundays - December 3\, 10 and 17\n\nTIME:\nBeginner (L
 evel 1): 4pm to 5pm\nBasics Plus (Level 2 Beginner): 5pm to 6pm\nIntermedi
 ate: 6pm to 7pm\nSocial Dance: 7pm to 9pm\n\nAll levels are welcome for th
 e social dance. FREE for people in any of the classes. $5 for just the dan
 ce.\n\nWHERE: Rhythm &amp\; Motion Dance Studio\, 3352 Dundas Street West\
 , Toronto (corner of Runnymede and Dundas)\n\nFor more information or to p
 re-register\, click the "More Info" tab at the top of this listing\, or vi
 sit www.ShelleyDance.com\n\n*** FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS ***\n\nQ. Do I 
 need any previous dance experience?\n\nAbsolutely not! The Level 1 beginne
 r class is perfect for you. You can learn West Coast Swing in three easy s
 teps\, even if you have never danced before and have two left feet.\n\nQ. 
 Do I need to come with a partner?\n\nNo\, you do not need a partner for th
 e class. If you have someone you would like to learn with\, that is fantas
 tic. But you do NOT need a partner to take the class. The class is structu
 red so you rotate with different partners throughout the class. It's a gre
 at way to meet new people and you also get to dance with a variety of lead
 s and follows.\n\nQ. What type of shoes should I wear?\n\nIf you already h
 ave dance shoes\, then bring those. If you don't have dance shoes\, then s
 omething with a leather or suede sole is best. If not\, then just wear you
 r most comfortable pair of shoes.\n\nQ. What type of clothes should I wear
  to class?\n\nWear whatever you will feel most comfortable in. West Coast 
 Swing is a very casual dance so wear your favorite jeans and t-shirt if yo
 u want.\n\nQ. Who is the instructor?\n\nYour instructor is Shelley Saxena.
  Shelley has been dancing\, studying and competing in West Coast Swing for
  18 years. With an extensive background in Jazz\, Ballet and Modern dance\
 , Shelley now specializes in West Coast Swing. You can contact Shelley at 
 www.ShelleyDance.com\n\nQ. Where can I practice what I've learned?\n\nTher
 e is a social dance after the class from 7pm to 9pm. The dance is FREE for
  people in any of the classes.\n\nQ. I still have a question about the cla
 ss or West Coast Swing. Can you help?\n\nOf course! If you have any other 
 questions\, please don't hesitate to contact Shelley by clicking the "More
  Info" tab at the top of this listing\, or visiting her website www.Shelle
 yDance.com. She will be very happy to help you any way she can.\n\nQ. I'm 
 excited to get started! What's my next step?\n\nSimply click the "More Inf
 o" tab at the top of this listing to let Shelley know you'd like to regist
 er\, or contact her at her website www.ShelleyDance.com (class size is lim
 ited so it's important to make sure you reserve your spot). West Coast Swi
 ng - Classes + Social Dance
