SUMMARY:School of Groove - All-Female Urban/Commercial Training Program (Ja
 n-Apr)
DESCRIPTION:Apply now for a chance to secure your spot early and get 15% of
 f your tuition fee! [www.schoolofgroove.ca/application]\n*we are happy to 
 answer any and all questions you may have!\n------------------------------
 ---------\n\nWhat is SOG?\n\nSchool Of Groove is a dance training and ment
 orship program dedicated to nurturing strong and confident young female da
 ncers. We act as a bridge – connecting dancers to like minded peers\, me
 ntors and the larger dance community. Our mission lies in giving emerging 
 talent a holistic approach to the learning experience and the tools they n
 eed in order to refine their practice and find success on their personal d
 ance journey.\n\nOur 3 month long program uses urban and commercial dance 
 techniques as a means to provide you with the skills and mindset to help y
 ou accomplish your personal dance goals\, all while keeping the female voi
 ce in mind. Our school-of-thought focuses on an in-depth understanding and
  application of the SOG pillars: music\, movement\, style\, empowerment.\n
 \n 	Limited class sizes &amp\; personalized attention\n 	structured curric
 ulum\n 	technical and artistic enrichment\n 	guest workshops\n 	profession
 al development\n 	and more...\n\n----------------------------------------\
 n\nWho can apply?\n\n 	ages 15-30 years old\n 	identify as female\n 	previ
 ous dance training an asset (formal or informal)\n 	able to commit to full
  3 month program (Sundays 3-6pm\, Sept 10-Dec 3rd)\n 	must have strong wor
 k ethic\, team mentality and desire to grow\n\n---------------------------
 -------------\n\nProgram runs Sundays 3-6pm\, Jan 28-Apr 29 (no class Marc
 h Break/Easter). 2700 Dufferin Street (Danceology)\nMore info: www.schoolo
 fgroove.ca\nApply now: www.schoolofgroove.ca/application\n\nUnder directio
 n of Queenie Seguban and Kelly Gammie of @deucendip dance crew.\n\nEarly a
 cceptance deadline: November 15\, 2017 (11:59pm) = 15% of tuition/free wor
 kshops/secure your spot first\nFinal deadline: December 15\, 2017 (11:59pm
 )\n\nType: Class\nAddress: 2700 Dufferin Unit 3\nCity: Toronto\nPostal Cod
 e: M9N 3A7\nEmail: fill out the "more info" tab School of Groove - All-Fem
 ale Urban/Commercial Training Program (Jan-Apr)
