URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/west-coast-swing-christmas-party-d
 ance/
SUMMARY:West Coast Swing Christmas Party &amp\; Dance
DESCRIPTION:*** West Coast Swing Christmas Party &amp\; Dance ***\n\nChrist
 mas Cheer + West Coast Swing = The Most Fun Christmas Dance Ever!\n\nJoin 
 us for this year's annual Christmas party and dance on Sunday\, December 1
 7 at Rhythm &amp\; Motion Studio.\n\nLots of great music to dance to\, plu
 s Christmas treats and refreshments!\n\nWHEN:\nSunday\, December 17\, 2017
 \n\nTIME:\nBeginner Class (Level 1): 4pm to 5pm\nBasics Plus Class (Level 
 2 Beginner): 5pm to 6pm\nIntermediate Class: 6pm to 7pm\nChristmas Party &
 amp\; Dance: 7pm to 9pm\n\nAll levels are welcome for the social dance. Fr
 ee for people taking any of the classes. $5 for just the dance.\n\nWHERE:\
 nRhythm &amp\; Motion Dance Studio\, 3352 Dundas Street West\, Toronto (co
 rner of Runnymede and Dundas)\n\nIf you have any questions\, click the “
 More Info” tab at the top of this listing\, or visit www.ShelleyDance.co
 m\n\n*** FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS ***\n\nQ. Do I need to come with a par
 tner?\n\nNo\, you do not need a partner for the class or the dance. If you
  have someone you would like to learn with\, that is fantastic. But you do
  NOT need a partner to take the class. The class is structured so you rota
 te with different partners throughout the class. It’s a great way to mee
 t new people and you also get to dance with a variety of leads and follows
 .\n\nQ. What type of shoes should I wear?\n\nIf you already have dance sho
 es\, then bring those. If you don’t have dance shoes\, then something wi
 th a leather or suede sole is best. If not\, then just wear your most comf
 ortable pair of shoes.\n\nQ. What type of clothes should I wear to class?\
 n\nWear whatever you will feel most comfortable in. West Coast Swing is a 
 very casual dance so wear your favorite jeans and t-shirt if you want.\n\n
 Q. Who is the instructor?\n\nYour instructor is Shelley Saxena. Shelley ha
 s been dancing\, studying and competing in West Coast Swing for 18 years. 
 With an extensive background in Jazz\, Ballet and Modern dance\, Shelley n
 ow specializes in West Coast Swing. You can contact Shelley at www.Shelley
 Dance.com\n\nQ. I still have a question about the class\, dance or West Co
 ast Swing. Can you help?\n\nOf course! If you have any questions\, please 
 don’t hesitate to contact Shelley by clicking the “More Info” tab at
  the top of this listing\, or visiting her website www.ShelleyDance.com. S
 he will be very happy to help you any way she can. West Coast Swing Christ
 mas Party &amp\; Dance
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2017/12/christmas-dance.jpg
