URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/west-coast-swing-for-beginners-2/
SUMMARY:West Coast Swing For Beginners
DESCRIPTION:*** West Coast Swing Dance For Beginners ***\n\nIf you have eve
 r wanted to try West Coast Swing\, now is your chance with these fun class
 es designed for people with little or no experience with West Coast Swing\
 , or dancing in general.\n\nYou will learn the basic steps and patterns of
  West Coast Swing in a fun and friendly class environment.\n\n– No previ
 ous dance experience needed\n– No partner needed\n– Taught by Shelley 
 Saxena – one of Toronto’s top rated West Coast Swing instructors\n– 
 Comfortable dance studio in central location\n– Fun and friendly class e
 nvironment\n– FREE social dance included after class for practice and fu
 n!\n– Wide variety of great music ranging from Blues to Top 40\n– Two 
 beginner classes to choose from to suit your level\n\nLEVELS:\nBeginner (L
 evel 1 Beginner) - for people brand new to West Coast Swing with little or
  no dance experience.\n\nBasics Plus (Level 2 Beginner) - for people alrea
 dy comfortable with the basic 6-count and 8-count patterns (ie. left-side 
 pass\, right-side pass\, sugar push\, basic whip and basket whip).\n\nDANC
 E STYLE: West Coast Swing\n\nWHEN: 6 Week Series - Starts Sunday January 7
 \, 2018\nBeginner: 4pm to 5pm\nBasics Plus: 5pm to 6pm\nSocial Dance: 7pm 
 to 9pm\n\nWHERE: Rhythm &amp\; Motion Dance Studio\, 3352 Dundas Street We
 st\, Toronto (corner of Runnymede and Dundas)\n\nFor more information or t
 o pre-register\, click the “More Info” tab at the top of this listing\
 , or visit www.ShelleyDance.com\n\n*** FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS ***\n\nQ
 . Do I need any previous dance experience?\n\nAbsolutely not! The Level 1 
 Beginner class is perfect for you. You can learn West Coast Swing in three
  easy steps\, even if you have never danced before and have two left feet.
 \n\nQ. Do I need to come with a partner?\n\nNo\, you do not need a partner
  for the class. If you have someone you would like to learn with\, that is
  fantastic. But you do NOT need a partner to take the class. The class is 
 structured so you rotate with different partners throughout the class. It
 ’s a great way to meet new people and you also get to dance with a varie
 ty of leads and follows.\n\nQ. What type of shoes should I wear?\n\nIf you
  already have dance shoes\, then bring those. If you don’t have dance sh
 oes\, then something with a leather or suede sole is best. If not\, then j
 ust wear your most comfortable pair of shoes.\n\nQ. What type of clothes s
 hould I wear to class?\n\nWear whatever you will feel most comfortable in.
  West Coast Swing is a very casual dance so wear your favorite jeans and t
 -shirt if you want.\n\nQ. Who is the instructor?\n\nYour instructor is She
 lley Saxena. Shelley has been dancing\, studying and competing in West Coa
 st Swing for 18 years. With an extensive background in Jazz\, Ballet and M
 odern dance\, Shelley now specializes in West Coast Swing. You can contact
  Shelley at www.ShelleyDance.com\n\nQ. Where can I practice what I’ve le
 arned?\n\nThere is a social dance after the classes from 7pm to 9pm. The d
 ance is FREE for people in the beginner classes.\n\nQ. I still have a ques
 tion about the class or West Coast Swing. Can you help?\n\nOf course! If y
 ou have any other questions\, please don’t hesitate to contact Shelley b
 y clicking the “More Info” tab at the top of this listing\, or visitin
 g her website www.ShelleyDance.com. She will be very happy to help you any
  way she can.\n\nQ. I’m excited to get started! What’s my next step?\n
 \nSimply click the “More Info” tab at the top of this listing to let S
 helley know you’d like to register\, or contact her at her website www.S
 helleyDance.com (class size is limited so it’s important to make sure yo
 u reserve your spot). West Coast Swing For Beginners
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2017/12/wcs-770x513.jpg
CATEGORIES:West Coast Swing
LOCATION:Rhythm and Motion Studio\, 3352 Dundas St West\, Toronto\, Ontario
 \, GTA\, Canada
GEO:43.665699;-79.481796
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=3352 Dundas St West\, Toron
 to\, Ontario\, GTA\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Rhythm and Motion S
 tudio:geo:43.665699,-79.481796
END:VEVENT
