URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/west-coast-swing-ladies-styling-se
 crets/
SUMMARY:West Coast Swing - Ladies Styling Secrets
DESCRIPTION:*** Feel and Look Better Than Ever On The Dance Floor! ***\n\nW
 hether you want to add some shaping and style to your West Coast Swing\, o
 r improve the quality of your movement\, these followers only styling clas
 ses reveal all the little secrets to fun and gorgeous West Coast Swing.\n\
 nYou'll learn:\n\n- How to move your body with confidence\n- Body isolatio
 ns\n- Beautiful arm styling\n- Shaping v​ariations on basic patterns\n- 
 Timing variations\n- Creating beautiful lines\n- How to be the best dancer
  you can be with any style or level of leader\n\nShelley's easy to learn l
 adies styling tips for West Coast Swing will have you looking and feeling 
 awesome on the dance floor!\n\nWHEN:\nSaturday\, January 20\n4pm to 5:30pm
 \nJoy of Dance\, 95 Danforth Ave.\n\nSaturday\, February 17\n11:30am to 1p
 m\nDovercourt House\, 805 Dovercourt Rd.\n\nSaturday\, March 17\n1:30pm to
  3pm\nDovercourt House\, 805 Dovercourt Rd.\n\nPRICE: Three different work
 shops. $20 per workshop or all 3 for just $50.\n\nFor more information or 
 to pre-register\, click the “More Info” tab at the top of this listing
 \, or visit www.ShelleyDance.com\n\nClass size is limited so please regist
 er as soon as possible to confirm your spot.\n\nIf you have any questions 
 whatsoever\, please don’t hesitate to contact Shelley.\n\n*** FREQUENTLY
  ASKED QUESTIONS ***\n\nQ. Do I need to come with a partner?\n\nNo\, you d
 o not need a partner for the class. This is a followers ONLY class so no p
 artner is required.\n\nQ. What type of shoes should I wear?\n\nIf you alre
 ady have dance shoes\, then bring those. If you don't have dance shoes\, t
 hen something with a leather or suede sole is best. If not\, then just wea
 r your most comfortable pair of shoes.\n\nQ. What type of clothes should I
  wear to class?\n\nWear whatever you will feel most comfortable in. West C
 oast Swing is a very casual dance so wear your favorite jeans and t-shirt 
 if you want.\n\nQ. Who is the instructor?\n\nYour instructor is Shelley Sa
 xena. Shelley has been dancing\, studying and competing in West Coast Swin
 g for 18 years. With an extensive background in Jazz\, Ballet and Modern d
 ance\, Shelley now specializes in West Coast Swing.\n\nQ. Do I need any pr
 evious dance experience to take the Styling class?\n\nThis is not a class 
 for complete beginners. You must have at least one year of recent experien
 ce as a follower in West Coast Swing and be comfortable with both the 6-co
 unt and 8-count basics.\n\nQ. I still have a question about the class. Can
  you help?\n\nOf course! If you have any other questions\, please don’t 
 hesitate to contact Shelley by clicking the “More Info” tab at the top
  of this listing\, or visiting her website www.ShelleyDance.com. She will 
 be very happy to help you any way she can.\n\nQ. I’m excited to get star
 ted! What’s my next step?\n\nSimply click the “More Info” tab at the
  top of this listing to let Shelley know you’d like to register\, or con
 tact her at her website www.ShelleyDance.com (class size is limited so it
 ’s important to make sure you reserve your spot). West Coast Swing - Lad
 ies Styling Secrets
