URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/west-coast-swing-ladies-styling-se
 crets-2/
SUMMARY:West Coast Swing – Ladies Styling Secrets
DESCRIPTION:*** Feel and Look Better Than Ever On The Dance Floor! ***\n\nW
 hether you want to add some shaping and style to your West Coast Swing\, o
 r improve the quality of your movement\, this ladies styling class reveals
  all the little secrets to fun and gorgeous West Coast Swing.\n\nYou’ll 
 learn:\n\n– How to move your body with confidence\n– Body isolations\n
 – Beautiful arm styling\n– Shaping v​ariations on basic patterns\n
 – Timing variations\n– Creating beautiful lines\n– How to be the bes
 t dancer you can be with any style or level of leader\n\nShelley’s easy 
 to learn ladies styling tips for West Coast Swing will have you looking an
 d feeling awesome on the dance floor!\n\nWHEN:\n\nSaturday\, February 17\n
 11:30am to 1pm\nDovercourt House\, 805 Dovercourt Rd.\n\nSaturday\, March 
 17\n1:30pm to 3pm\nDovercourt House\, 805 Dovercourt Rd.\n\nPRICE: Two dif
 ferent workshops. $20 per workshop.\n\nFor more information or to pre-regi
 ster\, click the “More Info” tab at the top of this listing\, or visit
  www.ShelleyDance.com\n\nClass size is limited so please register as soon 
 as possible to confirm your spot.\n\nIf you have any questions whatsoever\
 , please don’t hesitate to contact Shelley.\n\n*** FREQUENTLY ASKED QUES
 TIONS ***\n\nQ. Do I need to come with a partner?\n\nNo\, you do not need 
 a partner for the class. This is a followers ONLY class so no partner is r
 equired.\n\nQ. What type of shoes should I wear?\n\nIf you already have da
 nce shoes\, then bring those. If you don’t have dance shoes\, then somet
 hing with a leather or suede sole is best. If not\, then just wear your mo
 st comfortable pair of shoes.\n\nQ. What type of clothes should I wear to 
 class?\n\nWear whatever you will feel most comfortable in. West Coast Swin
 g is a very casual dance so wear your favorite jeans and t-shirt if you wa
 nt.\n\nQ. Who is the instructor?\n\nYour instructor is Shelley Saxena. She
 lley has been dancing\, studying and competing in West Coast Swing for 18 
 years. With an extensive background in Jazz\, Ballet and Modern dance\, Sh
 elley now specializes in West Coast Swing.\n\nQ. Do I need any previous da
 nce experience to take the Styling class?\n\nThis is not a class for compl
 ete beginners. You must have at least one year of recent experience as a f
 ollower in West Coast Swing and be comfortable with both the 6-count and 8
 -count basics.\n\nQ. I still have a question about the class. Can you help
 ?\n\nOf course! If you have any other questions\, please don’t hesitate 
 to contact Shelley by clicking the “More Info” tab at the top of this 
 listing\, or visiting her website www.ShelleyDance.com. She will be very h
 appy to help you any way she can.\n\nQ. I’m excited to get started! What
 ’s my next step?\n\nSimply click the “More Info” tab at the top of t
 his listing to let Shelley know you’d like to register\, or contact her 
 at her website www.ShelleyDance.com (class size is limited so it’s impor
 tant to make sure you reserve your spot). West Coast Swing – Ladies Styl
 ing Secrets
