URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/west-coast-swing-for-beginners-3/
SUMMARY:West Coast Swing For Beginners
DESCRIPTION:*** West Coast Swing Dance For Beginners ***\n\nIf you have eve
 r wanted to try West Coast Swing\, now is your chance with these fun class
 es designed for people with little or no experience with West Coast Swing\
 , or dancing in general.\n\nYou will learn the basic steps and patterns of
  West Coast Swing in a fun and friendly class environment.\n\n– No previ
 ous dance experience needed\n– No partner needed\n– Taught by Shelley 
 Saxena – one of Toronto’s top rated West Coast Swing instructors\n– 
 Comfortable dance studio in central location\n– Fun and friendly class e
 nvironment\n– FREE social dance included after class for practice and fu
 n!\n– Wide variety of great music ranging from Blues to Top 40\n– Two 
 beginner classes to choose from to suit your level\n\nLEVELS:\nBeginner (L
 evel 1 Beginner) – for people brand new to West Coast Swing with little 
 or no dance experience.\n\nBasics Plus (Level 2 Beginner) – for people a
 lready comfortable with the basic 6-count and 8-count patterns (ie. left-s
 ide pass\, right-side pass\, sugar push\, basic whip and basket whip).\n\n
 DANCE STYLE: West Coast Swing\n\nWHEN: 6 Class Series – Starts Sunday Fe
 bruary 18\, 2018\nBeginner: 4pm to 5pm\nBasics Plus: 5pm to 6pm\nSocial Da
 nce: 7pm to 9pm\n\nWHERE: Rhythm &amp\; Motion Dance Studio\, 3352 Dundas 
 Street West\, Toronto (corner of Runnymede and Dundas)\n\nFor more informa
 tion or to pre-register\, click the “More Info” tab at the top of this
  listing\, or visit www.ShelleyDance.com\n\n*** FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS
  ***\n\nQ. Do I need any previous dance experience?\n\nAbsolutely not! The
  Level 1 Beginner class is perfect for you. You can learn West Coast Swing
  in three easy steps\, even if you have never danced before and have two l
 eft feet.\n\nQ. Do I need to come with a partner?\n\nNo\, you do not need 
 a partner for the class. If you have someone you would like to learn with\
 , that is fantastic. But you do NOT need a partner to take the class. The 
 class is structured so you rotate with different partners throughout the c
 lass. It’s a great way to meet new people and you also get to dance with
  a variety of leads and follows.\n\nQ. What type of shoes should I wear?\n
 \nIf you already have dance shoes\, then bring those. If you don’t have 
 dance shoes\, then something with a leather or suede sole is best. If not\
 , then just wear your most comfortable pair of shoes.\n\nQ. What type of c
 lothes should I wear to class?\n\nWear whatever you will feel most comfort
 able in. West Coast Swing is a very casual dance so wear your favorite jea
 ns and t-shirt if you want.\n\nQ. Who is the instructor?\n\nYour instructo
 r is Shelley Saxena. Shelley has been dancing\, studying and competing in 
 West Coast Swing for 18 years. With an extensive background in Jazz\, Ball
 et and Modern dance\, Shelley now specializes in West Coast Swing. You can
  contact Shelley at www.ShelleyDance.com\n\nQ. Where can I practice what I
 ’ve learned?\n\nThere is a social dance after the classes from 7pm to 9p
 m. The dance is FREE for people in the beginner classes.\n\nQ. I still hav
 e a question about the class or West Coast Swing. Can you help?\n\nOf cour
 se! If you have any other questions\, please don’t hesitate to contact S
 helley by clicking the “More Info” tab at the top of this listing\, or
  visiting her website www.ShelleyDance.com. She will be very happy to help
  you any way she can.\n\nQ. I’m excited to get started! What’s my next
  step?\n\nSimply click the “More Info” tab at the top of this listing 
 to let Shelley know you’d like to register\, or contact her at her websi
 te www.ShelleyDance.com (class size is limited so it’s important to make
  sure you reserve your spot). West Coast Swing For Beginners
