SUMMARY:Community English Country dance
DESCRIPTION:English Country Dancing is the dance form of Shakespeare\, Jane
  Austen and Napoleon\, but new tunes and dances are being written all the 
 time. It is done in groups (no lead or follow)\, with dancers weaving intr
 icate patterns around each other to music ranging from lively jigs and ree
 ls to dreamy\, stately or dramatic melodies.\n\nLive music\, all dances ta
 ught\, walked through and cued during the music by professional callers. W
 e're a friendly and welcoming group\, and we all invite newcomers to dance
  with us\, so no partner is needed.\nEvery Friday through the end of May (
 except for Good Friday)!\nAfter that we move outdoors for our summer serie
 s in High Park on Sunday afternoons.\n\nBring low-heeled shoes with some g
 rip (old\, well-worn running shoes work well) and your own reusable water 
 bottle\, wear comfortable\, layered clothes\, and kindly refrain from wear
 ing scented body- and hair-care products. Community English Country dance
