SUMMARY:Cry Freedom
DESCRIPTION:In celebration of Canada 150\, this dance/drama by Bravo Niagar
 a and Ballet Creole commemorates the story of Chloe Cooley\, an enslaved w
 oman in Upper Canada whose struggles in 1793 served as the catalyst for th
 e passing of the first legislation in the British colonies to restrict the
  slave trade\, setting the stage for the Underground Railroad.\n\nCheck it
  out!:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?time_continue=14&amp\;v=wEoTFFNiFV
 A\n\nTimes:\nFri\, May 11\, 2018 at 8pm\nSat\, May 12\, 2018 at 8pm\nSun\,
  May 13\, 2018 at 3pm\n\nPurchase here: https://my.harbourfrontcentre.com/
 single/PSDetail.aspx?psn=30343 Cry Freedom
