URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/west-coast-swing-ladies-styling-se
 crets-4/
SUMMARY:West Coast Swing – Ladies Styling Secrets
DESCRIPTION:*** Feel and Look Better Than Ever On The Dance Floor! ***\n\nW
 hether you want to add some shaping and style to your West Coast Swing\, o
 r improve the quality of your movement\, this ladies styling class reveals
  all the little secrets to fun and gorgeous West Coast Swing.\n\nYou’ll 
 learn:\n\n– How to move your body with confidence\n– Body isolations\n
 – Beautiful arm styling\n– Shaping v​ariations on basic patterns\n
 – Timing variations\n– Creating beautiful lines\n– How to be the bes
 t dancer you can be with any style or level of leader\n\nShelley’s easy 
 to learn ladies styling tips for West Coast Swing will have you looking an
 d feeling awesome on the dance floor!\n\nWHEN:\n\nSaturday\, May 12\, 2018
 \n1:30pm to 3pm\n3rd Floor\, Dovercourt House\, 805 Dovercourt Rd.\n\nPRIC
 E: $20\n\nFor more information or to pre-register\, click the “More Info
 ” tab at the top of this listing\, or visit www.ShelleyDance.com\n\nClas
 s size is limited so please register as soon as possible to confirm your s
 pot.\n\nIf you have any questions whatsoever\, please don’t hesitate to 
 contact Shelley.\n\n*** FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS ***\n\nQ. Do I need to 
 come with a partner?\n\nNo\, you do not need a partner for the class. This
  is a followers ONLY class so no partner is required.\n\nQ. What type of s
 hoes should I wear?\n\nIf you already have dance shoes\, then bring those.
  If you don’t have dance shoes\, then something with a leather or suede 
 sole is best. If not\, then just wear your most comfortable pair of shoes.
 \n\nQ. What type of clothes should I wear to class?\n\nWear whatever you w
 ill feel most comfortable in. West Coast Swing is a very casual dance so w
 ear your favorite jeans and t-shirt if you want.\n\nQ. Who is the instruct
 or?\n\nYour instructor is Shelley Saxena. Shelley has been dancing\, study
 ing and competing in West Coast Swing for 18 years. With an extensive back
 ground in Jazz\, Ballet and Modern dance\, Shelley now specializes in West
  Coast Swing.\n\nQ. Do I need any previous dance experience to take the St
 yling class?\n\nThis is not a class for complete beginners. You must have 
 at least one year of recent experience as a follower in West Coast Swing a
 nd be comfortable with both the 6-count and 8-count basics.\n\nQ. I still 
 have a question about the class. Can you help?\n\nOf course! If you have a
 ny other questions\, please don’t hesitate to contact Shelley by clickin
 g the “More Info” tab at the top of this listing\, or visiting her web
 site www.ShelleyDance.com. She will be very happy to help you any way she 
 can.\n\nQ. I’m excited to get started! What’s my next step?\n\nSimply 
 click the “More Info” tab at the top of this listing to let Shelley kn
 ow you’d like to register\, or contact her at her website www.ShelleyDan
 ce.com (class size is limited so it’s important to make sure you reserve
  your spot). West Coast Swing – Ladies Styling Secrets
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2018/05/styling-v2-color-770x480.jpg
