 nato/
SUMMARY:Teaċ Daṁsa's Swan Lake @ Luminato
DESCRIPTION:Teaċ Daṁsa's Swan Lake/Loch na hEala combines traditional Ir
 ish music and contemporary dance for a powerful interpretation of the age-
 old folk tale.\n\nRooted in the midlands of Ireland where ancient mytholog
 y and the modern world collide\, a company of 13 world-class performers\, 
 including beloved Irish actor Mikel Murfi\, weave story-telling with song 
 and movement. Following a sold-out run in London\, a string of five-star r
 eviews\, and a Best Production award at the Irish Times Theatre Awards\, i
 t's a must-see performance at Luminato.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/71Ev5SsR6Vo\n\
 n&nbsp\; Teaċ Daṁsa&#039\;s Swan Lake @ Luminato
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2018/04/swan-lake.jpg
CATEGORIES:Contemporary
LOCATION:Bluma Appel Theatre - St. Lawrence Centre for the Arts\, 27 Front 
 St East\, Toronto\, Ontario\, Canada
GEO:43.647347;-79.375076
