URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/killer-boogie-workshop-part-1/
SUMMARY:Killer Boogie Workshop - Part 1
DESCRIPTION:THIS IS PART 1 of a 2-PART WORKSHOP\n\nThe Killer Boogie craze 
 started to sweep Europe a couple years ago\, with 24-hour video challenges
  and huge workshops. As more and more people have learned it\, it's become
  something like the boogie woogie Big Apple. When the first notes of the s
 ong get played\, people rush onto the dance floor and the place goes wild.
 \n\nNow it's Toronto's turn to learn this fast-paced\, fun\, solo rock n r
 oll routine\, choreographed by Marcus Koch.\n\nTwo 90-minute workshops on 
 consecutive Sundays will prepare you to join in on all the fun\, here at h
 ome or in your rock n roll travels.\n\nNo partner required. No experience 
 required.\n\nSUNDAYS - July 22 and July 29\nFrom noon to 1:30 pm\n700 Univ
 ersity Avenue - Queen's Park Subway Station - southwest corner of the inte
 rsection: meet in the courtyard behind Tim Horton's by noon\, and we'll al
 l go inside together (building is locked on Sundays\, so you need an escor
 t to go in)\n\n$25 (includes BOTH sessions)\;\n$15 for full-time students/
 seniors/under-employed Killer Boogie Workshop - Part 1
