URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/west-coast-swing-for-beginners-4/
SUMMARY:West Coast Swing For Beginners
DESCRIPTION:*** West Coast Swing Dance For Beginners ***\n\nIf you have eve
 r wanted to try West Coast Swing\, now is your chance with these fun class
 es designed for people with little or no experience with West Coast Swing\
 , or dancing in general.\n\nYou will learn the basic steps and patterns of
  West Coast Swing in a fun and friendly class environment.\n\n– No previ
 ous dance experience needed\n– No partner needed\n– Taught by Shelley 
 Saxena – one of Toronto’s top rated West Coast Swing instructors\n– 
 Comfortable air-conditioned dance studio in central location\n– FREE par
 king\n– Easy access by TTC\n– Fun and friendly class environment\n– 
 FREE social dance included after class for practice and fun!\n– Wide var
 iety of great music ranging from Blues to Top 40\n– Two beginner classes
  to choose from to suit your level\n\nLEVELS:\nBeginner (Level 1 Beginner)
  – for people brand new to West Coast Swing with little or no dance expe
 rience.\n\nBasics Plus (Level 2 Beginner) – for people already comfortab
 le with the basic 6-count and 8-count patterns (ie. left-side pass\, right
 -side pass\, sugar push\, basic whip and basket whip).\n\nDANCE STYLE: Wes
 t Coast Swing\n\nWHEN: 6 Class Series – Starts Sunday July 29\, 2018\nBe
 ginner: 4pm to 5pm\nBasics Plus: 5pm to 6pm\nSocial Dance: 7pm to 9pm\n\nW
 HERE: Rhythm &amp\; Motion Dance Studio\, 3352 Dundas Street West\, Toront
 o (corner of Runnymede and Dundas)\n\nFor more information or to pre-regis
 ter\, click the “More Info” tab at the top of this listing\, or visit 
 www.ShelleyDance.com\n\n*** FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS ***\n\nQ. Do I need
  any previous dance experience?\n\nAbsolutely not! The Level 1 Beginner cl
 ass is perfect for you. You can learn West Coast Swing in three easy steps
 \, even if you have never danced before and have two left feet.\n\nQ. Do I
  need to come with a partner?\n\nNo\, you do NOT need a partner for the cl
 ass. If you have someone you would like to learn with\, that is fantastic.
  But you do not need a partner to take the class. The class is structured 
 so you rotate with different partners throughout the class. It’s a great
  way to meet new people and you also get to dance with a variety of leads 
 and follows.\n\nQ. What type of shoes should I wear?\n\nIf you already hav
 e dance shoes\, then bring those. If you don’t have dance shoes\, then s
 omething with a leather or suede sole is best. If not\, then just wear you
 r most comfortable pair of shoes.\n\nQ. What type of clothes should I wear
  to class?\n\nWear whatever you will feel most comfortable in. West Coast 
 Swing is a very casual dance so wear your favorite jeans and t-shirt if yo
 u want.\n\nQ. Who is the instructor?\n\nYour instructor is Shelley Saxena.
  Shelley has been dancing\, studying and competing in West Coast Swing for
  18 years. With an extensive background in Jazz\, Ballet and Modern dance\
 , Shelley now specializes in West Coast Swing. You can contact Shelley at 
 www.ShelleyDance.com\n\nQ. Where can I practice what I’ve learned?\n\nTh
 ere is a social dance after the classes from 7pm to 9pm. The dance is FREE
  for people in the beginner classes.\n\nQ. I still have a question about t
 he class or West Coast Swing. Can you help?\n\nOf course! If you have any 
 other questions\, please don’t hesitate to contact Shelley by clicking t
 he “More Info” tab at the top of this listing\, or visiting her websit
 e www.ShelleyDance.com. She will be very happy to help you any way she can
 .\n\nQ. I’m excited to get started! What’s my next step?\n\nSimply cli
 ck the “More Info” tab at the top of this listing to let Shelley know 
 you’d like to register\, or contact her at her website www.ShelleyDance.
 com (class size is limited so it’s important to make sure you reserve yo
 ur spot). West Coast Swing For Beginners
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2018/07/20130402_TOWestCoast_2339_lyziane.jpg
CATEGORIES:West Coast Swing
LOCATION:Rhythm and Motion Studio\, 3352 Dundas St West\, Toronto\, Ontario
 \, GTA\, Canada
GEO:43.665699;-79.481796
