URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/west-coast-swing-ladies-styling-se
 crets-7/
SUMMARY:West Coast Swing – Ladies Styling Secrets
DESCRIPTION:*** Feel and Look Better Than Ever On The Dance Floor! ***\n\nW
 hether you want to add some shaping and style to your West Coast Swing\, o
 r improve the quality of your movement\, this ladies styling class reveals
  all the little secrets to fun and gorgeous West Coast Swing.\n\nYou’ll 
 learn:\n\n– How to move your body with confidence\n– Body isolations\n
 – Beautiful arm styling\n– Shaping variations on basic patterns\n– T
 iming variations\n– Creating beautiful lines\n– How to be the best dan
 cer you can be with any style or level of leader\n\nShelley’s easy to le
 arn ladies styling tips for West Coast Swing will have you looking and fee
 ling awesome on the dance floor!\n\nWHEN:\n\nSaturday\, February 23\, 2019
 \n3pm to 5pm\n1st Floor\, Dovercourt House\, 805 Dovercourt Rd.\n\nPre-reg
 istration by Feb 22 – $25\nAt the door – $30\n\nFor more information o
 r to pre-register\, visit the website below:\n\nClass size is limited so p
 lease register as soon as possible to confirm your spot.\n\nIf you have an
 y questions whatsoever\, please don’t hesitate to contact Shelley.\n\n**
 * FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS ***\n\nQ. Do I need to come with a partner?\n
 \nNo\, you do not need a partner for the class. This is a followers ONLY c
 lass so no partner is required.\n\nQ. What type of shoes should I wear?\n\
 nIf you already have dance shoes\, then bring those. If you don’t have d
 ance shoes\, then something with a leather or suede sole is best. If not\,
  then just wear your most comfortable pair of shoes.\n\nQ. What type of cl
 othes should I wear to class?\n\nWear whatever you will feel most comforta
 ble in. West Coast Swing is a very casual dance so wear your favorite jean
 s and t-shirt if you want.\n\nQ. Who is the instructor?\n\nYour instructor
  is Shelley Saxena. Shelley has been dancing\, studying and competing in W
 est Coast Swing for 18 years. With an extensive background in Jazz\, Balle
 t and Modern dance\, Shelley now specializes in West Coast Swing.\n\nQ. Do
  I need any previous dance experience to take the Styling class?\n\nThis i
 s NOT a class for complete beginners. You must have at least one year of r
 ecent experience as a follower in West Coast Swing and be comfortable with
  the 6-count and 8-count basics.\n\nQ. I still have a question about the c
 lass. Can you help?\n\nOf course! If you have any other questions\, please
  don’t hesitate to contact Shelley by clicking the “More Info” tab a
 t the top of this listing\, or visiting her website ShelleyDance.com. She 
 will be very happy to help you any way she can.\n\nQ. I’m excited to get
  started! What’s my next step?\n\nSimply click the “More Info” tab a
 t the top of this listing to let Shelley know you’d like to register\, o
 r contact her at her website ShelleyDance.com (class size is limited so it
 ’s important to make sure you reserve your spot). West Coast Swing – L
 adies Styling Secrets
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2019/01/ladies-styling.jpg
CATEGORIES:West Coast Swing
LOCATION:Dovercourt House\, 805 Dovercourt Road\, Toronto\, Ontario\, Canad
 a
GEO:43.662777;-79.429512
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=805 Dovercourt Road\, Toron
 to\, Ontario\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Dovercourt House:geo:43.6
 62777,-79.429512
END:VEVENT
