DTSTAMP:20190207T053547Z
URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/west-coast-swing-for-beginners-5/
SUMMARY:West Coast Swing for Beginners
DESCRIPTION:*** West Coast Swing Dance For Beginners ***\n\nIf you have eve
 r wanted to try West Coast Swing\, now is your chance with these fun class
 es designed for people with little or no experience with West Coast Swing\
 , or dancing in general.\n\nYou will learn the basic steps and patterns of
  West Coast Swing in a fun and friendly class environment.\n\n– No previ
 ous dance experience needed\n– No partner needed\n– Taught by Shelley 
 Saxena – one of Toronto’s top rated West Coast Swing instructors\n– 
 Comfortable dance studio in central location\n– FREE parking\n– Easy a
 ccess by TTC\n– Fun and friendly class environment\n– FREE social danc
 e included after class for practice and fun!\n– Wide variety of great mu
 sic ranging from Blues to Top 40\n– Two beginner classes to choose from 
 to suit your level\n\nLEVELS:\nBeginner (Level 1 Beginner) – for people 
 brand new to West Coast Swing with little or no dance experience.\n\nBasic
 s Plus (Level 2 Beginner) – for people already comfortable with the basi
 c 6-count and 8-count patterns (ie. left-side pass\, right-side pass\, sug
 ar push\, basic whip and basket whip).\n\nDANCE STYLE: West Coast Swing\n\
 nWHEN: 6 Class Series – Starts Sunday February 24\, 2019\nBeginner: 4pm 
 to 5pm\nBasics Plus: 5pm to 6pm\nSocial Dance: 7pm to 9pm\n\nWHERE: Rhythm
  &amp\; Motion Dance Studio\, 3352 Dundas Street West\, Toronto (corner of
  Runnymede and Dundas)\n\nFor more information or to pre-register\, click 
 the “More Info” tab at the top of this listing\, or visit www.ShelleyD
 ance.com\n\n*** FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS ***\n\nQ. Do I need any previou
 s dance experience?\n\nAbsolutely not! The Level 1 Beginner class is perfe
 ct for you. You can learn West Coast Swing in three easy steps\, even if y
 ou have never danced before and have two left feet.\n\nQ. Do I need to com
 e with a partner?\n\nNo\, you do NOT need a partner for the class. If you 
 have someone you would like to learn with\, that is fantastic. But you do 
 not need a partner to take the class. The class is structured so you rotat
 e with different partners throughout the class. It’s a great way to meet
  new people and you also get to dance with a variety of leads and follows.
 \n\nQ. What type of shoes should I wear?\n\nIf you already have dance shoe
 s\, then bring those. If you don’t have dance shoes\, then something wit
 h a leather or suede sole is best. If not\, then just wear your most comfo
 rtable pair of shoes.\n\nQ. What type of clothes should I wear to class?\n
 \nWear whatever you will feel most comfortable in. West Coast Swing is a v
 ery casual dance so wear your favorite jeans and t-shirt if you want.\n\nQ
 . Who is the instructor?\n\nYour instructor is Shelley Saxena. Shelley has
  been dancing\, studying and competing in West Coast Swing for 18 years. W
 ith an extensive background in Jazz\, Ballet and Modern dance\, Shelley no
 w specializes in West Coast Swing. You can contact Shelley at www.ShelleyD
 ance.com\n\nQ. Where can I practice what I’ve learned?\n\nThere is a soc
 ial dance after the classes from 7pm to 9pm. The dance is FREE for people 
 in the beginner classes.\n\nQ. I still have a question about the class or 
 West Coast Swing. Can you help?\n\nOf course! If you have any other questi
 ons\, please don’t hesitate to contact Shelley by clicking the “More I
 nfo” tab at the top of this listing\, or visiting her website www.Shelle
 yDance.com. She will be very happy to help you any way she can.\n\nQ. I’
 m excited to get started! What’s my next step?\n\nSimply click the “Mo
 re Info” tab at the top of this listing to let Shelley know you’d like
  to register\, or contact her at her website www.ShelleyDance.com (class s
