URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/right-to-dance-free-contemporary-c
 lasses/
SUMMARY:Right To Dance Free Contemporary Classes
DESCRIPTION:FREE Drop In Dance Class for young people 16-29 living on the m
 argins.\nEvery Wed 6-8pm\n+ Free Meal 4-5pm\n\nContemporary Dance is fun\,
  physical\, and emotionally expressive dance form. Come learn it in an aff
 irming environment for LGBTQ &amp\; BIPOC folks.\n\nEach session will have
  a guided warm up\, stretch and conditioning\, movement in the centre\, &a
 mp\; movement that travels through the space. This class draws from variou
 s movement techniques including: modern\, contemporary\, kung fu\, hip hop
 \, street styles\, &amp\; ballet\, to create a hybrid form of contemporary
  dance.\n\n**No experience necessary. Dialogue is encouraged. Movement var
 iations with lower impact are discussed and provided to create greater acc
 essibility\n\nClasses will be facilitated by Sze-Yang Ade-Lam of ILL NANA/
 DiverseCity Dance Company- a queer multiracial dance company that embraces
  difference as strength and are committed to changing the landscape of dan
 ce by performing our stories on stage as well as providing more accessible
  education and performance opportunities for LGBTTIQQ2S communities priori
 tizing people of colour\, various body types\, backgrounds\, classes\, and
  abilities. ILL NANA/DCDC coordinates and facilitates Right To Dance: free
  affirming drop-in dance classes and 2 month intensive.\n\n&nbsp\; Right T
 o Dance Free Contemporary Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2019/02/21821_image_51758549_2189399944415720_1527343417598672896_o.jpg
CATEGORIES:Contemporary,LGBT
LOCATION:SKETCH Working Arts\, 180 Shaw Street\, lower level\, Toronto\, ON
 \, M6J 2W5\, Canada
