BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Toronto Dance
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/
UID:2802@torontodance.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20190302T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20190302T173000
DTSTAMP:20190112T200333Z
URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/air-steps-lifts-tricks-and-drops-d
 ance-workshop/
SUMMARY:Air Steps\, Lifts\, Tricks and Drops Dance Workshop
DESCRIPTION:3pm to 5:30pm\, Saturday March 2.\n\nTeachers: Simon &amp\; Car
 lynn.\n\nCome do some of the best and most fun stuff in partner dance! At 
 least that's what we think.\n\nLearn some air steps\, lifts\, tricks and d
 rops suitable for Lindy Hop and other partner dances.\n\nThere will be no 
 overlap with the moves taught in our Saturday January 5 workshop.\n\nThis 
 is an all levels workshop\, but you must be athletic and bring your own da
 nce partner. In addition\, the lead must able to easily carry the follower
  around.\n\nNote this student comment from a 2011 Swing Toronto air steps 
 workshop taught by Simon &amp\; Cheryl: “They weren’t kidding about th
 e athletic part.”\n\nYou need to bring your own dance partner for the wo
 rkshop because there is no partner rotation in workshops of this kind\, un
 like all other workshops and classes Swing Toronto presents.\n\nLeads plea
 se bring shoes that have good traction especially under your heels (such a
 s running shoes and shoes with rubber heels).\n\nFollowers please bring sh
 oes that are good for landing from a jump (shoes that provide traction and
  absorption such as running shoes).\n\nFollowers\, knee pads are suggested
  (but not required) for one of the tricks we may do. They will not be need
 ed once you have it\, but may be helpful while learning.\n\nDo of course b
 ring clothes that are comfortable and allow freedom of movement\, and that
  you don't mind being upside down in.\n\nIf you wish you can come in a gro
 up of three\, as long as the three include one very sporting and fit leade
 r or follower who is happy to do double duty working and dancing with the 
 other two.\n\nComments on Carlynn &amp\; Simon's January 5\, 2019 Air Step
 s\, Lifts\, Dips\, Floorials Workshop:\n"This was my first aerials / dips 
 workshop and it was incredible! You both are great teachers\, making the m
 oves easy to follow and understand. Thank you!" (Ayla.)\n"Great workshop a
 nd very clear and balanced."\n"Love the workshop. ... I had a blast and wo
 uld love to do more!"\n"Open to all. Wonderful and engaging workshop. Defi
 nitely worth the trip out from Sudbury!"\n"Great workshop. We had so much 
 fun." (Alexander.)\n"Fantastic workshop! I appreciated the thorough breakd
 own of the moves\, and the individual correction and attention provided."\
 n"Excellent workshop. Nice pace that allowed for me to build comfort and c
 onfidence with aerials. I felt very safe."\n"Accessible to beginners but c
 an learn even as experts."\n"Instructors were really engaging! Moved throu
 gh more material than expected. Learned not just technicalities but gracef
 ulness too. :-)"\n"Awesome workshop!! ..."\n"Loved it! I'll be back!"\n"Th
 anks for a fantastic workshop Simon and Carlynn!" (Jackie.)\nParticipants 
 will be asked to sign a waiver\, and also a confirmation that they are fre
 e from injuries. This is a condition of taking the workshop.\n\n$35 each\,
  $30 for full-time students. Air Steps\, Lifts\, Tricks and Drops Dance Wo
 rkshop
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2019/01/Simon.Carlynn.StJames.June18.jpg
CATEGORIES:Ballroom,Blues,Folk,Latin,Lindy Hop,Other,Swing
LOCATION:Dovercourt House\, 805 Dovercourt Road\, Toronto\, Ontario\, Canad
 a
GEO:43.662777;-79.429512
