URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/west-coast-swing-for-beginners-6/
SUMMARY:West Coast Swing for Beginners
DESCRIPTION:*** West Coast Swing Dance For Beginners ***\n\nIf you have eve
 r wanted to try West Coast Swing\, now is your chance with these fun class
 es designed for people with little or no experience with West Coast Swing\
 , or dancing in general.\n\nYou will learn the basic steps and patterns of
  West Coast Swing in a fun and friendly class environment.\n\n– No previ
 ous dance experience needed\n– No partner needed\n– Taught by Shelley 
 Saxena – one of Toronto’s top rated West Coast Swing instructors\n– 
 Comfortable dance studio in central location\n– Easy access by TTC\n– 
 Fun and friendly class environment\n– Social dance included after class 
 for practice and fun!\n– Wide variety of great music ranging from Blues 
 to Top 40\n– Two beginner classes to choose from to suit your level\n\nL
 EVELS:\nBeginner (Level 1 Beginner) – for people brand new to West Coast
  Swing with little or no dance experience.\n\nBasics Plus (Level 2 Beginne
 r) – for people already comfortable with the basic 6-count and 8-count p
 atterns (ie. left-side pass\, right-side pass\, sugar push\, basic whip an
 d basket whip).\n\nDANCE STYLE: West Coast Swing\n\nWHEN: 6 Class Series 
 – Starts Sunday April 14\, 2019\nBeginner: 4pm to 5pm\nBasics Plus: 5pm 
 to 6pm\nSocial Dance: 7pm to 9pm\n\nWHERE: Rhythm &amp\; Motion Dance Stud
 io\, 3352 Dundas Street West\, Toronto (corner of Runnymede and Dundas)\n\
 nFor more information or to pre-register\, click the “More Info” tab a
 t the top of this listing\, or visit www.ShelleyDance.com\n\n*** FREQUENTL
 Y ASKED QUESTIONS ***\n\nQ. Do I need any previous dance experience?\n\nAb
 solutely not! The Level 1 Beginner class is perfect for you. You can learn
  West Coast Swing in three easy steps\, even if you have never danced befo
 re and have two left feet.\n\nQ. Do I need to come with a partner?\n\nNo\,
  you do NOT need a partner for the class. If you have someone you would li
 ke to learn with\, that is fantastic. But you do not need a partner to tak
 e the class. The class is structured so you rotate with different partners
  throughout the class. It’s a great way to meet new people and you also 
 get to dance with a variety of leads and follows.\n\nQ. What type of shoes
  should I wear?\n\nIf you already have dance shoes\, then bring those. If 
 you don’t have dance shoes\, then something with a leather or suede sole
  is best. If not\, then just wear your most comfortable pair of shoes.\n\n
 Q. What type of clothes should I wear to class?\n\nWear whatever you will 
 feel most comfortable in. West Coast Swing is a very casual dance so wear 
 your favorite jeans and t-shirt if you want.\n\nQ. Who is the instructor?\
 n\nYour instructor is Shelley Saxena. Shelley has been dancing\, studying 
 and competing in West Coast Swing for 18 years. With an extensive backgrou
 nd in Jazz\, Ballet and Modern dance\, Shelley now specializes in West Coa
 st Swing. You can contact Shelley at www.ShelleyDance.com\n\nQ. Where can 
 I practice what I’ve learned?\n\nThere is a social dance after the class
 es from 7pm to 9pm. The dance is FREE for people in the beginner classes.\
 n\nQ. I still have a question about the class or West Coast Swing. Can you
  help?\n\nOf course! If you have any other questions\, please don’t hesi
 tate to contact Shelley by clicking the “More Info” tab at the top of 
 this listing\, or visiting her website www.ShelleyDance.com. She will be v
 ery happy to help you any way she can.\n\nQ. I’m excited to get started!
  What’s my next step?\n\nSimply click the “More Info” tab at the top
  of this listing to let Shelley know you’d like to register\, or contact
  her at her website ShelleyDance.com (class size is limited so it’s impo
 rtant to make sure you reserve your spot). West Coast Swing for Beginners
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2019/03/wcs-770x513.jpg
CATEGORIES:West Coast Swing
LOCATION:Rhythm and Motion Studio\, 3352 Dundas St West\, Toronto\, Ontario
 \, GTA\, Canada
