URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/citadel-compagnie-against-nature/
SUMMARY:Citadel + Compagnie: Against Nature
DESCRIPTION:Citadel + Compagnie: Against Nature — May 22-25 &amp\; May 29
 -June 1\, 2019\n\nCitadel + Compagnie presents the highly anticipated retu
 rn of the 2016 Dora Mavor Moore Award-nominated production of James Kudelk
 a’s Against Nature\, running May 22-25 &amp\; May 29-June 1\, 2019 at 8p
 m at the Citadel: Ross Centre for Dance. The second in a series of salon-s
 tyle creations for Citadel + Compagnie\, Against Nature incorporates one d
 ancer\, two singers and three musicians with original composition by James
  Rolfe and libretto by Alex Poch-Goldin. Hailed as “a must-see” (Toron
 to Star)\, Against Nature pulls from Joris-Karl Huysmans novel by the same
  name. Says Kudelka of the novel\, “It is sensuous\, celebrating smell\,
  touch\, colour\, skin\, poetry\, painting\, sex and home decorating\; to 
 the point of decadence.”\n\nTickets $20-$25. Full details at citadelcie.
 com. Citadel + Compagnie: Against Nature
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2019/04/Against-Nature-photo-by-Jeremy-Mimnagh.jpg
CATEGORIES:Contemporary
LOCATION:Citadel Ross Centre for Dance\, 304 Parliament St\, Toronto\, Onta
 rio\, M5A2Z6\, Canada
