 -day-may-24th-2019/
SUMMARY:Toronto Celebrates World Lindy Hop Day
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Celebrates World Lindy Hop Day is BACK FRIDAY May 24th\
 , 2019 w/ Martin Loomer's Orange Devils (18 piece Big Band!) at the Jam Fa
 ctory T.O.\n\nThis is a night for lovers of Big Band Music &amp\; Swing Da
 nce. Step back in time to the Swing Era of the 1930's &amp\; 40's!\n\nBegi
 nner lesson will be available (no partner needed).\n\nSAVE THE DATE as we 
 announce all the details SOON (Including Ticket Pricing &amp\; Times for l
 esson and Band).\n\nABOUT TOWLHD:\n\nEach year\, Toronto has hosted a cele
 bration promoting the spirit of Frankie Manning\, Ambassador of Lindy Hop 
 (the swing dance of the 1930s/40s and today). Festivities fall on or aroun
 d Frankie’s birthday: May 26th. The last 2 years we have shifted our foc
 us only slightly to also encompass ‘World Lindy Hop Day‘ (which is als
 o on May 26th)\, to celebrate everyone who is keeping what Frankie and the
  other originators of Swing help create\, alive today!\n\nTOWLHD is also a
  Fundraiser\, raising money for Toronto Lindy Hop a Not-For-Profit Organiz
 ation.\n\n&nbsp\; Toronto Celebrates World Lindy Hop Day
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2019/02/21843_image_52065895_2276930909005731_7730674853417582592_o.jpg
