DTSTAMP:20190516T185445Z
URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/west-coast-swing-for-beginners-7/
SUMMARY:West Coast Swing for Beginners
DESCRIPTION:*** West Coast Swing Dance For Beginners ***\n\nIf you have eve
 r wanted to try West Coast Swing\, now is your chance with these fun class
 es designed for people with little or no experience with West Coast Swing\
 , or dancing in general.\n\nYou will learn the basic steps and patterns of
  West Coast Swing in a fun and friendly class environment.\n\n– No previ
 ous dance experience needed\n– No partner needed\n– Taught by Shelley 
 Saxena – one of Toronto’s top rated West Coast Swing instructors\n– 
 Comfortable dance studio in central location\n– Easy access by TTC\n– 
 Fun and friendly class environment\n– Social dance included after class 
 for practice and fun!\n– Wide variety of great music ranging from Blues 
 to Top 40\n– Two beginner classes to choose from to suit your level\n\nL
 EVELS:\nBeginner (Level 1 Beginner) – for people brand new to West Coast
  Swing with little or no dance experience.\n\nBasics Plus (Level 2 Beginne
 r) – for people already comfortable with the basic 6-count and 8-count p
 atterns (ie. left-side pass\, right-side pass\, sugar push\, basic whip an
 d basket whip).\n\nDANCE STYLE: West Coast Swing\n\nWHEN: 6 Class Series 
 – Starts Sunday May 26\, 2019\nBeginner: 4pm to 5pm\nBasics Plus: 5pm to
  6pm\nSocial Dance: 7pm to 9pm\n\nWHERE: Rhythm &amp\; Motion Dance Studio
 \, 3352 Dundas Street West\, Toronto (corner of Runnymede and Dundas)\n\nF
 or more information or to pre-register\, click the “More Info” tab at 
 the top of this listing\, or visit www.ShelleyDance.com\n\n*** FREQUENTLY 
 ASKED QUESTIONS ***\n\nQ. Do I need any previous dance experience?\n\nAbso
 lutely not! The Level 1 Beginner class is perfect for you. You can learn W
 est Coast Swing in three easy steps\, even if you have never danced before
  and have two left feet.\n\nQ. Do I need to come with a partner?\n\nNo\, y
 ou do NOT need a partner for the class. If you have someone you would like
  to learn with\, that is fantastic. But you do not need a partner to take 
 the class. The class is structured so you rotate with different partners t
 hroughout the class. It’s a great way to meet new people and you also ge
 t to dance with a variety of leads and follows.\n\nQ. What type of shoes s
 hould I wear?\n\nIf you already have dance shoes\, then bring those. If yo
 u don’t have dance shoes\, then something with a leather or suede sole i
 s best. If not\, then just wear your most comfortable pair of shoes.\n\nQ.
  What type of clothes should I wear to class?\n\nWear whatever you will fe
 el most comfortable in. West Coast Swing is a very casual dance so wear yo
 ur favorite jeans and t-shirt if you want.\n\nQ. Who is the instructor?\n\
 nYour instructor is Shelley Saxena. Shelley has been dancing\, studying an
 d competing in West Coast Swing for 18 years. With an extensive background
  in Jazz\, Ballet and Modern dance\, Shelley now specializes in West Coast
  Swing. You can contact Shelley at www.ShelleyDance.com\n\nQ. Where can I 
 practice what I’ve learned?\n\nThere is a social dance after the classes
  from 7pm to 9pm. The dance is FREE for people in the beginner classes.\n\
 nQ. I still have a question about the class or West Coast Swing. Can you h
 elp?\n\nOf course! If you have any other questions\, please don’t hesita
 te to contact Shelley by clicking the “More Info” tab at the top of th
 is listing\, or visiting her website www.ShelleyDance.com. She will be ver
 y happy to help you any way she can.\n\nQ. I’m excited to get started! W
 hat’s my next step?\n\nSimply click the “More Info” tab at the top o
 f this listing to let Shelley know you’d like to register\, or contact h
 er at her website ShelleyDance.com (class size is limited so it’s import
 ant to make sure you reserve your spot). West Coast Swing for Beginners
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2019/05/20130402_TOWestCoast_2339_lyziane.jpg
CATEGORIES:West Coast Swing
LOCATION:Rhythm and Motion Studio\, 3352 Dundas St West\, Toronto\, Ontario
 \, GTA\, Canada
GEO:43.665699;-79.481796
