X-SOURCE:Toronto Dance
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/
UID:2976@torontodance.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20190602T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20190602T173000
DTSTAMP:20190515T001300Z
URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/air-steps-lifts-drops-tricks-works
 hop/
SUMMARY:Air Steps\, Lifts\, Drops\, Tricks Workshop
DESCRIPTION:3pm to 5:30pm.\n\nTeachers: Simon Threlkeld &amp\; Carlynn Reed
 .\n\nCome do some of the best and most fun stuff in partner dance! At leas
 t that's what we think.\n\nLearn some air steps\, lifts\, tricks and drops
  suitable for Lindy Hop and other partner dances.\n\nThere will be no over
 lap with the moves taught in our previous workshops.\n\nThis is an all lev
 els workshop\, but you must be athletic and bring your own dance partner. 
 In addition\, the lead must able to easily carry the follower around.\n\nN
 ote this student comment from a 2011 Swing Toronto air steps workshop taug
 ht by Simon &amp\; Cheryl: “They weren’t kidding about the athletic pa
 rt.”\n\nYou need to bring your own dance partner for the workshop becaus
 e there is no partner rotation in workshops of this kind\, unlike all othe
 r workshops and classes Swing Toronto presents. Leads please bring shoes t
 hat have good traction especially under your heels (such as running shoes 
 and shoes with rubber heels). Followers please bring shoes that are good f
 or landing from a jump (shoes that provide traction and absorption such as
  running shoes). Do of course bring clothes that are comfortable and allow
  freedom of movement\, and that you don't mind being upside down in.\n\nIf
  you wish you can come in a group of three\, as long as the three include 
 one very sporting and fit leader or follower who is happy to do double dut
 y working and dancing with the other two.\n\nComments on Carlynn &amp\; Si
 mon's January 5\, 2019 Air Steps\, Lifts\, Dips\, Floorials Workshop:\n"Th
 is was my first aerials / dips workshop and it was incredible! You both ar
 e great teachers\, making the moves easy to follow and understand. Thank y
 ou!" (Ayla.)\n"Great workshop and very clear and balanced."\n"Love the wor
 kshop. ... I had a blast and would love to do more!" "Open to all. Wonderf
 ul and engaging workshop. Definitely worth the trip out from Sudbury!"\n"G
 reat workshop. We had so much fun." (Alexander.)\n"Fantastic workshop! I a
 ppreciated the thorough breakdown of the moves\, and the individual correc
 tion and attention provided."\n"Excellent workshop. Nice pace that allowed
  for me to build comfort and confidence with aerials. I felt very safe."\n
 "Accessible to beginners but can learn even as experts."\n"Instructors wer
 e really engaging! Moved through more material than expected. Learned not 
 just technicalities but gracefulness too. :-)"\n"Awesome workshop!! ..."\n
 "Loved it! I'll be back!"\n"Thanks for a fantastic workshop Simon and Carl
 ynn!" (Jackie.)\n\nParticipants will be asked to sign a waiver\, and also 
 a confirmation that they are free from injuries. This is a condition of ta
 king the workshop.\n\n$35 each\, $30 for full-time students. Air Steps\, L
 ifts\, Drops\, Tricks Workshop
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2019/05/Simon.Carlynn.StJames.June18.jpg
CATEGORIES:Ballroom,Blues,East Coast Swing,Latin,Lindy Hop,Musical
 Theatre,Other,Swing,Vintage
LOCATION:Dovercourt House\, 805 Dovercourt Road\, Toronto\, Ontario\, Canad
 a
GEO:43.662777;-79.429512
