BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Toronto Dance
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/
UID:3016@torontodance.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20190703T184500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20190703T193000
DTSTAMP:20190620T025215Z
URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/palabra-flamencos-fox-woman/
SUMMARY:Palabra Flamenco's Fox Woman
DESCRIPTION:Palabra Flamenco presents\nFOX WOMAN\nin association with the T
 he Toronto Fringe\n\nFOX WOMAN is a 45-minute performance of flamenco danc
 e and guitar alongside oral storytelling. When a mysterious and powerful f
 ox woman appears unexpectedly in his hut\, a lonely hunter is forced to ch
 oose between the wild and the tamed. How to accommodate one another? Befor
 e our hatred of the wild\, before today's ecological crisis\, there was a 
 love affair.\n\nFlamenco dancer and storyteller Denise Yeo retells this Si
 berian myth accompanied by her husband\, accomplished flamenco guitarist G
 areth Owen. With an array of evocative\, traditional flamenco dances\, Yeo
  embodies Fox Woman and the Hunter through hypnotic and improvised movemen
 t and rhythm\, drenched with the darkest impulses.\n\nFox Woman tells a st
 ory about our relationship with the wild — in ourselves and others — a
 nd our emerging ecological crisis. It's also a story that empowers us\, in
  our human relationships\, to leave situations that are not safe.\n\n“Th
 ere’s virtuosity to burn… Let it wash over you.”\n— The Georgia St
 raight\n\n"Passionate and desolate ... A gift to behold!"\n— Showbill Ca
 nada\n\n“Denise Yeo is a spitfire..."\n— Janis La Couvée\, theatre re
 viewer\n\n“Gareth Owen plays like he has a hundred fingers…”\n— Th
 e Georgia Straight\n\nTICKETS\nOnline: https://fringetoronto.com/fringe/sh
 ow/palabra-flamenco-fox-woman\nTelephone: 416-966-1062\nIn-person: at the 
 Fringe Box Office at 275 Bathurst Street or at the venue one hour prior to
  performances.\n\nFacebook Event: https://www.facebook.com/events/69417950
 4392479/\n\nVENUE: Streetcar Crowsnest Scotiabank Studio (345 Carlaw Avenu
 e)\n\nPERFORMANCES\nJuly 3 (6:45pm)\,\nJuly 5 (9:30pm)\,\nJuly 6 (8:30pm)\
 ,\nJuly 7 (3:15pm)\,\nJuly 9 (4:30pm)\,\nJuly 11 (6:00pm)\,\nJuly 13 (1:30
 pm).\n\nShows start on-time and latecomers are not permitted.\n\nWebsite: 
 https://www.palabraflamenco.ca/foxwoman\nFacebook: https://www.facebook.co
 m/PalabraFlamenco/\nTwitter: https://twitter.com/PalabraFlamenco\nInstagra
 m: http://instagram.com/palabraflamenco Palabra Flamenco&#039\;s Fox Woman
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2019/06/11x17-TO-Fringe-POSTER-v3.jpg
CATEGORIES:Flamenco
LOCATION:Streetcar Crowsnest Scotiabank Studio\, 345 Carlaw Avenue\, Toront
 o\, Ontario\, Canada
GEO:43.6651756;-79.34149509999997
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=345 Carlaw Avenue\, Toronto
 \, Ontario\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Streetcar Crowsnest Scotiab
 ank Studio:geo:43.6651756,-79.34149509999997
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Toronto Dance
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/
UID:3026@torontodance.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20190703T184500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20190703T193000
DTSTAMP:20190630T001527Z
URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/palabra-flamencos-fox-woman-8/
SUMMARY:Palabra Flamenco's Fox Woman
DESCRIPTION:Palabra Flamenco presents\nFOX WOMAN\nin association with the T
 he Toronto Fringe\nVENUE: Streetcar Crowsnest Studio (345 Carlaw Avenue).\
 n\nFOX WOMAN is a 45-minute depth-charge of flamenco dance and music combi
 ned with oral storytelling. When a mysterious and powerful fox woman appea
 rs unexpectedly in his hut\, a lonely hunter is forced to choose between t
 he wild and the tamed. Their relationship grows. How to accommodate one an
 other? What do we risk when we accommodate too much? And if violence emerg
 es\, do we recognize it? Do we leave? Before the West cultivated hatred of
  the wild\, before today's ecological crisis\, there was a love affair.\n\
 nFlamenco dancer and storyteller Denise Yeo retells this Siberian myth acc
 ompanied by her husband\, accomplished flamenco guitarist Gareth Owen. Wit
 h an array of evocative\, traditional flamenco dances\, Yeo embodies Fox W
 oman and the Hunter through hypnotic and improvised movement and rhythm\, 
 drenched with the darkest impulses.\n\nFlamenco has its origins around the
  hearth fire. Known for its contrast of incendiary emotion and control\, p
 ercussive rhythms\, and expansive representations of womanhood that includ
 e strength\, resiliency\, playfulness\, mockery\, empowerment\, and pride\
 , it is uniquely equipped for this story. This is joy tall as the flame\, 
 joy with ash in its teeth.\n\nFox Woman tells a story about our relationsh
 ip with the wild — in ourselves and others — and our emerging ecologic
 al crisis. It's also a story that empowers us\, in our human relationships
 \, to leave situations that are not safe.\n\n“There’s virtuosity to bu
 rn… Let it wash over you.”\n— The Georgia Straight\n\n"Passionate an
 d desolate ... A gift to behold!"\n— Showbill Canada\n\n“Denise Yeo is
  a spitfire..."\n— Janis La Couvée\, theatre reviewer\n\n“Gareth Owen
  plays like he has a hundred fingers…”\n— The Georgia Straight\n\nSt
 arring: Denise Yeo and Gareth Owen.\nArtistic Director: Denise Yeo.\nProdu
 ced by: Garth Martens.\n\nFox Woman is part of the 2019 Toronto Fringe Fes
 tival.\n\nTICKETS are purchased for $11 online at https://bit.ly/2IElhf2\,
  by telephone 416-966-1062\, or in person at the Fringe Box Office at 275 
 Bathurst Street (in the Hockey Rink south of Scadding Court) or at the ven
 ue one hour prior to performances.\n\nPERFORMANCES\nJuly 3 6:45pm\nJuly 5 
 9:30pm\nJuly 6 8:30pm\nJuly 7 3:15pm\nJuly 9 4:30pm\nJuly 11 6:00pm\nJuly 
 13 1:30pm\n\nShows start on-time and latecomers are not permitted.\n\n&nbs
 p\; Palabra Flamenco&#039\;s Fox Woman
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2019/06/11x17-TO-Fringe-POSTER-v3.jpg
CATEGORIES:Flamenco
LOCATION:Streetcar Crowsnest Scotiabank Studio\, 345 Carlaw Avenue\, Toront
 o\, Ontario\, Canada
GEO:43.6651756;-79.34149509999997
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=345 Carlaw Avenue\, Toronto
 \, Ontario\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Streetcar Crowsnest Scotiab
 ank Studio:geo:43.6651756,-79.34149509999997
END:VEVENT
