URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/palabra-flamencos-fox-woman-2/
SUMMARY:Palabra Flamenco's Fox Woman
DESCRIPTION:Palabra Flamenco presents\nFOX WOMAN\nin association with the T
 he Toronto Fringe\n\nFOX WOMAN is a 45-minute performance of flamenco danc
 e and guitar alongside oral storytelling. When a mysterious and powerful f
 ox woman appears unexpectedly in his hut\, a lonely hunter is forced to ch
 oose between the wild and the tamed. How to accommodate one another? Befor
 e our hatred of the wild\, before today's ecological crisis\, there was a 
 love affair.\n\nFlamenco dancer and storyteller Denise Yeo retells this Si
 berian myth accompanied by her husband\, accomplished flamenco guitarist G
 areth Owen. With an array of evocative\, traditional flamenco dances\, Yeo
  embodies Fox Woman and the Hunter through hypnotic and improvised movemen
 t and rhythm\, drenched with the darkest impulses.\n\nFox Woman tells a st
 ory about our relationship with the wild — in ourselves and others — a
 nd our emerging ecological crisis. It's also a story that empowers us\, in
  our human relationships\, to leave situations that are not safe.\n\n“Th
 ere’s virtuosity to burn… Let it wash over you.”\n— The Georgia St
 raight\n\n"Passionate and desolate ... A gift to behold!"\n— Showbill Ca
 nada\n\n“Denise Yeo is a spitfire..."\n— Janis La Couvée\, theatre re
 viewer\n\n“Gareth Owen plays like he has a hundred fingers…”\n— Th
 e Georgia Straight\n\nTICKETS\nOnline: https://fringetoronto.com/fringe/sh
 ow/palabra-flamenco-fox-woman\nTelephone: 416-966-1062\nIn-person: at the 
 Fringe Box Office at 275 Bathurst Street or at the venue one hour prior to
  performances.\n\nFacebook Event: https://www.facebook.com/events/69417950
 4392479/\n\nVENUE: Streetcar Crowsnest Scotiabank Studio (345 Carlaw Avenu
 e)\n\nPERFORMANCES\nJuly 3 (6:45pm)\,\nJuly 5 (9:30pm)\,\nJuly 6 (8:30pm)\
 ,\nJuly 7 (3:15pm)\,\nJuly 9 (4:30pm)\,\nJuly 11 (6:00pm)\,\nJuly 13 (1:30
 pm).\n\nShows start on-time and latecomers are not permitted.\n\nWebsite: 
 https://www.palabraflamenco.ca/foxwoman\nFacebook: https://www.facebook.co
 m/PalabraFlamenco/\nTwitter: https://twitter.com/PalabraFlamenco\nInstagra
 m: http://instagram.com/palabraflamenco Palabra Flamenco&#039\;s Fox Woman
