URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/dance-the-charleston-at-youth-day-
 toronto-2019/
SUMMARY:Dance the Charleston at YOUTH DAY Toronto 2019
DESCRIPTION:The FREE annual family Festival applauds young aspiring Artists
 \, focusing from little kids right through to 29 year olds\, showcasing th
 eir MUSIC\, DANCE\, ART\, PHOTOGRAPHY\, FASHION and FILM at the non-stop e
 vent which features over 500 YD participants during the fun day.  Youth D
 ay (YD) will again host around 40\,000 visitors\, while also closing down 
 Yonge Street from Dundas south to Queen to accommodate its vibrant YD Stre
 et Market with sumptuous Foods\, interesting Artisans\, valuable Community
  Organizations.\n\nDuring this Federal Election year\, ALL Candidates incl
 uding the Prime Minister are invited to attend. YD will also host a Diplom
 atic Delegation from Jamaica.\n\nThis Summer YOUTH DAY is also challenging
  Canada to set a new World Record in keeping with this year’s theme: “
 Looking back 100 years”\, and inviting ALL to dance to “The Charlston
 ” on the Square and Yonge Street closure! And why not Dress in Costume a
 nd enjoy the FUN…\nABOUT YOUTH DAY:\nYOUTH DAY was created by Canadian F
 ounder and Executive Producer Tylaine Duggan in 2006 to engage young peopl
 e\, and encourage them to find a passion in MUSIC\, DANCE\, ART\, PHOTOGRA
 PHY\, FASHION and FILM. The initiative focuses them during the year toward
 s a goal\, and at the festival allows them to showcase their positive achi
 evements across 3 outdoor stages in downtown Toronto\, which also features
  a Youth Gallery for more than 40\,000 visitors – applauding their effor
 ts and helping build self-esteem for our next generation of young people.\
 n\nYOUTH DAY is a non-profit entity operated solely by dedicated Volunteer
 s and caring Partner Organizations\, enabled by Corporate brands sponsorin
 g the operational costs of the festival’s production in a commendable ge
 sture of giving back to their customers\, and showing their valued partici
 pation in the Community. No Artists or Volunteers receive remuneration. Da
 nce the Charleston at YOUTH DAY Toronto 2019
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2019/02/youth-day.png
