URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/leapfrog-frog-in-hands-summer-inte
 nsive-program/
SUMMARY:LeapFrog - Frog in Hand's Summer Intensive Program
DESCRIPTION:If you aspire to create site-specific work\, where do you get s
 tarted? And what if you are a dancer seeking to learn more about acting? W
 hat if you are an actor seeking to deepen your movement practise? If you h
 ave considered any of the above questions\, Frog in Hand’s week-long sum
 mer intensive\, LeapFrog is for you. \nHosted by site-specific dance-theat
 re company Frog in Hand in collaboration with Daniel Levinson of Rapier Wi
 t (Combat for Stage and Screen)\, LEAPfrog will offer integrated training 
 in movement/dance\, site-specific composition and acting. Participants wil
 l be challenged and supported as they approach text\, cultivate their phys
 ical capacity for movement\, deepen their reflective process and learn abo
 ut collaborative creation in a site-specific environment. This compelling 
 and fun intensive will take place from August 5th-10th (August 5-6 Toronto
 \, August 7th-10th in Port Credit\, Mississauga)\, culminating in a final 
 showing of participant-generated site-specific work on Saturday August 10t
 h.\nSample Schedule (tbc)\n8:30am Arrival\n9am-10am Physical warm up class
  with Frog in Hand company members\n10am-noon Dance-theatre class co-facil
 itated by Colleen Snell and Daniel Levinson\nNoon-1 LUNCH\n1pm-5pm Collabo
 rative creation\, site-specific project (in situ)\nAbout Frog in Hand\nCol
 leen Snell &amp\; Noelle Hamlyn\, Co-Founders\nWe are a dance-theatre comp
 any based in Mississauga\, Ontario. We are curious about people\, and the 
 spaces we inhabit. Our mission is to uncover\, make\, and share stories th
 rough dance. We contribute to community by sharing resources\, knowledge a
 nd experience through creation\, performance and education.\nWe create int
 egrated dance-theatre experiences that resonate physically\, emotionally a
 nd contextually. We push the boundaries of dance performance through colla
 borative processes that embrace and advocate for embodied ways of knowing 
 about the world. We attend not only to the details of the work we make\, b
 ut also to the processes we use to create our work.\nOur work is innovativ
 e and reflects our passion for dance as a medium that transcends language.
  We are committed to dance that engages with its site and is rooted in com
 munity\; recognizing and honouring diverse stories and storytellers. For 
 more: https://www.froginhand.com/\nAbout Daniel Levinson &amp\; Rapier Wi
 t\nFight Master\, Fight Director’s Canada Owner\, Rapier Wit\nA graduate
  of the York University BFA Acting Conservatory program\, Daniel has been 
 performing\, directing and teaching stage combat professionally since 1991
 . He is the owner of Rapier Wit\, Canada’s oldest stage combat school an
 d production company\, and a founding member of the Riot A.C.T. stunt team
 . He is one of the founding advanced members of Fight Directors Canada\, a
  past president as well as one of only ten FDC Fight Masters in Canada. D
 aniel has created fights for companies such as The Stratford Festival (5 s
 easons)\, Canadian Stage\, Jesus Christ Superstar Broadway\, Volcano Theat
 re\, Actors Repertory Company\, Second City\, A.C.T. Productions\, Shakesp
 eare In the Square\, Factory Theatre\, Shakespeare in the Rough\, Theatre 
 Aquarius\, The Actor’s Repertory Company\, Theatre Passe Muraille\, and 
 The Tarragon Theatre. He is the resident stage combat instructor for Sheri
 dan College\, the University of Toronto’s Theatre and Drama Studies Prog
 ram\, and is a frequent instructor at the University of Waterloo. He also 
 teaches stage combat workshops across Canada and internationally\; worksho
 p highlights include the Fight Directors Canada National Workshop (Banff\,
  Victoria\, Toronto\, Montreal)\, Brock University’s Walker Cultural Lea
 der Series\, Boston University\, Arcadia University\, the International Sc
 uola Brancaleoni Stage Combat Workshop (Italy)\, and the Paddy Crean Inter
 national Art of the Sword Workshop (Banff). Daniel is a member of CAEA and
  ACTRA. For more: https://www.rapierwit.com/\n LeapFrog - Frog in Hand&#03
 9\;s Summer Intensive Program
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2019/07/22786_image.jpg
CATEGORIES:Contemporary
LOCATION:Rapier Wit\, 575 Wellington St West\, Toronto\, ON\, Canada
GEO:43.6422818;-79.4030702
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=575 Wellington St West\, To
 ronto\, ON\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Rapier Wit:geo:43.6422818,-
 79.4030702
END:VEVENT
