URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/west-coast-swing-for-beginners-cla
 ss-plus-social-dance/
SUMMARY:West Coast Swing for Beginners - Class Plus Social Dance
DESCRIPTION:*** West Coast Swing Dance For Beginners ***\n\nIf you have eve
 r wanted to try West Coast Swing\, now is your chance with these fun class
 es designed for people with little or no experience with West Coast Swing\
 , or dancing in general.\n\nYou will learn the basic steps and patterns of
  West Coast Swing in a fun and friendly class environment.\n\n– No previ
 ous dance experience needed\n– No partner needed\n– Taught by Shelley 
 Saxena – one of Toronto’s top rated West Coast Swing instructors\n– 
 Comfortable dance studio in central location\n– Easy access by TTC\n– 
 Fun and friendly class environment\n– Social dance included after class 
 for practice and fun!\n– Wide variety of great music ranging from Blues 
 to Top 40\n– Two beginner classes to choose from to suit your level\n\nL
 EVELS:\nBeginner (Level 1 Beginner) – for people brand new to West Coast
  Swing with little or no dance experience.\n\nBasics Plus (Level 2 Beginne
 r) – for people already comfortable with the basic 6-count and 8-count p
 atterns (ie. left-side pass\, right-side pass\, sugar push\, basic whip an
 d basket whip).\n\nDANCE STYLE: West Coast Swing\n\nWHEN: 6 Class Series 
 – Starts Sunday September 8\, 2019\nBeginner: 4pm to 5pm\nBasics Plus: 5
 pm to 6pm\nSocial Dance: 7pm to 9pm\n\nWHERE: Rhythm &amp\; Motion Dance S
 tudio\, 3352 Dundas Street West\, Toronto (corner of Runnymede and Dundas)
 \n\nFor more information or to pre-register\, click the “More Info” ta
 b at the top of this listing\, or visit https://shelleydance.com\n\n*** FR
 EQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS ***\n\nQ. Do I need any previous dance experience
 ?\n\nAbsolutely not! The Level 1 Beginner class is perfect for you. You ca
 n learn West Coast Swing in three easy steps\, even if you have never danc
 ed before and have two left feet.\n\nQ. Do I need to come with a partner?\
 n\nNo\, you do NOT need a partner for the class. If you have someone you w
 ould like to learn with\, that is fantastic. But you do not need a partner
  to take the class. The class is structured so you rotate with different p
 artners throughout the class. It’s a great way to meet new people and yo
 u also get to dance with a variety of leads and follows.\n\nQ. What type o
 f shoes should I wear?\n\nIf you already have dance shoes\, then bring tho
 se. If you don’t have dance shoes\, then something with a leather or sue
 de sole is best. If not\, then just wear your most comfortable pair of sho
 es.\n\nQ. What type of clothes should I wear to class?\n\nWear whatever yo
 u will feel most comfortable in. West Coast Swing is a very casual dance s
 o wear your favorite jeans and t-shirt if you want.\n\nQ. Who is the instr
 uctor?\n\nYour instructor is Shelley Saxena. Shelley has been dancing\, st
 udying and competing in West Coast Swing for 18 years. With an extensive b
 ackground in Jazz\, Ballet and Modern dance\, Shelley now specializes in W
 est Coast Swing. You can contact Shelley at https://shelleydance.com\n\nQ.
  Where can I practice what I’ve learned?\n\nThere is a social dance afte
 r the classes from 7pm to 9pm. The dance is FREE for people in the beginne
 r classes.\n\nQ. I still have a question about the class or West Coast Swi
 ng. Can you help?\n\nOf course! If you have any other questions\, please d
 on’t hesitate to contact Shelley by clicking the “More Info” tab at 
 the top of this listing\, or visiting her website ShelleyDance.com. She wi
 ll be very happy to help you any way she can.\n\nQ. I’m excited to get s
 tarted! What’s my next step?\n\nSimply click the “More Info” tab at 
 the top of this listing to let Shelley know you’d like to register\, or 
 contact her at her website https://ShelleyDance.com (class size is limited
  so it’s important to make sure you reserve your spot). West Coast Swing
  for Beginners - Class Plus Social Dance
