URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/fall-for-dance-north-4/
SUMMARY:Fall for Dance North
DESCRIPTION:Fall for Dance North (FFDN) proudly presents its momentous fift
 h anniversary edition\, October 2–6\, 2019 at MERIDIAN HALL and Ryerson 
 Theatre in partnership with the Ryerson School of Performance. The 2019 fe
 stival will showcase a phenomenal range of expression including a special 
 focus on international Indigenous artists at Ryerson Theatre\, three FFDN 
 commissions\, lots of live music\, and FREE programming at Union Station
 ’s newly restored\, historic West Wing. Audiences will experience the po
 werful style of Brazil’s Grupo Corpo\, the remarkably gifted Indian clas
 sical solo artist Shantala Shivalingappa\, the North American debut of The
  New Zealand Dance Company\, the exquisite artists from The National Balle
 t of Canada\, and much more. Toronto’s own emerging choreographic talent
 s Caroline ‘Lady C’ Fraser and Cody Berry will unveil world premieres\
 , alongside the premiere of FFDN artist-in-residence Anne Plamondon’s FI
 DDLE EMBRACE. Fall for Dance North
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2019/06/FFDN-2019_Shiva-Tarangam-by-Shantala-Shivalingappa_Photo-by-Hector
 -Perez.jpg
CATEGORIES:Ballet,Contemporary,Indian Classical,Indigenous
