URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/stories-in-the-woods-a-theatrical-
 experience-in-the-forest/
SUMMARY:Stories in the Woods: a theatrical experience in the forest
DESCRIPTION:This October for two nights only\, dance-theatre company Frog i
 n Hand will present their latest site-specific production\, Stories in the
  Woods.\n\nThis eerie\, poetic performance will unfold in the forest surro
 unding a heritage site in Mississauga\, where audiences will find themselv
 es in the middle of the story as they are led through the woods to explore
  the sights and sounds around them. Inspired by nature and reflective of t
 he current climate crisis\, the show will bring guests face-to-face with s
 trange and wonderful creatures as they encounter scenes up close amongst t
 he trees.\n\nUnder the direction of sisters Noelle Hamlyn and Colleen Snel
 l\, Stories in the Woods will educate and engage the community to consider
  the environment and drive positive social change.\n\nStories in the Woods
  will take place at 7:00 pm and 9:30 pm on October 4th and 5th at the hist
 oric Small Arms Inspection Building (1352 Lakeshore Rd E\, Mississauga)\, 
 and tickets can be purchased for $25 at https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/storie
 s-in-the-woods-a-performance-by-frog-in-hand-tickets-72273647425. Stories 
 in the Woods: a theatrical experience in the forest
