URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/the-light-and-the-dance/
SUMMARY:The Light and the Dance
DESCRIPTION:Walk into an experience of light and performance at Professor P
 avlo Bosyy's showcase of photography and dance.\n\n\n\n\nAn enthralling ph
 otographic exhibit showcasing the work of Pavlo Bosyy\, Associate Professo
 r of Theatre Production in the School of Performance at Ryerson University
 \, and the intimate relationship between light and dance and the spaces in
  between. This exciting event will incorporate still photography\, perform
 ers moving to light and music\, and a discussion of innovation in light wi
 th the creators of this dynamic experience.\n\nMessage from the Artist:\n\
 nI am interested in creating the aesthetics that helps life performers in 
 storytelling\, enriches the audience’s experience and links the emotiona
 l and the rational elements in the structure of a performing art piece. I 
 explore how different art forms inform each other and produce creative syn
 ergy.\n\nBesides directing and designing the visual elements of theatre an
 d dance shows I practice stage photography\; since 2002 photographing of p
 erformances has been an important part of my creative agenda. I discovered
  that it has become the most effective way to analyze my own work and crea
 tions of my fellow designers\, directors and choreographers. I have photog
 raphed performances of plays\, musicals and dance shows internationally an
 d domestically.\n\nThis photo exhibit is based on the shows of the Ryerson
  School of Performance’s Dance Program\; the artistic theme of the colle
 ction is focused on the interaction of light\, body and movement. Besides 
 exhibiting my photographs\, I included the moving images and videos into t
 he display.\n\nI am very grateful to the curator of the exhibit\, Associat
 e Professor of Dance Tanya Evidente\, Ryerson School of Performance\, the 
 professional ballerina and former soloist of Canada’s National Ballet\, 
 to Dr. Svitlana Kukharenko\, who assisted at curating the exhibit and edit
 ing of the catalogue texts and translated them\, to my student assistant\,
  Angelo Pileggi and graphic designer\, Serhiy Zaplatnikov for their help i
 n creating the catalogue\, and to the wonderful team of the Kirovohrad Reg
 ional Museum of Fine Arts led by Tetyana Tkachenko for the invitation to e
 xhibit my work and for working so hard on mounting of the exhibit. I have 
 been collaborating with the museum for more than thirty years: I initiated
  performing of theatre shows and concerts at the museum main exhibition in
  the late 1980s\; I curated the exhibit Contemporary American Theatre (200
 7) and American Scenography Today: Works of West Virginia University Facul
 ty and Graduate Students (2005)\; the museum hosted the solo exhibits of m
 y art in 2003 and 2015.\n\nThis exhibit was made possible through the gene
 rous support of Ryerson University’s Faculty of Communication and Design
  2016 Creative Innovation Fund. I would like to express my wholehearted gr
 atitude to my colleagues and to the institution I belong to for their cont
 inuous support to my creative endeavours.\n\n&nbsp\;\n\n*Doors close 15 mi
 nutes after event start*\n\n\n\n The Light and the Dance
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2019/10/23362_image.png
CATEGORIES:Ballet,Contemporary
LOCATION:HQ\, 110 Bond Street 2nd Floor\, Toronto\, ON M5B 1X8\, Toronto\, 
 ON\, M5B 1X8\, Canada
