URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/free-exploring-fusion-dance-classe
 s-with-artists-in-motion/
SUMMARY:FREE Exploring Fusion Dance Classes with Artists in Motion
DESCRIPTION:Exploring Fusion. A mixture of dancehall\, Afro\, hip hop\, etc
  movements. The classes will blend dance genres of the African descent\
 , or the diaspora mixed with other influences.\nSeptember 12\, 19 &amp\; 2
 6\nOctober 10 &amp\; 17\n6:00PM - 7:00PM \n• No previous experience req
 uired.\n• Washrooms are available for changing\n• Please bring your wa
 ter bottle.\n\n20 drop-in spots available at each class (first-come\, firs
 t-serve). Please arrive early to sign-in.\n\nArtists in Motion Dance Compa
 ny is a multidisciplinary Toronto dance company incorporating a fusion of 
 dance genres including West African\, hip hop\, dancehall\, jazz and Weste
 rn contemporary. The company consists of gifted young dancers dedicated to
  elevating the art of urban dance.\nLed by Shameka Blake\, 2015 Black Cana
 dian Award recipient for Best Urban Dance Act\, Artists in Motion has work
 ed the stage with Lady Gaga\, Snoop Dogg\, Divine Brown\, Deborah Cox\, Hi
 lary Duff\, Nelly Furtado\, Flo Rida\, Jully Black\, Victoria Duffield\, a
 nd Hedley. The company won MuchMusic’s New.Music.Live. Best Dance Crew\,
  choreographed the Victory Celebration of the 2015 Pan Am Games\, and has 
 participated in the MuchMusic Video Awards\, World Partnership Walk\, Toro
 nto International Film Festival\, and Toronto Pride Festival.\n\nClass Loc
 ation &amp\; Arrival Information\n\n 	Location: Meridian Hall (formerly S
 ony Centre) – Rehearsal Hall\n 	Entrance: Yonge Street Entrance (locate
 d along Yonge Street on the west side of the building halfway between Fron
 t St. and Esplanade).\n 	Doors will open at 5:00PM\n 	TO Live Community Cl
 ass Waiver Form. As a participant\, you only need to complete and return t
 his form once.  After that\, you are eligible to participate in all commu
 nity classes.  Copies of this form are available upon arrival at each cla
 ss.\n 	To Live Community Class Rules &amp\; Regulations\n 	Accessibility:
  The Yonge Street Entrance has no steps and a button to open the doors. T
 o get from the Yonge Street Entrance to the Rehearsal Hall\, there are 29
  steps or 2 elevators. Washrooms are located at the Rehearsal Hall level
 .\n 	Questions: Contact us by email at education@tolive.com or call us 
 at 416-368-6161 ext. 8242\n\n\nWaitlist &amp\; Drop-In Information\n\n\n 	
 Waitlist: We will contact the waitlist with a class reminder and any upda
 tes regarding the number of available drop-in spots. If you are not contac
 ted by Eventbrite to join the class\, you are welcome to attend as a drop-
 in participant (first come\, first served).\n 	Drop-ins: Regardless of be
 ing on the waitlist\, anyone is welcome to arrive as a drop-in participant
 . We will reserve 15 spots per class for drop-ins and will allow additiona
 l drop-ins up to the capacity of the class in case there are cancellations
  or no-shows.\n\n\nEventbrite Registration Policy\n\n 	Registered Particip
 ants are guaranteed a spot until 5:55pm. If registered participants have n
 ot arrived by this time\, their spot will be released to drop-in participa
 nts.\n 	Cancellation Deadline - If you are no longer able to attend\, we 
 kindly ask that you cancel your order or email education@tolive.com to n
 otify us a minimum of 24 hours prior to the class.\n 	After three “no-sh
 ow” instances or three cancellations received with less than 24 hours' n
 otice\, TO Live reserves the right to cancel any future Eventbrite orders 
 you may have for Community Classes.\n\nCheck out our other TO Live communi
 ty classes here!\n\nYonge Street Entrance\n FREE Exploring Fusion Dance Cl
 asses with Artists in Motion
