SUMMARY:In The Abyss
DESCRIPTION:World Premiere\nOctober 30-November 2\, 2019\nChoreographer: Ar
 ia Evans / Political Movement\nPresented by Citadel + Compagnie through Br
 ight Nights\n\nAria Evans’ In The Abyss\, a full-length dance theatre pi
 ece\, applies choreography and metaphor to a heart-driven exploration of t
 he mysteries of life on earth. It explores common expressions of humanity 
 as it intersects with the science that situates us within the universe. Us
 ing the scientific theory that everything is made of stardust\, it dives i
 nto the inescapable physics of the galaxies beyond us in relationship to o
 ur earth-bound lives. It grapples with how to live with purpose\, find mea
 ning in one’s journey\, all the while colliding honest explorations of l
 oneliness with our innate need for connection.\n\nChoreographer: Aria Evan
 s\n\nDancers:\nIrvin Chow\nAna Groppler\nSyreeta Hector\nDavid Norsworthy\
 n\nSet designer: Rachel Forbes\nSound designer: Babak Taghinia\nScenograph
 er: Andy Moro\nWriter: Liam Zarrillo In The Abyss
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2019/09/In-the-Abyss-photo-Photo-by-Aria-Evans-copy.png
CATEGORIES:Contemporary,Experimental,Other
LOCATION:Citadel Ross Centre for Dance\, 304 Parliament St\, Toronto\, Onta
 rio\, M5A2Z6\, Canada
GEO:43.6591;-79.366
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=304 Parliament St\, Toronto
 \, Ontario\, M5A2Z6\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Citadel Ross Centr
 e for Dance:geo:43.6591,-79.366
END:VEVENT
