URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/west-coast-swing-for-beginners-8/
SUMMARY:West Coast Swing for Beginners
DESCRIPTION:*** West Coast Swing Dance For Beginners ***\n\nIf you have eve
 r wanted to try West Coast Swing\, now is your chance with these fun class
 es designed for people with little or no experience with West Coast Swing\
 , or dancing in general.\n\nYou will learn the basic steps and patterns of
  West Coast Swing in a fun and friendly class environment.\n\n– No previ
 ous dance experience needed\n– No partner needed\n– Taught by Shelley 
 Saxena – one of Toronto’s top rated West Coast Swing instructors\n– 
 Comfortable dance studio in central location\n– Easy access by TTC\n– 
 Fun and friendly class environment\n– Social dance included after class 
 for practice and fun!\n– Wide variety of great music ranging from Blues 
 to Top 40\n– Two different beginner classes to choose from to suit your 
 level\n\nLEVELS:\nBeginner (Level 1 Beginner) – for people brand new to 
 West Coast Swing with little or no dance experience.\n\nBasics Plus (Level
  2 Beginner) – for people already comfortable with the basic 6-count and
  8-count patterns (ie. left-side pass\, right-side pass\, sugar push\, bas
 ic whip and basket whip).\n\nDANCE STYLE: West Coast Swing\n\nWHEN: 6 Clas
 s Series – Starts Sunday November 3\, 2019\nBeginner: 4pm to 5pm\nBasics
  Plus: 5pm to 6pm\nSocial Dance: 7pm to 9pm\n\nWHERE: Rhythm &amp\; Motion
  Dance Studio\, 3352 Dundas Street West\, Toronto (corner of Runnymede and
  Dundas)\n\nFor more information or to pre-register\, click the “More In
 fo” tab at the top of this listing\, or visit https://shelleydance.com\n
 \n*** FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS ***\n\nQ. Do I need any previous dance ex
 perience?\n\nAbsolutely not! The Level 1 Beginner class is perfect for you
 . You can learn West Coast Swing in three easy steps\, even if you have ne
 ver danced before and have two left feet.\n\nQ. Do I need to come with a p
 artner?\n\nNo\, you do NOT need a partner for the class. If you have someo
 ne you would like to learn with\, that is fantastic. But you do not need a
  partner to take the class. The class is structured so you rotate with dif
 ferent partners throughout the class. It’s a great way to meet new peopl
 e and you also get to dance with a variety of leads and follows.\n\nQ. Wha
 t type of shoes should I wear?\n\nIf you already have dance shoes\, then b
 ring those. If you don’t have dance shoes\, then something with a leathe
 r or suede sole is best. If not\, then just wear your most comfortable pai
 r of shoes.\n\nQ. What type of clothes should I wear to class?\n\nWear wha
 tever you will feel most comfortable in. West Coast Swing is a very casual
  dance so wear your favorite jeans and t-shirt if you want.\n\nQ. Who is t
 he instructor?\n\nYour instructor is Shelley Saxena. Shelley has been danc
 ing\, studying and competing in West Coast Swing for 18 years. With an ext
 ensive background in Jazz\, Ballet and Modern dance\, Shelley now speciali
 zes in West Coast Swing. You can contact Shelley at https://shelleydance.c
 om\n\nQ. Where can I practice what I’ve learned?\n\nThere is a social da
 nce after the classes from 7pm to 9pm. The dance is FREE for people in the
  beginner classes.\n\nQ. I still have a question about the class or West C
 oast Swing. Can you help?\n\nOf course! If you have any other questions\, 
 please don’t hesitate to contact Shelley by clicking the “More Info”
  tab at the top of this listing\, or visiting her website ShelleyDance.com
 . She will be very happy to help you any way she can.\n\nQ. I’m excited 
 to get started! What’s my next step?\n\nSimply click the “More Info”
  tab at the top of this listing to let Shelley know you’d like to regist
 er\, or contact her at her website https://ShelleyDance.com (class size is
  limited so it’s important to make sure you reserve your spot). West Coa
 st Swing for Beginners
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2017/11/20130402_TOWestCoast_2339_lyziane.jpg
CATEGORIES:West Coast Swing
LOCATION:Rhythm and Motion Studio\, 3352 Dundas St West\, Toronto\, Ontario
 \, GTA\, Canada
GEO:43.665699;-79.481796
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=3352 Dundas St West\, Toron
 to\, Ontario\, GTA\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Rhythm and Motion S
 tudio:geo:43.665699,-79.481796
END:VEVENT
