SUMMARY:Intro to Latin Hustle Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Part 1: Introduction to Latin Hustle!\n\nLatin Hustle\, or "the
  Hustle" was created in the early '70s as Salsa and Mambo dancers tried to
  incorporate their Latin dance moves into the house music of the era: Disc
 o. The most popular counting pattern is "&amp\; 1\, 2 3".\nToday\, Hustle 
 can be danced to almost any top 40's song\, House\, Old House\, and to Dis
 co music!\n\nThis 4 week course will teach you the hustle technique you wi
 ll need to social dance well and some new turns and patterns to add to you
 r repertoire.\n\nOnce students have completed Hustle Foundations Part 2\, 
 they may join the Hustle Level 2 weekly course.\nStudents must start on th
 e first day.\n\nPrice:$60 for 4 weeks.\nFREE for students with a monthly a
 uto renew or annual membership! Intro to Latin Hustle Workshop
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2019/09/nov_hustle.jpg
