URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/canadas-royal-winnipeg-ballet-prof
 essional-division-auditions/
SUMMARY:Canada's Royal Winnipeg Ballet Professional Division Auditions
DESCRIPTION:Canada’s Royal Winnipeg Ballet School (RWB School) is about t
 o embark on a tour of 18 cities across North America in search of talented
  young artists with the potential to become professional dancers and dance
  teachers. Over the duration of the tour dancers will audition for one of 
 three full-time programs:\n\n 	Ballet Academic (academic grade 6 and up)\,
 \n 	Aspirant (post-secondary)\, and\n 	Teacher Training (post-secondary).\
 n\nAuditions run one hour in length and are conducted in groups decided by
  age. Students must be entering academic grade 6 in September 2020 in orde
 r to audition. No previous training is required for young students and no 
 special preparation is required for the class. In the audition\, students 
 will be led through barre and centre work\, during which time they will be
  assessed on talent\, aptitude for classical dance\, flexibility\, coordin
 ation\, musicality\, and artistry of motion.\n\nMaster classes are availab
 le in most locations and are open to auditioning and non-auditioning dance
 rs alike. These classes present an excellent opportunity for dancers to st
 ep outside of their comfort zone and work with different teachers than tho
 se at their home studios. Participating in a new exercise or receiving dir
 ection from a new teacher can resonate in a stronger way.\n\nPlease visit 
 rwb.org/auditions to register and for more information Canada&#039\;s Roya
 l Winnipeg Ballet Professional Division Auditions
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2016/10/ballet-ttc-move-you.jpg
