SUMMARY:WinterSong - dances for a sacred season
DESCRIPTION:Canadian Contemporary Dance Theatre’s WinterSong 2019 warms t
 he hearts of family audiences with a breathtaking tapestry of seasonal dan
 ce inspired by the world’s rich solstice traditions.\n\nA world premiere
  by 2019 Dora Award-winning choreographer Jera Wolfe (Red Sky Performance)
  highlights the program. Hanna Kiel's A Day of Light returns with its cele
 bratory vibrancy for a second year\, alongside WinterSong classics Les Bel
 les Heures and Nowell Sing We by esteemed Canadian dance artist Carol Ande
 rson\, and more.\n\n“… a national treasure”— The Globe and Mail\n\
 n"... a thoroughly refreshing take on the season" — The Toronto Star\n\n
 "... simply breathtaking" — Dance International WinterSong - dances for 
 a sacred season
