URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/the-moving-connections-project-at-
 the-mnjcc/
SUMMARY:The Moving Connections Project at the MNJCC
DESCRIPTION:COMMUNITY DANCE OPPORTUNITY\n\nIn partnership with the MNJCC\, 
 supported by Kaeja d'Dance and the Ontario Trillium Foundation.\n\nWe invi
 te you to join movement workshops which aim to establish meaningful connec
 tions. By exploring moments that have touched us in our lives\, we will cr
 eate small dances together through the mining of participants’ stories a
 nd memories. Led by established professional choreographer Karen Kaeja\, C
 o-Artistic Director of Kaeja d’Dance\, Karen will share her expertise wo
 rking with community engagement dance creation over the past 30 years.\n\n
 No previous dance experience is necessary! First come first served\, so si
 gn up early! We welcome participants from all backgrounds and walks of lif
 e and of all abilities.\n\nWhile all adults (18+) are welcome to join\, th
 is workshop is geared towards the older adult demographic.\n\nSign up for 
 some or all of the sessions! PLEASE NOTE: You can only register for one da
 te at a time. When you finish this registration please begin a new one to 
 join another module.\n\nDATES &amp\; TIMES\nJANUARY 15\, 2020 – 1PM-2:30
 PM\nJANUARY 22\, 2020 – 1PM-2:30PM\nJANUARY 29\, 2020 – 1PM-2:30PM\nFE
 BRUARY 5\, 2020 – 1PM-2:30PM\n\nLOCATION\nMiles Nadal Jewish Community C
 enter\n\nGETTING HERE/ACCESSIBILITY\nThe Miles Nadal Jewish Community Cent
 re is located at 750 Spadina Avenue\, on the south-west corner of Spadina 
 and Bloor\, just steps from Spadina subway station. Parking is available a
 t the ‘Green P’ parking lot located just north of the 7-Eleven that is
  on the north-west corner of Spadina and Bloor\, at the ‘Green P’ park
 ing lot just north of Spadina subway (on the east side of Spadina)\, or on
  side streets. The Miles Nadal JCC is a completely accessible building\, a
 nd is a designated WheelTrans stop.\n\nWater will be provided.\n\nPlease n
 ote\, space is limited – we’ll be in touch to confirm your participati
 on once we collect all responses.\n\nIf you have any questions\, please co
 ntact Beata at urban@kaeja.org or 416-516-6030.\n\n The Moving Connections
  Project at the MNJCC
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2019/11/23660_image-770x480-1.jpg
CATEGORIES:Experimental,Therapeutic
LOCATION:Miles Nadal Jewish Community Centre\, 750 Spadina Ave\, Toronto\, 
 Ontario\, GTA\, Canada
GEO:43.666500;-79.403801
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=750 Spadina Ave\, Toronto\,
  Ontario\, GTA\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Miles Nadal Jewish Comm
 unity Centre:geo:43.666500,-79.403801
END:VEVENT
