URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/8-minutes-17-seconds/
SUMMARY:8 minutes 17 seconds
DESCRIPTION:Propelled by the curiosity between the length of time it takes 
 light to travel from the sun to the earth (8:17)\, Blue Ceiling dance pres
 ents its most ambitious work to date. The company celebrates its 16th year
  with 8 minutes 17 minutes\, on stage from January 23rd to 25th\, 2020\, a
 t 8:00pm at The Theatre Centre with a Pay-What-You-Can community matinée 
 performance on Sunday\, January 26th at 2:30pm. Conceived and co-choreogra
 phed by the company's Artistic Director Lucy Rupert\, 8 minutes 17 seconds
  is a lyrical exploration of the science language inspired by the soul of 
 cosmology and behaviour of light in space through contemporary dance. This
  is part of DanceWorks CoWorks' 2019/20 Series Event.\n\nPerformances run 
 January 23-25 8:00PM - 9:30PM and January 26 2:30PM - 4:00PM. The matinée
  performance on the 26th is a Pay-What-You-Can. 8 minutes 17 seconds
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2019/12/MG_2869.jpg
CATEGORIES:Contemporary
