URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/dance-immersion-presents-limbo-by-
 tabanka-dance-ensemble/
SUMMARY:dance Immersion presents Limbo by Tabanka Dance Ensemble
DESCRIPTION:The Tabanka Dance Ensemble captures the vibrancy of African and
  Caribbean dance with the Canadian debut of Limbo\, February 21 and 22 in 
 North York at the Meridian Arts Centre. Developed by beloved dancer and ch
 oreographer Thomas Prestø\, this newest masterpiece is the bodily express
 ion of emancipation and freedom. Set to an original score by renowned nort
 hern African and Norwegian composer Malika Makouf Rasmussen\, the show is 
 a feast for the senses.\n\nFresh from thrilling audiences the world over\,
  it’s Canada’s turn to experience the Norwegian ensemble’s latest co
 ntemporary work. A deconstruction of the historical ritual and dance\, Lim
 bo is bodies in synch with the rhythm and colour of the African and Caribb
 ean experience and set to the soundtrack of its spirit. A juxtaposition of
  light and dark\, sound and silence\, capture and liberation\, Limbo is a 
 journey of displacement and triumph. Audiences will leave changed.\n\nLear
 n more at danceimmersion.ca and find tickets at meridianartscentre.com.\n\
 nDates\n8:00 pm | Friday\, February 21\, 2020\n1:00pm | Saturday\, Februar
 y 22\, 2020\n8:00 pm | Saturday\, February 22\, 2020\n\nTicket Prices\n$35
 -$45 | Student\, Senior and Groups rates available\n\nLocation\nGreenwin T
 heatre at Meridian Arts Centre\n5040 Yonge St\, North York M2N 6R8\n\nBox 
 Office\nmeridianartscentre.com or 1-855-985-2787 dance Immersion presents 
 Limbo by Tabanka Dance Ensemble
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2019/12/tabanka2.jpg
CATEGORIES:African
LOCATION:Meridian Arts Centre\, 5040 Yonge St\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M2N 6R8
 \, North York\, Canada
GEO:43.766058;-79.414495
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=5040 Yonge St\, Toronto\, O
 ntario\, M2N 6R8\, North York\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Meridian
  Arts Centre:geo:43.766058,-79.414495
END:VEVENT
