URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/air-steps-tricks-lifts-drops-dips-
 workshop/
SUMMARY:Air Steps Tricks Lifts Drops Dips Workshop
DESCRIPTION:We think this is some of the best and most fun stuff in partner
  dance\, (though it is not suited for everyone).\n\nThis material is of co
 urse athletic. You need to be athletic for these workshops. A student comm
 ent from 2011: “They weren’t kidding about the athletic part.”\n\nYo
 u need to come with your own dance partner for these workshops (unlike all
  other workshops and classes\, partners do not rotate in air steps and tri
 cks workshops and classes). (It is o.k. to come as a trio with the one lea
 d or the one follower doing double duty.)\n\nWear athletic or comfortable 
 clothing. For followers running shoes are good (or other shoes with both a
 bsorption and traction). Wear things you are comfortable being upside down
  in. Don’t wear jeans. Leads\, wear shoes that have good traction\, or a
 t least traction under the heel (rubber soles under the heel are good).\n\
 nIn air steps (aerials) one of the partners\, usually the follower\, flies
  or flips in the air. Tricks include lifts\, drops\, floorials (“floor a
 erials” which involve falling to or towards the floor for a slide or spi
 n)\, perches\, carries\, and low or more extreme dips.\n\nComments from pe
 ople who took Carlynn &amp\; Simon’s January 5\, 2019 Air Steps\, Lifts\
 , Dips\, Floorials Workshop:\n“This was my first aerials / dips workshop
  and it was incredible! You both are great teachers\, making the moves eas
 y to follow and understand. Thank you!” (Ayla.)\n“Great workshop and v
 ery clear and balanced.”\n“Love the workshop. … I had a blast and wo
 uld love to do more!”\n“Open to all. Wonderful and engaging workshop. 
 Definitely worth the trip out from Sudbury!”\n“Great workshop. We had 
 so much fun.” (Alexander.)\n“Fantastic workshop! I appreciated the tho
 rough breakdown of the moves\, and the individual correction and attention
  provided.”\n“Excellent workshop. Nice pace that allowed for me to bui
 ld comfort and confidence with aerials. I felt very safe.”\n“Accessibl
 e to beginners but can learn even as experts.”\n“Instructors were real
 ly engaging! Moved through more material than expected. Learned not just t
 echnicalities but gracefulness too. :-)”\n“Awesome workshop!! …”\n
 “Loved it! I’ll be back!”\n“Thanks for a fantastic workshop Simon 
 and Carlynn!” (Jackie.)\n\nComments from people who took Simon\, Cheryl 
 and Katherine’s January 8\, 2011 workshop in Tricks\, Drops\, Floorials\
 , Lifts and Dips:\n“So clear and concise. A real joy to learn from this 
 group.” ~ Paul\n“I can’t wait!!! This was SO much fun last year &#x
 1f642\; EXCITED!!!!!” ~ Dee\n“Thank you for an amazing class! Please 
 keep on doing these regularly – would love to do an airstep class!” ~ 
 Sabrina\n“Great instruction and some really fun exercise. Definitely doi
 ng this again.” ~ Jon\n“Thanks for a great class Simon\, Cheryl and Ka
 therine. It was lots of fun and very challenging!” ~ Cheryl\n\nComments 
 from people who took Simon &amp\; Cheryl’s December 6\, 2014 Floorials a
 nd Drops Workshop (the last workshop in our Fall Air Steps and Tricks seri
 es):\n“Best class ever! This series is very fun!” Alex\n“What a romp
 ! Super fun.” Barb\n“Thanks so much Simon and Cheryl! Fantastic instru
 ction with plenty of one on one feedback and a great focus on safety. Can
 ’t wait for the next one!” Jill\n“Loved these classes Simon &amp\; C
 heryl! Never doubt Cheryl! : ) Can’t wait for the next one.” Karen (an
 d two others)\n“Thank you so much! I had a great time learning some sw
 eet new tricks … safely : )” Name not left.\n“Great class!” G.K.\n
 “Confident direction\, with attention to detail\, all while making it lo
 ok effortless.” Doug\n\nPosted comment from one of the people who took S
 imon &amp\; Cheryl’s December 5\, 2015 Air Steps &amp\; Tricks workshop:
 \n“Great workshop! Thank you Simon and Cheryl! ” ~Michael\n\nCarlynn a
 nd Carlos performing at Canada Super Stars in 2017.\n\nCarlynn performing
  in a dance competition with her former cabaret dance competition partner 
 Carlos. Carlos and Carlynn have won many dance competitions together. Air 
 Steps Tricks Lifts Drops Dips Workshop
