URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/west-coast-swing-for-beginners-cla
 ss-plus-social-dance-2/
SUMMARY:West Coast Swing for Beginners - Class Plus Social Dance
DESCRIPTION:*** West Coast Swing Dance For Beginners ***\n\nIf you have eve
 r wanted to try West Coast Swing\, now is your chance with these fun class
 es designed for people with little or no experience with West Coast Swing\
 , or dancing in general.\n\nYou will learn the basic steps and patterns of
  West Coast Swing in a fun and friendly class environment.\n\n– No previ
 ous dance experience needed\n– No partner needed\n– Taught by Shelley 
 Saxena – one of Toronto’s top rated West Coast Swing instructors\n– 
 Comfortable dance studio in central location\n– Easy access by TTC\n– 
 Fun and friendly class environment\n– Social dance included after class 
 for practice and fun!\n– Wide variety of great music ranging from Blues 
 to Top 40\n– Two different beginner classes to choose from to suit your 
 level\n\nLEVELS:\nBeginner (Level 1 Beginner) – for people brand new to 
 West Coast Swing with little or no dance experience.\n\nBasics Plus (Level
  2 Beginner) – for people already comfortable with the basic 6-count and
  8-count patterns (ie. left-side pass\, right-side pass\, sugar push\, bas
 ic whip and basket whip).\n\nDANCE STYLE: West Coast Swing\n\nWHEN: 6 Clas
 s Series – Starts Sunday March 1\, 2020\nBeginner: 4pm to 5pm\nBasics Pl
 us: 5pm to 6pm\nSocial Dance: 7pm to 9pm\n\nWHERE: Rhythm &amp\; Motion Da
 nce Studio\, 3352 Dundas Street West\, Toronto (corner of Runnymede and Du
 ndas)\n\nFor more information or to pre-register\, click the “More Info
 ” tab at the top of this listing\, or visit https://shelleydance.com\n\n
 *** FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS ***\n\nQ. Do I need any previous dance expe
 rience?\n\nAbsolutely not! The Level 1 Beginner class is perfect for you. 
 You can learn West Coast Swing in three easy steps\, even if you have neve
 r danced before and have two left feet.\n\nQ. Do I need to come with a par
 tner?\n\nNo\, you do NOT need a partner for the class. If you have someone
  you would like to learn with\, that is fantastic. But you do not need a p
 artner to take the class. The class is structured so you rotate with diffe
 rent partners throughout the class. It’s a great way to meet new people 
 and you also get to dance with a variety of leads and follows.\n\nQ. What 
 type of shoes should I wear?\n\nIf you already have dance shoes\, then bri
 ng those. If you don’t have dance shoes\, then something with a leather 
 or suede sole is best. If not\, then just wear your most comfortable pair 
 of shoes.\n\nQ. What type of clothes should I wear to class?\n\nWear whate
 ver you will feel most comfortable in. West Coast Swing is a very casual d
 ance so wear your favorite jeans and t-shirt if you want.\n\nQ. Who is the
  instructor?\n\nYour instructor is Shelley Saxena. Shelley has been dancin
 g\, studying and competing in West Coast Swing for 18 years. With an exten
 sive background in Jazz\, Ballet and Modern dance\, Shelley now specialize
 s in West Coast Swing. You can contact Shelley at https://shelleydance.com
 \n\nQ. Where can I practice what I’ve learned?\n\nThere is a social danc
 e after the classes from 7pm to 9pm. The dance is FREE for people in the b
 eginner classes.\n\nQ. I still have a question about the class or West Coa
 st Swing. Can you help?\n\nOf course! If you have any other questions\, pl
 ease don’t hesitate to contact Shelley by clicking the “More Info” t
 ab at the top of this listing\, or visiting her website ShelleyDance.com. 
 She will be very happy to help you any way she can.\n\nQ. I’m excited to
  get started! What’s my next step?\n\nSimply click the “More Info” t
 ab at the top of this listing to let Shelley know you’d like to register
 \, or contact her at her website ShelleyDance.com (class size is limited s
 o it’s important to make sure you reserve your spot). West Coast Swing f
 or Beginners - Class Plus Social Dance
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2020/02/20130402_TOWestCoast_2339_lyziane.jpg
