URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/free-moving-stories-by-yvonne-ng-t
 hree-week-seniors-movement-workshops/
SUMMARY:FREE Moving Stories by Yvonne Ng: Three Week Seniors Movement Works
 hops
DESCRIPTION:Moving Stories\, is our dance-based arts program created in 201
 5 by Yvonne Ng\, Artistic Director of tiger princess dance projects. Open 
 to older adults ages 60 and beyond\, this workshop offers an introduction 
 into the enriching world of art\, dance and creativity. Participants will 
 be guided through an inspiring creative dance journey.\nParticipants will 
 be led through fun\, playful and gentle warm-ups as an introduction to the
  creative process. Dance and theatre arts will be explored through improvi
 sation and gentle movement exercises.\nOffering a window into the world of
  artmaking\, Moving Stories is an opportunity for self-expression\, sharin
 g and most importantly\, a chance to have fun. This program promises to be
  a positive\, accessible and memorable experience for all.\nFor Older Adul
 ts ages 60 and beyond and suitable for participants with reduced mobility.
  Register through Eventbrite or call us at 416-368-6161 ext 8242!\nTUESDAY
 S 10AM - 11:15AM\nWeek 1 - Tuesday\, March 3\, 2020\nWeek 2 - Tuesday\, Ma
 rch 10\, 2020\nWeek 3 - Tuesday\, March 17\, 2020\nWhat will we do in the 
 Three Week Program?\nEach week will be a one hour and 15 minute session th
 at builds upon the previous week. No previous arts (dance\, music\, visu
 al or theatre) experience required. Only your curiousity and desire to exp
 eriment\, enjoy and share.\nCan I join in at any time or attend as a drop-
 in?\nYes! Although you will benefit more by attending all the classes\, yo
 u can still join in at any time. Drop-ins are welcomed but we encourage 
 participants to attend all three sessions if possible.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n\n\n\n\nAbout Yvonne Ng - Artistic D
 irector\, tiger princess dance projects\n\nBorn and raised in Singapore\, 
 Yvonne Ng is founder\, choreographer\, presenter\, arts educator and artis
 tic director of tiger princess dance projects (1996). The company’s repe
 rtoire includes Yvonne’s works and commissioned work\, creating original
  roles for Bill James\, José Navas\, Dominique Dumais\, Kevin O’Day\, M
 arie-Josée Chartier\, Robert Glumbek\, Stephanie Skura and Tedd Robinson.
  tiger princess dance projects has toured to Singapore\, Ireland\, Italy\,
  Germany\, Australia\, China\, Canada and the USA.\n\nYvonne received her 
 Masters in Intergenerational Practice at York University\, and is a certif
 ied Open Source Forms©\, Dance for Dementia (NBS Baycrest Sharing Dance) 
 and Ashtanga Yoga teacher. Trained in Partners for Youth Empowerment Creat
 ive Facilitator (Level 1&amp\; 2)\, C-I Training&#x2122\;\, Senior Fitness
 (CCAA) and Dance for PD&#x2122\; (Parkinson’s). She has taught at and cr
 eated work for Ryerson and York University\, University of Waterloo and fo
 r 6 years at Juniata College\, Pennsylvania and the Nanyang Academy of Fin
 e Arts and La Salle College of the Arts\, Singapore.\n\nYvonne is the reci
 pient of the 2017 Muriel Sherrin Award\, the 2016 Jacqueline Lemieux Award
 \, K.M. Hunter Artist Award\, New Pioneers Arts Award\, Chalmers Arts Fell
 owship\, Soulpepper’s Community Artist Award and the Ontario Premier’s
  Awards for Excellence in the Arts – New Talent. In 2000\, Yvonne receiv
 ed a Dora Mavor Moore Award for best performance and has received multiple
  nominations.\n\nPhotos are courtesy of tiger princess dance projects and 
 taken by Irvin Chow\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\
 n\n\nClass Details &amp\; Location\n\n\n\n\n\n 	Location: Rehearsal Hall a
 t Meridian Hall (formerly Sony Centre)\n 	Entrance: Meridian Hall’s Re
 hearsal Hall is wheelchair accessible and the workshop entrance is through
  the Yonge Street Entrance (located along Yonge Street on the west side of
  the building halfway between Front St. and Esplanade)\n 	Doors will open 
 at 9:30AM\n 	Suggested Attire: Please bring socks or soft dance slippers/s
 hoes. We will be dancing in them. If you have ballet or jazz slippers\, yo
 u’re welcome to bring them.\n 	Accessibility: The Yonge Street Entrance
  is accessible and has an automatic door opener. To get from the Yonge Str
 eet Entrance to the Rehearsal Hall\, there are 29 steps or 2 elevators. Wa
 shrooms are located at the Rehearsal Hall level.\n 	Waiver and Rules &amp\
 ; Regulations: All new community class participants are required to sign 
 a TO Live Community Class Waiver Form before participating. Copies will 
 be provided at the class. Click here to view the To Live Community Class 
 Rules &amp\; Regulations.\n 	Questions? Contact us by email at education
 @tolive.com or call us at 416-368-6161 ext. 8242\n\n\nPhoto of Yonge Stre
 et Entrance\n\n FREE Moving Stories by Yvonne Ng: Three Week Seniors Movem
 ent Workshops
