URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/open-studio-a-dance-studio-without
 -walls/
SUMMARY:Open Studio: A Dance Studio Without Walls
DESCRIPTION:THIS EVENT IS CANCELLED TO HELP MITIGATE THE SPREAD OF CORONAVI
 RUS \n\nCatch a behind-the-scenes glimpse of the creation and rehearsal p
 rocesses of new dance works\, watch a professional company dance class or 
 participate in one of our NEW public workshops within the unique context o
 f a train station. Linger for 5 minutes or stay the whole day! All activit
 ies are FREE and take place in the West Wing\, just west of the Great Hall
 .\n\nVisit ffdnorth.com/openstudio for more info and workshop registration
 .\n\nMonday March 16\n\n1:00 – 4:00 pm\nJohnson/Perry Productions\nRehea
 rsing “TALENT/SHOW”\, by Sabina Perry\n\n​4:30 – 7:00 pm\nHATAW Pe
 rforming Arts\nRehearsing “Gong Spirits”\, “Ice Palaces”\nand “K
 alipay” by Crista Aguinaldo\n\n_\n\nTuesday March 17\n\n8:00 – 8:30 am
 \nEarly Morning Tai Chi\nClass with Eti Greenberg\nOPEN TO THE PUBLIC!\n\n
 10:30 am – 12:00 pm\nMamaDances\nParent Child Dance Workshop\, with Jess
 ica Runge\nOPEN TO THE PUBLIC!\n\n​12:30 – 2:45 pm\ntiger princess dan
 ce projects\nSwallowing Clouds: Creative Arts &amp\; Movement Workshop\nOP
 EN TO THE PUBLIC!\n\n3:15 – 6:30 pm\nNorman Dance Company\nRehearsing Ch
 inese Classical Dance – Dun Huang\, by Tia Lu\n\nThe Union and Fall for 
 Dance North partnership continues into its fourth year to offer free publi
 c programming in one of Toronto’s most historic buildings. This partners
 hip presents unique programming\, specifically curated for Union Station\,
  to bring you closer to where Toronto is going on the arts and cultural sc
 ene. Open Studio: A Dance Studio Without Walls
