DTSTAMP:20200105T220647Z
URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/leapfrog-a-dance-theatre-workshop/
SUMMARY:LEAPfrog: a dance-theatre workshop
DESCRIPTION:LEAPfrog March Break Workshop\nAre you a dancer who wants to le
 arn about acting? Are you an actor seeking to learn more about movement? A
 re you interested in performance\, creation and storytelling? Frog in Hand
 s March workshop "LEAPfrog" was designed just for you!\n\nThis workshop ap
 proaches storytelling through the expressive lens of the body. Our teachin
 g philosophy is based on the belief that dancers and actors both can and s
 hould train together to explore narrativity\, character development\, phys
 ical expressiveness and storytelling tools. At LEAPfrog\, participants are
  welcomed with classes in the morning and a collaborative creation lab in 
 the afternoon. The workshop refines what it means to engage in "dance-thea
 tre" or "physical-theatre" work\, while cultivating a reflective practise.
 \n\nThis compelling and fun intensive will take place next on March 20-21\
 , from 9am-4pm at Rapier Wit in Toronto. LEAPfrog was created by Frog in H
 and in partnership with Daniel Levinson and Rapier Wit.\n\nProposed Schedu
 le (subject to change)\n\n 	8:30am Arrival\n 	9am-10am Warm up movement cl
 ass with Colleen\n 	10am-noon Dance-theatre class co-facilitated by Collee
 n Snell and Daniel Levinson\n 	Noon-1 LUNCH\n 	1pm-4pm Creation lab\n\nAbo
 ut Frog in Hand\nColleen Snell\, Artistic Director\nWe are a dance-theatre
  company based in Mississauga\, Ontario. We are curious about people\, and
  the spaces we inhabit. Our mission is to uncover\, make\, and share stori
 es through dance. We contribute to community by sharing resources\, knowle
 dge and experience through creation\, performance and education.\nWe creat
 e integrated dance-theatre experiences that resonate physically\, emotiona
 lly and contextually. We push the boundaries of dance performance through 
 collaborative processes that embrace and advocate for embodied ways of kno
 wing about the world. We attend not only to the details of the work we mak
 e\, but also to the processes we use to create our work.\nOur work is inno
 vative and reflects our passion for dance as a medium that transcends lang
 uage. We are committed to dance that engages with its site and is rooted i
 n community\; recognizing and honouring diverse stories and storytellers. 
 For more: https://www.froginhand.com/\n\nAbout Daniel Levinson &amp\; Rapi
 er Wit\nFight Master\, Fight Directors Canada. Owner\, Rapier Wit\nA gradu
 ate of the York University BFA Acting Conservatory program\, Daniel has be
 en performing\, directing and teaching stage combat professionally since 1
 991. He is the owner of Rapier Wit\, Canadas oldest stage combat school an
 d production company\, and a founding member of the Riot A.C.T. stunt team
 . He is one of the founding advanced members of Fight Directors Canada\, a
  past president as well as one of only ten FDC Fight Masters in Canada. Da
 niel has created fights for companies such as The Stratford Festival (5 se
 asons)\, Canadian Stage\, Jesus Christ Superstar Broadway\, Volcano Theatr
 e\, Actors Repertory Company\, Second City\, A.C.T. Productions\, Shakespe
 are In the Square\, Factory Theatre\, Shakespeare in the Rough\, Theatre A
 quarius\, The Actors Repertory Company\, Theatre Passe Muraille\, and The 
 Tarragon Theatre. He is the resident stage combat instructor for Sheridan 
 College\, the University of Torontos Theatre and Drama Studies Program\, a
 nd is a frequent instructor at the University of Waterloo. He also teaches
  stage combat workshops across Canada and internationally\; workshop highl
 ights include the Fight Directors Canada National Workshop (Banff\, Victor
 ia\, Toronto\, Montreal)\, Brock Universitys Walker Cultural Leader Series
 \, Boston University\, Arcadia University\, the International Scuola Branc
 aleoni Stage Combat Workshop (Italy)\, and the Paddy Crean International A
 rt of the Sword Workshop (Banff). Daniel is a member of CAEA and ACTRA. Fo
 r more: https://www.rapierwit.com/ LEAPfrog: a dance-theatre workshop
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2020/01/frong-in-hand.png
CATEGORIES:Contemporary
LOCATION:Rapier Wit\, 575 Wellington St West\, Toronto\, ON\, Canada
GEO:43.6422818;-79.4030702
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=575 Wellington St West\, To
 ronto\, ON\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Rapier Wit:geo:43.6422818,-
 79.4030702
END:VEVENT
