SUMMARY:Dusk Dances 2020: A virtual edition
DESCRIPTION:Dusk Dances features an array of choreographic works presented 
 at sunset. As dusk descends\, a theatrical host leads the audience to an a
 rray of dance pieces that unfold in different areas of a park. Throughout 
 its 26 years history\, Dusk Dances has made dance accessible to audiences 
 in economically\, socially and culturally diverse communities.\n\nIn 2020\
 , Dusk Dances will present its very first virtual edition. Join us for thi
 s unique performance on October 17\, 2020 at 7:30pm. Our host extraordinai
 re\, Coach Tanguay\, will lead you to four exquisite dance pieces featurin
 g choreographers Santee Smith\, Carmen Romero\, Julia Aplin and Gerry Tren
 tham and live music by Amadou Kienou\, Patty Chan and Marjolaine Fournier.
  Directed by William Yong.\n\nTo participate:\nGo to duskdances.ca or foll
 ow our social media (@duskdances) to access the online event. The performa
 nce recording will be available on our website for 30 days\, until Novembe
 r 17.\n\nIt is a pay-what-you-can / if-you-can event. Dusk Dances 2020: A 
 virtual edition
