 e/
SUMMARY:Valentine's Day with Propeller Dance!
DESCRIPTION:Looking for a date night activity this Valentine's Day?\nJoin u
 s on Sunday\, February 14 at 2pm for a special live virtual event!\n\n\n\n
 The live celebration will start with a screening of a compilation of some 
 of our favourite loving\, affectionate\, and sometimes passionate on-stage
  Propeller Dance moments.\n\nFollowing the screening\, join members of the
  Propeller Artistic Team as they\n\n 	Lead a mini movement workshop centre
 d around self-love\, sharing energies through the screen with one another.
  This offers everyone a glimpse of the kind of warm up Propeller Dance Com
 pany members are familiar with.\n 	Host a Q&amp\;A with Propeller Dance pe
 rformers about the compilation video\, and intimacy on stage. Everyone is 
 invited to participate\, and welcome to ask questions. Questions can be su
 bmitted during the event\, or in advance by emailing info@propellerdance.c
 om.\n 	Present a poetry exchange about love. Poems can be shared during th
 e event\, or in advance by emailing info@propellerdance.com.\n\nEvent is b
 y donation\, suggested $10 or PWYC (Pay-What-You-Can).\n\nAccessibility: T
 he event will include closed captioning. If any other accommodations are n
 eeded\, please email info@propellerdance.com by Monday\, February 8.\n\nPh
 oto credit: Dancers Sylvain Bouchard and anonymous in Spasticus\, choreogr
 aphed by Liz Winkelaar\, photographer Alvin Sim\n\n[Image description: A p
 hotograph of Sylvain Bouchard and another dancer seated on the ground\, fa
 cing one another\, they lean their heads on each other's shoulders. The an
 onymous dancer extends one leg behind her\, toe pointed. They wear costume
 s made of ripped fabric. The image is a soft pink\, white\, and black. Tex
 t reads: "Digital Presentation Series Celebrate Valentine's Day with Prope
 ller Dance.]\n\n\n Valentine&#039\;s Day with Propeller Dance!
