URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/an-evening-of-love-dances-with-dan
 iel-gwirtzman-dance-company/
SUMMARY:An Evening of Love Dances with Daniel Gwirtzman Dance Company
DESCRIPTION:Daniel Gwirtzman Dance Company presents An Evening of Love Danc
 es. Four brief duets on film with commentary from the choreographer and ca
 st.\n\n\n\n\nThis Valentine’s Day the NYC-based Daniel Gwirtzman Dance C
 ompany offers An Evening of Love Dances\, a live Zoom event celebrating th
 e duet form in the DGDC repertory\, the push and pull of relationships\, a
 nd the lauded dancers in the Company. Reserve your ticket for a front-row 
 view to several dances from the acclaimed 20th Anniversary season Intersec
 tions\, performed two Februarys ago at The 92nd Street Y in New York. Be t
 he first to see this footage! Choreographer Daniel Gwirtzman\, dancers Der
 ek Crescenti and Vanessa Martínez de Baños\, and moderator Daisy Rudin w
 ill provide commentary discussing the critical\, public\, and personal con
 versations surrounding these favorites from the rep.\n\nThe title refers t
 o a program held exactly twenty-one years ago when DGDC premiered An Eveni
 ng of Love Dances\, two back-to-back sold-out performances of ten dances f
 or a cast of eleven\, at Joyce SoHo the evening of February 14\, 2000. Rev
 iewing the program in Attitude: The Dancers’ Magazine\, summer 2000\, da
 nce writer Madeleine L. Dale wrote:\n“For love of dance\, audience and p
 erformers were romanced at Joyce SoHo…it was nice to just sit back and b
 e nuzzled by Mr. Gwirtzman’s gift and to enjoy the satisfying feeling of
  love at first sight\, with hope in your heart that you will meet again so
 on.”\nThe event will screen Coupling\, Museum\, Together\, and the duet 
 from Timebomb\, as captured in the 2008 live dance film\, Timebomb 360° w
 hich was produced at Manhattan's Baryshnikov Arts Center.\n\nRegarding Int
 ersections OnStageBlog’s critic Natalie Rine writes:\n"Provocative\, whi
 msical\, and ethereal\, the Daniel Gwirtzman Dance Company defies expectat
 ions of postmodern dance and soars\, unafraid to take risks and dazzle wit
 h unflinching honesty...The company shoots energy through every limb and g
 lance the entire evening\, and Gwirtzman’s choreography shines through i
 n every piece as an ultimate force of nature." (Winter 2019)\nRead the ful
 l review.\n\nAn Evening of Love Dances features the work of Daniel Gwirtzm
 an (Director\, Choreographer)\, Jeff Story (Composer)\, and Company member
 s Oren Barnoy\, Derek Crescenti\, Jason Garcia Ignacio\, Lauren Kravitz\, 
 Vanessa Martínez de Baños\, Stacy Martorana\, Simon Phillips\, Ryan Plis
 s\, Frances Samson\, Simone Stevens\, and Christian von Howard.\n\nPlease 
 note this is a Zoom Webinar and as an attendee you will not be seen. After
  registering\, you will receive an email from Eventbrite with information 
 about how to join the event. For any technical questions\, please contact 
 the Company directly at info@gwirtzmandance.org.\n\n\n An Evening of Love 
 Dances with Daniel Gwirtzman Dance Company
