URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/daybreaker-live-a-joy-supreme-danc
 ing-to-motown-magic/
SUMMARY:Daybreaker LIVE // A Joy Supreme: Dancing to Motown Magic
DESCRIPTION:On Saturday\, February 20 at 11AM ET (US)\, meet us ONLINE for 
 A Joy Supreme: Dancing to Motown Magic—a Daybreaker LIVE sponsored by AA
 RP.\n\n\n\nFam\, bring on the tears of joy—this one’s going straight f
 or the soul. &#x1f64f\;\n\nTHE biggest R&amp\;B act of all time—Boyz II 
 Men\, performing on our virtual stage. Grammy-winning R&amp\;B Diva Thelma
  Houston singing to fill our hearts. AND MC Lyte\, one of the greatest MCs
  of all time and a quintessential pioneer of female rap\, on the decks to 
 make us dance with reckless abandon... &#x1f525\;\n\nThis one’s a dream 
 come true. And on Saturday\, February 20th—from 11am to 1pm Eastern Time
 —we’ll be making history together with a global livestream dance party
  to call in A Joy Supreme.\n\nTo honor Black History Month\, we’re comin
 g together with AARP for an intergenerational celebration of dance\, music
 \, community and more than a half-century of Motown magic—the sound and 
 legacy that changed America.\n\nAARP is empowering this experience to make
  tix free for the community—so snag your RSVP before we hit max Zoom Roo
 m capacity. &#x1f64c\;\n\nTogether\, we’ll enjoy a little slice of bliss
  at home with the irreverent\, glorious melodies and unforgettable hooks t
 hat didn’t just define a sound but also a joyous state of mind. It all s
 tarts with a 20 minute dance warm-up to introduce Steppin’ &amp\; Line-D
 ancing into our movement vocabulary.\n\nThen dressed in sleek\, sequined d
 resses\, colorful high-style suits and all things reminiscent of Hitsville
  U.S.A. (&#x2728\;this is the one to dress up for&#x2728\;)\, we’ll move
  into the dance party letting our freedom of expression take the lead. *Cu
 e the trifecta that is Boyz II Men\, Thelma Houston &amp\; MC Lyte*\n\nOur
  OG Daybreaker MC Elliott LaRue will be on the mic to inspire and remind u
 s that the power of Black Joy truly knows no bounds. And for two sweet hou
 rs we’ll all be connected\, with only the language of dance filling the 
 space between us. &#x26a1\;&#xfe0f\;\n\nWe’ve all got music in us. Join 
 us—and let’s set it wild. In joy\, we dance. &#x1f483\;\n\nSee you on 
 the (virtual) dancefloor.\n\n——\n\nThe Lineup\n\n11am | Steppin' &amp\
 ; Line-Dancing Warm-up Dance Class (no experience required)\n\n11:50am | G
 uided Dance Party Experience  hosted by Elliott LaRue\, featuring live DJ 
 set from MC Lyte and Thelma Houston performing "Don’t Leave Me This Way"
 \n\n12:45pm - 1pm |  Closing Ceremony featuring Boyz II Men\n\n**All times
  are posted in Eastern Daylight Time (US)\n Daybreaker LIVE // A Joy Supre
 me: Dancing to Motown Magic
