SUMMARY:Youth America Grand Prix Virtual Benefit
DESCRIPTION:The Youth America Grand Prix (YAGP) 2021 Virtual Benefit on Mar
 ch 31 will feature the world premiere of a brand new performance by Americ
 an Ballet Theatre (ABT) Soloist and YAGP Alum Gabe Stone Shayer\, performe
 d by Shayer and YAGP alumna\, ABT Principal Dancer Skylar Brandt. Blind Ju
 illiard piano prodigy Matthew Whitaker was commissioned to create and perf
 orm the accompanying music.\n\nMariinsky Ballet’s Maria Khoreva and Kimi
 n Kim (YAGP Alum) will perform a duet from Le Corsaire\, while May Nagahis
 a and Victor Caixeta (both YAGP Alumni) will perform a duet from Romeo and
  Juliet. There will also be a musical performance by former dancer and par
 ticipant on So You Think You Can Dance – and now a successful singer/son
 gwriter – Tate McRae\n\nThe finale will include a compilation of the bes
 t performances from YAGP’s 2021 Season participants worldwide.\n\nHelp Y
 AGP support the future of dance.\n\nFor more information or to register: h
 ttps://yagp.org/yagp-2021-virtual-gala/ Youth America Grand Prix Virtual B
 enefit
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2021/03/Screen-Shot-2021-03-05-at-6.16.25-PM.jpg
