URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/mental-skills-in-dance-workshop/
SUMMARY:Mental Skills in Dance Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Date: Wednesday\, June 9th\n\nTime: 2:00- 3:30 pm\n\nPlace: ZOO
 M\n\nCost: FREE to all Dance Ontario members with promo code\n\nAs a human
 \, we can train three things\; the mind\, body\, and craft. As dancers and
  dance educators\, we have spent years building and nurturing body and cra
 ft\, but have not yet explored the power of mental skills within our class
 es and performances. Join educator\, facilitator and speaker Lauren Ritchi
 e for the Community Workshop\, “Mental Skills in Dance” as part of the
  #DanceONSeries. On June 9th from 2-3:30 pm. Lauren will share research an
 d foundations of mental skills\, as well as awareness and resilience exerc
 ises that can be easily applied before\, during\, and after training and p
 erformance. You don’t want to miss this session from a professional Ment
 al Performance Consultant!\n\nAbout the Facilitator:\n\nLauren Ritchie (ME
 d\, BA\, ESFCC) has been researching\, studying\, and educating dancers an
 d teachers on the physical\, emotional and mental intricacies of dance. Sh
 e holds a Master’s Degree from the University of Victoria in Coaching St
 udies with a focus on mental skills training. Recognizing the lack of ment
 al skills training in dance\, Lauren has created programs and exercises de
 dicated to educating and empowering both dancers’ and educators’ menta
 l health and mindset to optimize physical and artistic training. She is fo
 cused on helping performers of all kinds to practice and perform optimally
 \, with grit\, grace\, and resilience. Her work is centered on aiding clie
 nts to use their minds and bodies in complementary ways by uncovering\, de
 veloping\, and harnessing their mental and emotional resources. Lauren is 
 currently delivering mental skills workshops internationally to dancers an
 d dance educators.\n\nAn established educator\, facilitator and speaker\, 
 Lauren has worked with prestigious schools and programs like Harbour Dance
  Centre\, the Alberta Ballet School\, the Dancer Transition Resource Centr
 e\, Capilano University and The Bridge Program with The Protege Movement. 
 Lauren is also a Student Member of the Canadian Sport Psychology Associati
 on (CSPA). She created the renowned Mental Skills Training Teacher Trainin
 g\, is the co-founder of the Dance Teacher retreat\, and has been a keynot
 e speaker for the Women In Sport Speaker Series\, Dance Studio Owners Asso
 ciation\, House of Jazz (London)\, and the Dance Teacher Expo.\n\nShe is a
 lso the producer and host of The Dance Podcast\; an invaluable resource de
 dicated to inspiring and educating dancers\, teachers\, and parents. Ritch
 ie unpacks and decodes each guest’s professional journey\, mental framew
 ork\, and mindset skills and practices. Past guests include Mia Michaels\,
  NappyTabs\, Misty Lown\, Alex Wong\, Stacey Tookey\, Clint Salter\, Josh 
 Assor\, and Bree Wasylenko. Mental Skills in Dance Workshop
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-06-04-at-11.06.14-AM.png
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Toronto Dance
