UID:3795@torontodance.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20210707T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20210707T160000
DTSTAMP:20210615T210033Z
URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/dancing-through-challenging-times-
 health-and-safety-guidance-and-resources/
SUMMARY:Dancing Through Challenging Times - Health and Safety Guidance and 
 Resources
DESCRIPTION:Date: July 7th\n\nTime: 2:00- 4:00 pm\n\nPlace: ZOOM\n\nCost: F
 REE to all Dance Ontario members with promo code\n\nREGISTER HERE\n\nWonde
 ring what the future of dance will look like in our province\, as Ontario 
 plans to re-open this summer? Join us at 2-4pm on June 16th for the Commun
 ity Workshop\, “Dancing Through Challenging Times” with Janet Sellery\
 , as part of the #DanceOnSeries. Whether you’re a dancer\, choreographer
 \, teacher\, company\, or anyone who supports the Ontario dance community
 —you won’t want to miss this session with one of Canada’s leading ex
 perts in health and safety within the arts. Janet will discuss lessons lea
 rned throughout the Pandemic\, as well as current health and safety resour
 ces for the dance community\, including class\, creation\, rehearsal and p
 erformance.\n\nLearn about our Workshop Host:\n\nJanet Sellery is the Exec
 utive Director of Event Safety Alliance Canada a board member of the Event
  Safety Alliance (U.S.). Janet pioneered the health and safety program at 
 the Stratford Festival\, Canada’s largest repertory theatre\, and one of
  her favourite projects was working as the Health &amp\; Safety Manager fo
 r the Opening\, Closing and Victory Ceremonies at the Vancouver 2010 Winte
 r Olympics. Janet was a Co-Founder of the Canadian Event Safety Summit (20
 16-2018) and is also an active volunteer with the Ontario Ministry of Labo
 ur Live Performance\, Health &amp\; Safety Advisory Committee.\n\nHer work
  as a Health &amp\; Safety Consultant\, with Sellery Health + Safety focus
 es on customizing programs\, training\, and resources to reflect the const
 antly evolving and unique demands of dancers. She has been awarded the “
 Jack McAllister Award” (Ryerson University)\, the “Ron Epp Memorial Aw
 ard for Professional Achievement” (Canadian Institute for Theatre Techno
 logy) and “Canada’s Safety Manager of the Year” (Canadian Occupation
 al Safety Magazine).\n\nDuring the Pandemic Janet has been working to supp
 ort the arts community\, as well as to figure out how to have everyone ret
 urn safely to the profession we love most. Dancing Through Challenging Tim
 es - Health and Safety Guidance and Resources
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2021/06/unnamed.jpg
END:VEVENT
