SUMMARY:The Miserere Project
DESCRIPTION:Bright Nights Presents: The Miserere Project\nProduced by Danie
 lle Baskerville\nMay 18th-22nd @ 8PM\nOn the 40th anniversary of the creat
 ion of David Earle’s celebrated masterwork\, Miserere\, three choreograp
 hers have been commissioned to create contemporary responses using Earle
 ’s Miserere as their creative seed. The evening will be comprised of thr
 ee world premieres by choreographers Penny Couchie\, Same As Sister (S.A.S
 .)\, and Brodie Stevenson as well as a remount of Earle’s Miserere in it
 s’ original form for fifteen dancers.\nLivestream also available until M
 ay 23rd @ 11:59 PM\nLive Tickets - $25.00\nLivestream Tickets- $5.00 The M
 iserere Project
LOCATION:Citadel Ross Centre for Dance\, 304 Parliament St\, Toronto\, Onta
 rio\, M5A2Z6\, Canada
