URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/community-classes-bollywood-with-s
 hereen/
SUMMARY:Community Classes: Bollywood with Shereen
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Bollywood with Shereen Ladha at Meridian Hall on Tu
 esdays from May 24th to July 26th at 6:00PM!\n\n\nJoin us for Bollywood wi
 th Shereen Ladha!\nMeridian Hall\, 1 Front Street East\nEntrance @ Yonge S
 treet\n6:00-7:00PM\n\n 	Tues. May 24 | Rehearsal Hall\n 	Tues. July 5 | Re
 hearsal Hall\n 	Tues. July 19 | O'Keefe Lounge\n 	Tues. July 26 | Rehearsa
 l Hall\n\nJoin Shereen Ladha in this all-level class that explores:\n\n 	t
 he diversity of South Asian dance in the Bollywood film industry\n 	footwo
 rk\, hand gestures\, spins\, and expressions\n 	creating short routines to
  iconic Bollywood songs\n\nAbout the Instructor\nShereen Ladha is a profes
 sional dancer\, choreographer\, artist\, instructor\, and movement directo
 r based in Toronto. She is the director of the viral YouTube channel 'danc
 ewithSL' that features Bollywood\, Classical Indian\, and modern styles (a
 nd was even used by Apple in their most recent ads!) Shereen has been name
 d Google Canada/YouTube's Next 15 Canadian Stars on the rise\, FLARE Top 1
 00 Canadian women with cool jobs and CBC Canada’s top female artists.\n\
 nShereen has also been profiled by BuzzFeed\, the Globe and Mail\, Huffing
 ton Post\, CTV\, CBC\, Breakfast Television\, and Strategy Magazine for he
 r work.\n\nShereen was a finalist on Canada’s Got Talent with her former
  team Broken Dance. DancewithSL is also the creative force behind several 
 YouTube viral videos including viral sensation 'Maafi' - the Bollywood cov
 er of Justin Bieber's 'Sorry\,' the hit touring stage shows 'Roots: A Jour
 ney Through India' and 'Rihla: From Roots to Dreams\,' and exhibits like T
 IFF Bell Lightbox’s Picture Palace and Nuit Blanche Toronto.\n\nClass Lo
 cation &amp\; Arrival Information\nLocation: Meridian Hall\, 1 Front St E
  (see dates above for room location)\n\nEntrance: Yonge Street Entrance (
 located along Yonge Street on the west side of the building halfway betwee
 n Front St. and Esplanade).\n\nDoors will open at 5:30PM\n\nCovid Guidelin
 es  All participants are encouraged to wear a mask when inside the venue. 
 Maximum capacity of the classes has been set to allow for physical distanc
 ing of 6 feet between participants. Click here to view TO Live's Covid pol
 icy.\n\nAccessibility The Yonge Street Entrance is accessible and has an a
 utomatic door opener and lift.\n\nScent-Reduced Environment To help share 
 the air\, community classes promote a scent-reduced environment. Many peop
 le have chemical and scent sensitivities\, which can cause mild to severe 
 physical reactions. Please help reduce the use of scented products in clas
 s.\n\nWaiver and Rules &amp\; Regulations All participants are required to
  sign the class waivers as part of the Eventbrite registration form befor
 e participating. Click here to view the TO Live Community Class Rules &am
 p\; Regulations.\n\nQuestions? Contact us by email at education@tolive.co
 m.\n\n\n Community Classes: Bollywood with Shereen
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2022/04/25913_image.png
CATEGORIES:Bollywood
LOCATION:Meridian Hall\, 1 Front Street East\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5E 1B2\
 , GTA\, Canada
GEO:43.646801;-79.376701
