URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/dancehall-with-mustbefaby/
SUMMARY:Dancehall with MustBeFaby
DESCRIPTION:Yensa Festival invites you to Dancehall with MustBe Faby\n\n\n\
 nJamaican dancehall with MustBeFABY will take you on a journey to the root
 s of its inner-city history\, its message of personal empowerment and its 
 international popularity!\n\n\n\n\n\nMUSTBEFABY’S ARTISTIC PRACTICE make
 s her feel free\, refreshed\, and exhilarated! Art gives meaning to her li
 fe and helps her understand our world. “I’m being authentic and I’m 
 just listening to my needs in terms of expression. I’ve been so lucky to
  have the means to express myself and not wait in the corner for years. So
 ... When you see me\, don't be shy to twist in my world :)”\n\n\n\n\n\nB
 orn in Montreal\, MustBeFaby was from a young age captivated by movement. 
 In her youth she took part in figure skating\, gymnastics and has been hon
 ing her skills in dance for over 15 years. Moving to Toronto for dance\, s
 he had the opportunity to teach Dancehall in the most reputable institutio
 ns and spaces in the city such as Millenium Dance Complex\, The Undergroun
 d Dance Centre\, Toronto Dance Theatre\, Art Gallery of Ontario\, Ryerson 
 University (now TMU) and internationally! For the past years\, she has bee
 n training and embracing Jamaican culture. She organizes a broad range of 
 cultural\, educational and artistic events and workshops across Eastern Ca
 nada and abroad!\n\n\n Dancehall with MustBeFaby
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2022/05/26079_image.jpg
CATEGORIES:Dance Hall
LOCATION:Regent Park Community Centre\, 402 Shuter St\, Toronto\, ON M5A 1X
 6\, Toronto\, ON\, M5A 1X6\, Canada
