SUMMARY:Chinatown Festival
DESCRIPTION:\nOn August 20 &amp\; 21\, 2022\, the Toronto Chinatown Busines
 s Improvement Area (CBIA) will host the 22nd Toronto Chinatown Festival un
 der the theme of the “Eight Immortals” (八仙)\, taking after the pop
 ular Chinese mythology. In Chinese mythology\, the Eight Immortals are bel
 ieved to know the secrets of nature. They represent separately male\, fema
 le\, the old\, the young\, the rich\, the noble\, the poor\, and the humbl
 e.\n\n\nAfter a turbulent whirlwind of events in the last two years\, the 
 CBIA is pleased to bring back the iconic annual festival bringing over 250
 \,000 visitors every year during the two-day event. Visitors may expect an
  enchanted two-day program filled with cultural performances\, traditional
  street eats\, family activities on Huron Street\, Dragon and Lion Dance p
 erformances and many more!\n Chinatown Festival
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2022/08/chinatown-festival.jpg
CATEGORIES:Asian
LOCATION:ChinaTown\, Spadina Ave &amp\; Dundas Street\, Toronto\, ON\, Cana
 da
GEO:43.652913;-79.398155
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Spadina Ave & Dundas Street
 \, Toronto\, ON\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=ChinaTown:geo:43.65291
 3,-79.398155
END:VEVENT
