SUMMARY:Slipping
DESCRIPTION:Kaeja d'Dance is excited to announce the world premiere of Slip
 ping\, a new dance film created by Karen Kaeja &amp\; Roshanak Jaberi. Joi
 n us this September 23-24\, 2022 for two live screenings at the Betty Olip
 hant Theatre &amp\; York University\, presented by Fall for Dance North.\n
 \nSlipping is an intimate journey of four women's lives\, as they slip bet
 ween emotional and psychological torment. The characters coexist through t
 heir unfolding stories in a century-old mansion. Their only link to realit
 y is each other.\n\nhttps://vimeo.com/739016064\n\nConceived and filmed in
  rural Quebec with an all-female team\, co-directors Roshanak Jaberi and K
 aren Kaeja set out to merge their artistic voices. The fictional and haunt
 ing narrative of Slipping was shot through the lens of cinematographer Oly
 a Glotka\, and scored by Edgardo Moreno.\n\nA Jaberi Dance Theatre Product
 ion\n\nConcept\, Directors\, Choreographers – Karen Kaeja &amp\; Roshana
 k Jaberi\nProducers – Karen Kaeja &amp\; Roshanak Jaberi\nDirector of Ph
 otography – Olya Glotka\nEditor – Olya Glotka\nComposer – Edgardo Mo
 reno\nDramaturg – Shannon Litzenberger\nEditing Advisor – Allen Kaeja\
 nProduction Assistant &amp\; Coordinator – Jessica Cen\n\nCreated with P
 erformers – Mairéad Filgate\, Nickeshia Garrick\, Victoria Mata\, Irma 
 Villafuerte\nAppearances by – Karen Kaeja &amp\; Roshanak Jaberi Slippin
 g
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2022/08/slipping.jpg
CATEGORIES:Contemporary
LOCATION:Betty Oliphant Theatre\, 404 Jarvis St\, Toronto\, Ontario\, GTA\,
  Canada
GEO:43.664398;-79.377602
