URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/__trashed/
SUMMARY:Harbourfront Centre presents Torque
DESCRIPTION:Harbourfront Centre announces its international contemporary da
 nce series\, Torque\, on stage from October 2022 to May 2023. The 2022/23 
 season will showcase five dance presentations and three world premieres. U
 K’s Hofesh Shechter Company\, October 27-29\, presents the Ontario premi
 ere of Double Murder\, the internationally celebrated choreographer’s th
 rilling new double bill of contrasting works - Clowns and The Fix\; Toront
 o’s own Kaeja d’Dance\, November 11-13\, presents two world premieres 
 with TouchX// I am the Child of…and examines the universal power of refl
 ection\, resilience and touch\; Quebec’s Compagnie Virginie Brunelle\, F
 ebruary 24-25\, presents the Toronto premiere of Les corps avalés\, a mov
 ing union between contemporary dance and classical music\, performed live 
 by the Molinari Quartet\; Six Nations of the Grand River’s and Toronto
 ’s Kaha:wi Dance Theatre\, April 13-15\, presents the world premiere of 
 Homelands\, a multimedia performance created to uphold power\, sacred exis
 tence and continuance of feminine creative force\; and South Africa’s Da
 da Masilo\, May 16-17\, presents The Sacrifice\, an exploration of the min
 imalism and animality of Tswana dance in relation to Igor Stravinsky's The
  Rite of Spring. For Torque tickets and to explore Harbourfront Centre’s
  full season lineup\, visit: harbourfrontcentre.com Harbourfront Centre pr
 esents Torque
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2022/09/DOUBLE-MURDER-THE-FIX-IMAGE-1-Todd-MacDonald-1-2.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Toronto Dance
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/
UID:3993@torontodance.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20221027T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20221027T213000
DTSTAMP:20221204T201428Z
URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/harbourfront-centre-presents-hofes
 h-shechter-companys-double-murder/
SUMMARY:Harbourfront Centre presents Hofesh Shechter Company’s Double Mur
 der
DESCRIPTION:Harbourfront Centre presents the Ontario premiere of Hofesh She
 chter Company’s hypnotic and high-energy double bill Double Murder\, on 
 stage October 27–29\, 2022 at 7:30pm at Fleck Dance Theatre\, part of th
 e international contemporary dance series Torque. Created by international
 ly celebrated choreographer and composer Hofesh Shechter\, Double Murder i
 s a thrilling exploration of the chaotic and oppressive forces in our mode
 rn times. The performance features two distinctly contrasting works that e
 xplore societal schisms and human kinship: Clowns is a sarcastic and playf
 ul nod to our ever-growing indifference to violence. At the same time\, Th
 e Fix presents a tender\, fragile antidote to the omnipresent forces of ag
 gression that press on us daily. Set to Shechter’s sweepingly cinematic\
 , percussive score\, Double Murder exposes painful truths and deep emotion
 s. For tickets and further information\, visit: harbourfrontcentre.com Har
 bourfront Centre presents Hofesh Shechter Company’s Double Murder
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2022/10/DOUBLE-MURDER-THE-FIX-IMAGE-1-by-Todd-MacDonald-copy.jpg
CATEGORIES:Contemporary
END:VEVENT
