DTSTAMP:20220922T170030Z
URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/31-touchx-i-am-the-child-of/
SUMMARY:31 (TouchX + I am the Child of...)
DESCRIPTION:31 years. 2 world premieres. 50 performers. 4 AR experiences.\n
 \nCelebrating our 31st Anniversary\, Kaeja d'Dance presents two world prem
 ieres in 31 (TouchX + I am the Child of...) This in-person double-bill sho
 w investigates the complexity of our lived experience\, using community\, 
 perspective\, and augmented reality technology to create two evocative wor
 lds. With over 25 artistic collaborators and 33 community participants\, t
 hese works devise movement from deeply personal stories\, examining the un
 iversal power of reflection\, resilience\, and touch. Experience it for yo
 urself at Harbourfront Centre between November 11-13 as PART OF TORQUE Int
 ernational Contemporary Dance Series 2022!\n\n&nbsp\; 31 (TouchX + I am th
 e Child of...)
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2022/09/31IG.jpg
LOCATION:Harbourfront Centre\, 235 Queens Quay West\, Toronto\, Ontario\, G
 TA\, Canada
GEO:43.638847;-79.382996
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=235 Queens Quay West\, Toro
 nto\, Ontario\, GTA\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Harbourfront Centr
 e:geo:43.638847,-79.382996
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Toronto Dance
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/
UID:3995@torontodance.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20221111T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20221111T213000
DTSTAMP:20221110T005350Z
URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/kaeja-ddance-31-touchx-i-am-the-ch
 ild-of/
SUMMARY:Kaeja d’Dance: 31 (TouchX + I am the Child of)
DESCRIPTION:Harbourfront Centre presents the world premiere of two deeply p
 ersonal and expressive new works from Kaeja d’Dance: 31 (TouchX + I am t
 he Child of)\, on stage November 11–13\, 2022 at 7:30pm at Harbourfront 
 Centre Theatre\, as part of the international contemporary dance series\, 
 Torque. TouchX\, choreographed by Karen Kaeja\, and I am the Child of chor
 eographed by Allen Kaeja\, both consider the impact of memories on our liv
 es and bodies and take us on a multi-sensory journey towards connection an
 d resilience. TouchX explores the ephemeral nature of touch and its essent
 ial role in our lives\, while I am the Child of examines the concept of pe
 rspective\, using augmented reality and multiple livestreamed camera angle
 s to embody the idea of one’s personal experience. Audience members are 
 encouraged to interact with the performance through their mobile devices\,
  adding another layer of perspective to the dance experience. For tickets 
 and further information\, visit: harbourfrontcentre.com Kaeja d’Dance: 3
 1 (TouchX + I am the Child of)
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2022/10/I-Am-A-Child-Of...-HCT-Residency-Nickeshia-Garrick-and-Karen-Kaeja
 -4-Photo-by-Kevin-Jones-copy.jpg
CATEGORIES:Contemporary
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Toronto Dance
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/
UID:3996@torontodance.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20221113T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20221113T200000
DTSTAMP:20221110T013550Z
URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/duende-flamenco-festival-2022/
SUMMARY:Duende Flamenco Festival 2022
DESCRIPTION:The Aga Khan Museum's annual Duende Flamenco Festival returns t
 his year with seven days of workshops\, film screenings\, and live perform
 ances by award-winning artists from all over the world.\n\nFrom lively dan
 ce performances by The National Ballet of Canada's RBC Apprentice Program 
 to masterful workshops led by world-class artists\, this year's celebratio
 n is our biggest yet. Pushing past the boundaries of tradition\, you will 
 be taken on an explorative journey through the fiery history and spirit of
  flamenco dance and music.\n\nCheck the schedule below for festival highli
 ghts and explore the daily schedules for more information about the perfor
 mers and additional programs.\n\nSunday\, November 13\n\n 	6 pm | Duende: 
 Ignite Your Passion Festival Opening Celebration | $80 | Reserve tickets\n
 \nTuesday\, November 15\n\n 	8 pm | Offsite event at 3030 Dundas West | Fl
 amenco in the Six! by FabCollab | $35 | Reserve tickets\n\nWednesday\, Nov
 ember 16\n\n 	10:30 am | Singing Workshop (Cante Flamenco) with Vincente G
 elo | $75 | Reserve tickets\n 	12 pm | Flamenco Guitar Workshop with Gaspa
 r Rodriguez | $75 | Reserve tickets\n 	12 pm | Masterclass Dance Workshop 
 with Isaac Tovar | $100 | Reserve tickets\n 	8 pm | Qairo and TelaFlamenca
  by Compañia Carmen Romero | $45 | Reserve tickets\n\nThursday\, November
  17\n\n 	10:30 am | Tech Workshop with José Amosa | $75 | Reserve tickets
 \n 	12 pm | Flamenco Guitar Workshop with Santiago Lara | $75 | Reserve ti
 ckets\n 	12:30 pm | Masterclass Dance Workshop with Mercedes Ruiz | $100 |
  Reserve tickets\n 	8 pm | Añejo by Isaac Tovar | $50 | Reserve tickets\n
 \nFriday\, November 18\n\n 	8 pm | Dual by Mercedes Ruiz and Santiago Lara
  | $60 | Reserve tickets\n\nSaturday\, November 19\n\n 	8 pm | Seville in 
 the Six! by FabCollab | $45 | Reserve tickets\n\nSunday\, November 20\n\n 
 	7 pm | Esperando el Alba by Benjamin Barrile and Festival Fiesta by FabCo
 llab | Reserve tickets\n\nThe eighth annual Duende Flamenco Festival has b
 een curated by Carmen Romero\, the artistic director and principal dancer 
 of Toronto's Compañía Carmen Romero.\n\nAbout Carmen Romero\nCarmen Rome
 ro is an award-winning flamenco dance artist\, performer\, teacher\, and p
 roducer. With a strong presence in the national and international dance sc
 ene\, Romero has an unmatched talent for improvisation\, choreography\, an
 d storytelling. Romero's mesmerizing ability to create transcendent experi
 ences on stage has won her countless awards and nominations. Aside from co
 aching Latin Pop star Shakira\, she has received the Chalmers Award for th
 e K.M. Hunter Emerging Artists Award\, represented Canada at the 9th Annua
 l Certamen de Coreografía de Danza Española y Flamenco in Madrid\, and p
 erformed as a soloist in the International Castanet festival in Girona\, S
 pain.\n\nAbout FabCollab\nFounded by five of Toronto’s key performing ar
 tists and arts advocates\, FabCollab is a music initiative that fosters ar
 tistic creation and collaboration. Their aim is to address the challenges 
 faced in the music and arts community as a result of the pandemic and are 
 committed to amplifying minority and underrepresented groups\, particularl
 y BIPOC and female-identifying artists.\n\nFor prices &amp\; detailed info
 rmation visit the Festival's website: Duende Flamenco Festival 2022
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2022/10/Duende-2022_header_1200-X-672.jpg
CATEGORIES:Flamenco
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, Ontario\, Canada
GEO:43.725252;-79.332069
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\
 , Ontario\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Aga Khan Museum:geo:43.72525
 2,-79.332069
END:VEVENT
