SUMMARY:WINTERSONG—dances for a sacred season
DESCRIPTION:Celebrating 34 years of illuminating the solstice through dance
  with a world premiere by Colin Connor\, plus works by Rodney Diverlus\, A
 lyssa Martin\, Carol Anderson and Apolonia Velasquez. WINTERSONG warms the
  hearts of family audiences with a breathtaking tapestry of seasonal dance
  inspired by the world’s rich solstice traditions.\n\nA thoroughly refre
 shing take on the season - The Toronto Star\nCanadian Contemporary Dance T
 heatre is a Toronto based repertory company of exceptional next-generation
  artists founded in 1980 by Artistic Director Deborah Lundmark and Managin
 g Director Michael deConinck Smith. Highlights include appearances at Toro
 nto’s Princess of Wales and Royal Alexandra Theatres\, five invitations 
 to the Canada Dance Festival and tours to Singapore\, Malaysia\, China\, S
 cotland and NYC. Most recently CCDT was featured at Fall For Dance North\,
  Toronto’s premiere international dance festival.\n\na national treasure
  – The Globe and Mail WINTERSONG—dances for a sacred season
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2022/11/wintersong.jpg
CATEGORIES:Contemporary
LOCATION:Fleck Dance Theatre\, Harbourfront Centre\, 207 Queens Quay West\,
  Toronto\, Ontario\, M5J1A7\, GTA\, Canada
