URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/%d9%86%db%8c-%d9%86%d8%a7%d9%85%d9
 %87-song-of-the-reed-from-balkh-with-love/
SUMMARY:نی نامه / Song of the Reed: from Balkh with Love
DESCRIPTION:نی نامه / Song of the Reed is a captivating exploration o
 f the first poem titled “Beshno” or “Listen” in the book of Masnav
 i by the universally acclaimed poet Rumi. Drawing inspiration from Rumi's 
 birthplace\, the ancient city of Balkh\, and the rich cultural tapestry of
  Afghanistan\, it creates space and time for the audience to actively list
 en. This atmosphere is facilitated by a cast of six cross-generational and
  multi-disciplinary artists whose breaths and bodies collaboratively creat
 e a flowing river of dance and music.\nThe hypnotizing dance is presented 
 in the contemporary style of Mugham\, an integrated practice developed by 
 Sashar Zarif that blends dance\, music\, and storytelling and is inspired 
 and informed by the Sufi and Shamanic rituals of Muslim societies.\nZarif 
 will be joined by guest artists Nasrullah Tavakoli (Afghan Dutar and vocal
 )\, Günay Akca (Turkish Reed/Ney)\, Sashar Zarif Dance Theatre’s Mairea
 d Filgate\, Kathia Wittenborn\, Ethan Kim\, Sully Malaeb Proulx\, creative
  facilitator Katherine Duncanson\, and lighting designer Gabriel Cropley.\
 nنی نامه / Song of the Reed will be performed on Saturday\, February
  11\, 2023 at 8:00 pm\, and Sunday\, February 12th\, 2023 at 2:00 pm. Admi
 ssion to the galleries is included with the ticket the day of the show. Th
 e address for Aga Khan Museum is 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON.\nPlease 
 note\, Sunday’s afternoon performance will be followed by a conversation
  and Q&amp\;A with the artist. نی نامه / Song of the Reed: from Balk
 h with Love
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2023/02/song-of-the-reed.jpg
CATEGORIES:Contemporary,Folk
END:VEVENT
