URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/hold-up-save-the-last-dance-2001/
SUMMARY:Hold Up: SAVE THE LAST DANCE (2001)
DESCRIPTION:Hold Up is celebrating a movie as iconic as Julia Stiles' blue 
 and red sneakers -- SAVE THE LAST DANCE!\n\n\n\n\nNew city. New life. New 
 school. New vocabulary. New... perspectives on 21st century race politics?
  This month\, Hold Up is celebrating a movie as iconic as Julia Stiles' bl
 ue and red sneakers (seriously\, I've googled them so many times\, can any
 one help me find a pair?) Save The Last Dance (2001) is an exceptional hig
 hlight of 2000's era teen movies\, with a legendary soundtrack\, unforgett
 able dance moves\, and a healthy dose of cultural appropriation - just lik
 e the real 2000's!\n\nSarah (Julia Stiles) is a Midwestern white girl who 
 moves to a predominately black neighbourhood of Chicago. Her new boyfriend
 \, Derek (Sean Patrick Thomas)\, a black teen from the South Side\, tries 
 to invite her into his life by taking her to Steps\, a cool - no\, slammin
 ' - local hip hop club. Everything about them seems to be different\; thei
 r language\, their music\, their dance styles\, but with the help of Derek
 's sister Chenille (Kerry Washington)\, Sara learns to code switch just en
 ough to get by. When Derek learns about her traumatic past\, and her hidde
 n talents as a ballet dancer\, he helps her prepare for her upcoming audit
 ion to Juilliard\, causing Sara to learn that the world isn't always - wai
 t for it - black and white. - ALICE ROSE\nABOUT THE FILM\nUSA | 2001 | 112
  mins | PG\n\nDirected by: Thomas Carter\n\nStarring: Julia Stiles\, Sean 
 Patrick Thomas\, Kerry Washington\n\nRegular admission applies. For INDIVI
 DUAL MEMBERSHIPS ($350 - $450) and FAMILY MEMBERSHIPS\, please email us at
  info@revuecinema.ca to get a ticket!\n\n\n Hold Up: SAVE THE LAST DANCE (
 2001)
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2023/02/26764_image.png
CATEGORIES:Hip Hop
LOCATION:The Revue Cinema\, 400 Roncesvalles Ave\, Toronto\, ON M6R 2M9\, T
 oronto\, ON\, M6R 2M9\, Canada
GEO:43.651112;-79.450936
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=400 Roncesvalles Ave\, Toro
 nto\, ON M6R 2M9\, Toronto\, ON\, M6R 2M9\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TI
 TLE=The Revue Cinema:geo:43.651112,-79.450936
END:VEVENT
