 -resurrection/
SUMMARY:Opera Atelier presents Handel’s The Resurrection
DESCRIPTION:Opera Atelier welcomes spring and the Easter season with its pr
 esentation of Handel’s The Resurrection\, on stage April 6 and 8 at 7:30
 pm and April 9 at 2:30pm at Koerner Hall\, TELUS Centre for Performance an
 d Learning.\n\nThe Resurrection marks the Canadian premiere of Handel’s 
 first acknowledged masterpiece in a fully-staged production for a live aud
 ience. The company’s lavish production will feature musical accompanimen
 t from Tafelmusik Baroque Orchestra under the baton of David Fallis\, chor
 eography by Founding Co-Artistic Director Jeannette Lajeunesse Zingg C.M.\
 , performed by Artists of Atelier Ballet\, and an innovative\, multi-level
  set by Opera Atelier’s resident set designer Gerard Gauci. The all-star
  Canadian cast includes Soprano Carla Huhtanen\, Soprano Meghan Lindsay\, 
 Mezzo-Soprano Allyson McHardy\, Tenor Colin Ainsworth\, and Bass-Baritone 
 Douglas Williams. Opera Atelier presents Handel’s The Resurrection
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2023/03/210424_02180-copy.jpg
