URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/kashedance-presents-trilogy-of-bei
 ng/
SUMMARY:KasheDance Presents: Trilogy of BEing
DESCRIPTION:Citadel + Compagnie is thrilled to be hosting the presentation 
 of Kevin A. Ormsby’s Trilogy of BEing\, in association with KasheDance. 
 This triple bill runs April 13th – 15th at The Citadel: Ross Centre for 
 Dance.\n\nTrilogy of BEing is a creative collaboration between Canadian an
 d American choreographers — all of whom have worked or danced with Ormsb
 y throughout his career. The production is grounded in Black existence and
  experiences: environmental\, social\, and cultural\, and thematically fol
 lows three distinct varying stages of Ormsby’s life’s work.\n\nTrilogy
  of BEing is a series of three solos performed by Ormsby:\n\nUnmasked: Sea
 weed King – choreographed by Christopher Walker\nUnmasked: Seaweed King 
 depicts a sort of phoenix rising from the refuse / ashes\; addressing huma
 n impact on the environment told through a character of ancient wisdom lin
 king Afro-Caribbean mas performance traditions.\n\nSomebody – choreograp
 hed by Denise Fujiwara\nSomebody was inspired by Ormsby’s call to action
  in the wake of George Floyd’s murder. “I suggested a collaborative cr
 eative process that resulted in the solo for him.” Poetry by Giller Priz
 e-winning Canadian author Ian Williams\, Poet Laureate of Jamaica 2021-202
 4\, Olive Senior\, and Lambda Literary Award winner\, American Rosamund S.
  King shapes this solo\, rich in contemporary butoh technique.\n\n Dear 
 Brother – choreographed by Joel Valentin-Martinez*\nThrough visual resea
 rch of images and music of significant Black historical periods\, emerges 
 Dear Brother\, commenting on how we see contemporary Black and Brown lives
 \, by shaping music\, fashion and popular culture.\n\n*Dear Brother will b
 e performed as a solo on April 13 and 15\, and as a quartet (performed by 
 Will Brown\, Benjamin Russel\, and Kevin Shawn along with Ormsby) on April
  14. KasheDance Presents: Trilogy of BEing
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2023/04/FB-twitter.jpg
CATEGORIES:Contemporary
LOCATION:Citadel Ross Centre for Dance\, 304 Parliament St\, Toronto\, Onta
 rio\, M5A2Z6\, Canada
GEO:43.6591;-79.366
