URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/dance-in-public-space-residency-sh
 owcase/
SUMMARY:Dance in Public Space Residency Showcase
DESCRIPTION:Join The Bentway and our Dance in Public Space Artists-in-Resid
 ence on September 13 for an evening of participatory presentations where t
 hey will share insights and inspirations gained through their summer of on
 site research at The Bentway.\n\nTogether\, the artists and visitors will 
 explore new possibilities for dance\, movement\, and embodied practices in
  public spaces like The Bentway and beyond.\n\nThis summer\, The Bentway t
 eamed up with Toronto Dance Theatre on our 2023 Artist Residency and selec
 ted three artists to develop a research-based project to further their dan
 ce practice\, provide learning opportunities with local dance and public a
 rt practitioners\, and\, in turn\, contribute to re-imagining the possibil
 ities of The Bentway’s spaces. In June 2023\, we welcomed Resident Artis
 ts: Charlotte Carbone\, Saysah\, and Jessie Jakumeit.\n\nHow can street da
 nce floors be more inclusive spaces? How can movement in public space keep
  histories of the land alive in the face of change? What can we learn from
  animals and the way they navigate public spaces?\n\nWant to come but aren
 ’t sure if you want to participate in dancing or movement? That’s okay
 ! You are welcome to attend and observe. Dance in Public Space Residency S
 howcase
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2023/08/The-Bentway-Dance-in-Public-Space-Residency-Showcase-Photo-2.jpg
CATEGORIES:AfroCuban,Asian,Contemporary,LGBT,Other
LOCATION:The Bentway\, 250 Fort York Blvd\, Toronto\, Canada
GEO:43.6374082;-79.40664609999999
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=250 Fort York Blvd\, Toront
 o\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=The Bentway:geo:43.6374082,-79.40664
 609999999
END:VEVENT
