URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/dance-the-library-common-ground-da
 nce-festival-at-nycl/
SUMMARY:Dance @ the Library - Common Ground Dance Festival at NYCL
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy an afternoon of curious and thought-provoking dance perfo
 rmances at the library\, where dancers explore intimacy and art-making.\n\
 n\n\nCommon Ground Dance Festival produced by TOES FOR DANCE (@toesfordanc
 e) returns to North York\, Toronto from September 21-23 and includes an af
 ternoon of curious and thought-provoking performances at North York Centra
 l Library on September 23 between 1-4pm.\n\nCatch emerging artist Ellen Mo
 ore’s choreography titled 51\, 52\, 53 in the atrium\; a nuanced explora
 tion of intimacy. Then\, venture up to the 2nd floor auditorium to witness
  Tia Ashley Kushniruk (亚女弟) perform their bold and theatrical work-i
 n-progress titled The artist isn't present - a tour into the mind of Canad
 a's greatest non-existent artist.\n\nRSVP to receive event reminders. More
  info about all of CGDF’s free events in 2023\, including dance workshop
 s and additional performances at Lee Lifeson Art park\, at www.toesfordanc
 e.ca/common-ground.\n\nEvent is free and all are welcome. The schedule for
  the afternoon looks like this:\n\n1:00-1:20 - performance of 51\, 52\, 53
  in the atrium\n\n1:30-2:00 - performance of The Artist isn't Present in t
 he auditorium\n\n2:00-2:20 - performance of 51\, 52\, 53 in the atrium\n\n
 2:30-3:00 - performance of The Artist isn't Present in the auditorium\n\n3
 :00-3:20 - performance of 51\, 52\, 53 in the atrium\n\n3:30-4:00 - perfor
 mance of The Artist isn't Present in the auditorium\n\n\n Dance @ the Libr
 ary - Common Ground Dance Festival at NYCL
