URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/swing-101-with-hannah-bild-enkin-a
 nd-catherine-carriere/
SUMMARY:Swing 101 with Hannah Bild-Enkin and Catherine Carriere
DESCRIPTION:Learn some of the basics of Lindy Hop\, a partnered swing dance
  from the 1930s and 1940s. No prior dance experience necessary!\n\n\n\nEmb
 race the music and movement of the swing era in this Lindy Hop for beginne
 rs workshop! Learn some of the basics of Lindy Hop\, a partnered swing dan
 ce from the 1930s and 1940s. No dance experience necessary\, just bring yo
 urself\, some water\, some comfy shoes and join the fun!\n\nHannah Bild-En
 kin is a Lindy Hop and Vernacular Jazz social dancer\, performer\, choreog
 rapher\, and instructor based in Toronto. Originally training in tap\, bal
 let\, and figure skating\, Hannah fell in love with swing era dances in 20
 11. She enjoys the improvisational nature of jazz music and dancing\, and 
 continues to find inspiration in the relationship that music and dance hav
 e with each other. Hannah strives to encourage everyone to find the joy in
  dancing.\n\nFree to attend\, please register to secure your spot!\n\nThis
  workshop is part of Dance Together Festival York Region. It is free for p
 articipants\, thanks to the generous support of the Richmond Hill Communit
 y and Cultural Grant Program and in partnership with Assembly Park\, York 
 Region Arts Council\, City of Vaughan and Richmond Hill Public Library.\n\
 nPhoto by Mirna Chacin\n\n\n Swing 101 with Hannah Bild-Enkin and Catherin
 e Carriere
