SUMMARY:entre chien et loup
DESCRIPTION:CITADEL LIVE PRESENTS\nentre chien et loup\nChoreographed and P
 erformed by James Gnam\n\nentre chien et loup is an expression from old Fr
 ench commonly used to describe a time of day when the light is so dim you 
 can’t distinguish a dog from a wolf. Twilight\, dawn\, dusk. The gloamin
 g.\n\nIn this solo work\, Gnam embodies multiple layers of the “dog and 
 wolf” expression to expose his process of making a solo during a pandemi
 c.\n\nDetails: https://www.citadelcie.com/event/entre-chien-et-loup/ entre
  chien et loup
