URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/12th-annual-human-rights-film-fest
 ival-by-jayu-canada/
SUMMARY:12th Annual Human Rights Film Festival by JAYU Canada
DESCRIPTION:JAYU Canada is thrilled to announce its 12th annual Human Right
 s Film Festival+ 2023 (HRFF+). This year from December 7-10\, 2023\, HRFF+
  is excited to present 4 feature-length documentaries including 3 Toronto 
 premieres\, as well as accompanying Q&amp\;As\, and 4 short films.\n\nThe 
 festival will screen these films at Hot Docs alongside a moving gallery in
 stallation of We Grow Together\, in partnership with the White Owl Native 
 Ancestry Association and Wisahkotewinowak\, featuring the work of 6 Indige
 nous youth. On closing night\, HRFF + is proud to present its 4th annual J
 AYU Slams Poetry Competition featuring Eddie Lartey at the Ace Hotel.\n\nT
 his year HRFF + is pleased to share the following films:\n\nA Bullet Pulli
 ng Thread (December 7\, 2023): In January 2020\, the RCMP killed homelessn
 ess activist Barry Shantz at his home in Lytton\, B.C during a mental heal
 th crisis. In response to this tragedy\, his sister Marilyn creates a seri
 es of art quilts called Kairos – a Greek word which means ‘an opportun
 e time for action’. The film will be followed by a Q&amp\;A with directo
 r Ian Daffern and Marilyn Shantz.\n\nComing Around (December 8\, 2023\, To
 ronto Premiere): Coming Around follows 28-year-old Eman as she weighs the 
 decision to come out to her devout Muslim mother. The film will be followe
 d by a Q&amp\;A with Eman Abdelhadi and Sandra Itäinen.\n\nThe Space Race
  (December 9\, 2023\, Toronto Premiere): The Space Race weaves together th
 e stories of Black astronauts seeking to break the bonds of social injusti
 ce to reach for the stars\, including Guion Bluford\, Ed Dwight and Charle
 s Bolden\, among many others.\n\nHong Kong Mixtape (December 10\, 2023): U
 sing her own voice to guide us through this time\, filmmaker San San F You
 ng pieces together works by underground artists\, musicians\, dancers\, il
 lustrators and performance artists\, showcasing how art can provide some o
 f the most powerful forms of activism. The film will be followed by a Q&am
 p\;A with San San F Young and Nikki Parrott. 12th Annual Human Rights Film
  Festival by JAYU Canada
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2023/11/Screen-Shot-2023-11-21-at-10.22.03-PM.png
CATEGORIES:Contemporary
LOCATION:Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema\, 506 Bloor Street West\, Toronto\, Ont
 ario\, M5S 1Y3\, Canada
GEO:43.6654163;-79.41038530000003
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=506 Bloor Street West\, Tor
 onto\, Ontario\, M5S 1Y3\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Hot Docs Ted 
