URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/west-coast-swing-for-beginners-9/
SUMMARY:West Coast Swing for Beginners
DESCRIPTION:*** West Coast Swing Dance For Beginners ***\n\nIf you have eve
 r wanted to try West Coast Swing\, now is your chance with these fun class
 es designed for people with little or no experience with West Coast Swing\
 , or dancing in general.\n\nYou will learn the basic steps and patterns of
  West Coast Swing in a fun and friendly class environment.\n\n– No previ
 ous dance experience needed\n– No partner needed\n– Taught by Shelley 
 Saxena – one of Toronto’s top rated West Coast Swing instructors\n– 
 Comfortable dance studio in central location\n– Easy access by TTC\n- Fr
 ee parking right at dance studio\n– Fun and friendly class environment\n
 \nLEVEL: Beginner – for people brand new to West Coast Swing\n\nDANCE ST
 YLE: West Coast Swing\n\nWHEN: 4 Class Series – Every Thursday From Janu
 ary 4 to 25\, 2024\n\nClass is 7:15 - 8:15pm PLUS a bonus 30 minute practi
 ce 8:15 - 8:45pm. The complete series of four classes is $95.\n\nWHERE: Go
 tta Dance Studio\, 3581 Dundas St. West\, Toronto (at the corner of Jane a
 nd Dundas)\n\nWHAT TO DO NEXT: Please note class size is limited and fills
  up quickly so register early to have your spot guaranteed.\n\nTo register
  and confirm your spot in class\, click the “More Info” tab at the top
  of this listing\, or visit https://shelleydance.com\n\n*** FREQUENTLY ASK
 ED QUESTIONS ***\n\nQ. Do I need any previous dance experience?\n\nAbsolut
 ely not! The Level 1 Beginner class is perfect for you. You can learn West
  Coast Swing in three easy steps\, even if you have never danced before an
 d have two left feet.\n\nQ. Do I need to come with a partner?\n\nNo\, you 
 do NOT need a partner for the class. If you have someone you would like to
  learn with\, that is fantastic. But you do not need a partner to take the
  class. The class is structured so you rotate with different partners thro
 ughout the class. It’s a great way to meet new people and you also get t
 o dance with a variety of leads and follows.\n\nQ. What type of shoes shou
 ld I wear?\n\nIf you already have dance shoes\, then bring those. If you d
 on’t have dance shoes\, then something with a leather or suede sole is b
 est. If not\, then just wear your most comfortable pair of shoes.\n\nQ. Wh
 at type of clothes should I wear to class?\n\nWear whatever you will feel 
 most comfortable in. West Coast Swing is a very casual dance so wear your 
 favorite jeans and t-shirt if you want.\n\nQ. Who is the instructor?\n\nYo
 ur instructor is Shelley Saxena. Shelley has been dancing\, studying and c
 ompeting in West Coast Swing for 23 years. With an extensive background in
  Jazz\, Ballet and Modern dance\, Shelley now specializes in West Coast Sw
 ing. You can contact Shelley at https://shelleydance.com\n\nQ. Where can I
  practice what I’ve learned?\n\nThere is a bonus 30 minute practice righ
 t after class from 8:15 - 8:45pm.\n\nQ. I still have a question about the 
 class or West Coast Swing. Can you help?\n\nOf course! If you have any oth
 er questions\, please don’t hesitate to contact Shelley by clicking the 
 “More Info” tab at the top of this listing\, or visiting her website S
 helleyDance.com. She will be very happy to help you any way she can.\n\nQ.
  I’m excited to get started! What’s my next step?\n\nSimply click the 
 “More Info” tab at the top of this listing to let Shelley know you’d
  like to register\, or visit her website https://shelleydance.com (class s
 ize is limited so it’s important to make sure you reserve your spot).\n\
 nEvent Type: Dance Class (4 Week Series)\n\n&nbsp\; West Coast Swing for B
 eginners
