SUMMARY:Adult Tap Classes
DESCRIPTION:TAP CLASSES\n\n6 Week Session beginning Tuesday\, January 16 20
 24 with 2 levels to choose from - Continuing Beginner and Intermediate.\n\
 nA great chance to learn and practice in a fun\, supportive environment.\n
 \nDates: Tuesdays - January 16- February 20\, 2024\nIntermediate - 6-7:15p
 m\nContinuing Beginner - 7:20-8:30pm\n\nLocation: Winchester Street Theatr
 e - 80 Winchester St\n\nCost: $130 payable by e-transfer - Includes practi
 ce videos to work on between classes.\n\nPlease contact allisonplamondon@
 gmail.com for more info and to register.\n\nA bit about Allison -\nAlliso
 n Plamondon is a choreographer\, director\, performer\, and teacher origin
 ally from Edmonton. Canadian choreography highlights include Irving Berlin
 ’s White Christmas\, Damn Yankees\, and Holiday Inn all for the Shaw Fes
 tival. Most recently\, Allison choreographed Grease for Western Canada The
 atre and participated in the National Ballet of Canada’s Open Space prog
 ram. As a performer\, Allison has been onstage at some of North America’
 s most exciting venues including Madison Square Garden\, La MaMa\, Symphon
 y Space\, the Charlottetown Festival\, and the National Arts Centre.\nAn a
 vid teacher\, Allison is passionate about sharing movement with dancers of
  all ages and abilities. New York teaching highlights include AMDA\, Queen
 s Theater\, Tom Todoroff Conservatory\, Abrons Arts Center and Broadway Da
 nce Center. Allison completed the Uta Hagen Teacher Training at HB Studio 
 in 2016 and is a certified GYROTONIC® and GYROKINESIS® Trainer. Allison 
 currently teaches tap in the Musical Theatre program at Sheridan College. 
 Adult Tap Classes
