SUMMARY:Introduction to English Country Dance
DESCRIPTION:A free introduction to English Country Dancing. Please register
  at info@tecda.ca.\nJoin us for one\, two\, or three classes as you wish.\
 n\n\n\nA free dance to introduce you to English Country Dancing. Please re
 gister to attend by e-mail to info@tecda.ca.\n\nMondays January 29\, Febru
 ary 26\, March 25 (2004)\, from 7:00 to 9:00 PM. Not a progressive class -
 - join us for one\, two\, or three Mondays as you wish.\n\nSecond-floor au
 ditorium\, Ralph Thornton Centre\, 765 Queen Street East\, Toronto.\n\nEng
 lish Country Dance began as a combination of formal court dance and folk d
 ance circa 1600. It travelled from England to continental Europe and even 
 to North America in colonial times. The dance form was revived in the earl
 y 1900s and new dances are written to this day. This sampler will teach a 
 few basic steps and include a variety of approachable dances to give you a
 n idea of how ECD works.\n\nNo partner required. No lead or follow roles. 
 Wear flat\, soft-soled shoes and comfortable clothes.\n\nMask optional. Sc
 ent free.\n\nRegistration mandatory by e-mail to info@tecda.ca.\n\nToronto
  English Country Dance Assembly http://www.tecda.ca\n\n\n Introduction to 
 English Country Dance
