URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/opera-atelier-presents-all-is-love
 -2/
SUMMARY:Opera Atelier presents All Is Love
DESCRIPTION:Opera Atelier is delighted to announce the triumphant return of
  ALL IS LOVE\, a fully staged mixed program celebrating love in all its sp
 lendor at Koerner Hall\, TELUS Centre for Performance and Learning\, graci
 ng the stage from April 11 to April 14\, 2024.\n\nFeaturing a rich selecti
 on of beloved musical pieces cherished by Opera Atelier\, including works 
 by J.P. Rameau\, M.A. Charpentier\, and Renaldo Hahn\, alongside excerpts 
 from Henry Purcell\, Matthew Locke\, and G.F. Handel\, the production is f
 urther elevated by the mesmerizing performances of the full corps of Artis
 ts of Atelier Ballet.\n\nBreaking new ground\, the company presents Act 1 
 of Debussy’s operatic masterpiece Pelléas et Mélisande\, rendered with
  authentic 19th-century period instruments by the esteemed musicians of Ta
 felmusik.\n\nALL IS LOVE stars Opera Atelier audience favorites such as so
 prano Measha Brueggergosman-Lee\, tenor Colin Ainsworth\, soprano Karine W
 hite\, soprano Meghan Lindsay\, mezzo-soprano Danielle MacMillan\, soprano
  Cynthia Smithers\, bass-baritone Douglas Williams\, baritone Jesse Blumbe
 rg\, alongside the renowned Tafelmusik under the baton of Opera Atelier Mu
 sic Director David Fallis. Opera Atelier presents All Is Love
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2024/03/all-is-love.png
CATEGORIES:Contemporary
END:VEVENT
