URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/harbourfront-centre-celebrates-50-
 years-of-arts-culture-and-unity/
SUMMARY:Harbourfront Centre Celebrates 50 Years of Arts\, Culture and Unity
DESCRIPTION:&nbsp\;\n\nHarbourfront Centre Celebrates 50 Years of Arts\, Cu
 lture and Unity with an Exciting Summer Lineup of Anniversary Events and L
 ong Weekend Festivals\n\nHarbourfront Centre announces the 2024 summer pro
 gramming lineup to celebrate its landmark 50th anniversary with a mix of t
 icketed\, free and pay-what-you-wish events.\n\nHighlights of free summer 
 programming include:\n\n 	June 1: Block Party – Neighbours and friends a
 re invited to join us for a live performance by Canadian alternative count
 ry band Elliott Brood\, a chance to sing on stage with Good Enough Live Ka
 raoke band\, participate in a free social line dancing class\, enjoy famil
 y-friendly activities and delicious street food\, drinks and a birthday ca
 ke (of course)!\n 	Tuesdays\, June 25 – August 27: Free Flicks – One o
 f the city’s favourite summer traditions returns with ten free outdoor f
 ilm screenings at the Concert Stage every Tuesday all summer\, showing pop
 ular films and old-school classics.\n 	Wednesdays\, July 10 – August 28:
  Dancing on the Square – Enjoy live dance at the new Public Square with 
 an eclectic lineup of Latin\, Bollywood\, hip-hop and contemporary dance.\
 n 	Thursdays and Sundays\, June 21 – August 27: Summer Music in the Gard
 en – 18 free concerts at the Toronto Music Garden\, including the Nation
 al Youth Orchestra of Canada\, Moneka Arabic Jazz and Nichol Robertson’s
  Country All-Stars.\n 	June 28–July 1: Canada Day Long Weekend – Celeb
 rate on the waterfront with Harbourfront Centre’s July long weekend line
 up of free and ticketed programming in music\, dance\, comedy\, food and f
 amily-friendly activities for all ages.\n 	June 28: Fefe Dobson and Tyler 
 Shaw (pay-what-you-wish)\n 	June 29: Choir! Choir! Choir! (ticketed)\n 	Ju
 ne 30: Martha Chaves (free) and the Toronto Symphony Orchestra (free)\n 	J
 uly 1: Crystal Shawanda (free)\n 	August 1–5: Island Soul Festival – I
 nspired by the many different flavours of the islands\, the 26th edition o
 f Island Soul celebrates the vibrant people and culture of the Caribbean t
 hrough a unique blend of music\, film\, food\, comedy\, multidisciplinary 
 arts and cultural activities.\n 	August 1: Comedy Night with Trixx and Fri
 ends (ticketed)\n 	August 2: Destra and DJ Power (ticketed)\n 	August 3: J
 ohnny Osbourne (free) and The Clash! (free)\n 	August 4: Sean Jones’ Sum
 mer Soul (ticketed)\, Etana (free) and Jay Douglas (free)\n\nAlso returnin
 g this summer are the adored multicultural festivals\, Habari Africa\, TAI
 WANfest\, Toronto International Tap Dance Festival and Fun Philippines Tor
 onto Food &amp\; Music Festival\, promising a rich exploration of culture.
 \n\nTo learn more about summer programming and purchase tickets\, please v
 isit HarbourfrontCentre.com/summer.\n\nLocation: 235 Queens Quay West Toro
 nto\, ON\n\nMedia Contact:\nAlyssa Bomben Tomczak\, Senior Consultant\naly
 ssa.bomben@mediaprofile.com\n905-865-2177\n\nHarbourfront Centre Contact:\
 nSam Caldicott\, Senior Marketing Manager\nscaldicott@harbourfrontcentre.c
 om Harbourfront Centre Celebrates 50 Years of Arts\, Culture and Unity
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2024/05/Harbourfront-at-50.png
LOCATION:** If your location is not here please add it to Details\, 1 yonge
  street\, Toronto\, Canada
