URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/creative-movement-for-non-dancers-
 w-natalia-waterfront-wednesdays/
SUMMARY:Creative Movement for non-dancers w/ Natalia | Waterfront Wednesday
 s
DESCRIPTION:Waterfront Wednesdays with Art and Water is an exciting initiat
 ive aimed at bringing together dance\, water\, and community.\n\n\n\nWorks
 hop name: Creative Movement for non-dancers w/Natalia Arancibia\n\nWorksho
 p level: non-dancers/beginner\n\nWhat to Bring: Please note this event is 
 OUTDOORS and happens on our floating dock. Please prepare for the weather.
  Check our instagram for weather cancellations\; which will be posted by 4
 pm the day of the event.\n\nWaterfront Wednesdays with Art and Water: Wate
 rfront Wednesdays with Art and Water is an exciting initiative aimed at br
 inging together dance\, water\, and community on Toronto's beautiful water
 front. Led by multiple dance artists from varying styles and backgrounds\,
  our free two-hour workshops every Wednesday from May 29th to June 26\, 20
 24 offer a unique experience for all participants.\n\n&nbsp\;\n\n**please 
 only reserve tickets for this event if you are certain you are able to att
 end. There are a limited number of tickets/space available. Thank you.**\n
 \n&nbsp\;\n\nCheck out the full calendar of events here: www.art-water.ca/
 waterfront-wednesdays\n\nNatalia Arancibia on instagram: @adultajoven\n\nA
 rt &amp\; Water on instagram: @artwatercultura\n\n&nbsp\;\n\nAbout this wo
 rkshop:\n\n"My name is Natalia Arancibia\, I’m an independent artist fro
 m Chile and I moved to Toronto in May 2023\; during my time in the city I
 ’ve been able to connect with amazing artists that have inspired me trem
 endously in this fast paced year. My practice is mostly whitin the realm o
 f contemporary “technique” this going from floor work to full improvis
 ation. I would like to offer a creative movement practice for non dancers\
 ; Ihave had the chance to offer movement classes for non dancers before\, 
 where we worked basing the class on drills related to coordination\, rhyth
 m and flow\; all this with the objective to generate a very calm and non i
 ntimidating approach to movement for people who are simply not used nor aw
 are of the possibilities and capabilities of their bodies. I think regardi
 ng the space\, it’s a good invitation for the participants to reunite in
  a communal atmosphere that happens very naturally in the place where the 
 dock is located."\n\n&nbsp\;\n\n&nbsp\;\n\n\n\n Creative Movement for non-
 dancers w/ Natalia | Waterfront Wednesdays
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2024/05/27958_image.png
CATEGORIES:Therapeutic
LOCATION:585 Queens Quay W\, 585 Queens Quay West\, Toronto\, ON M5V 3G3\, 
 Toronto\, ON\, M5V 3G3\, Canada
GEO:43.6364;-79.3971
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=585 Queens Quay West\, Toro
 nto\, ON M5V 3G3\, Toronto\, ON\, M5V 3G3\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TI
 TLE=585 Queens Quay W:geo:43.6364,-79.3971
END:VEVENT
