 n-dance-camp/
SUMMARY:Community Connects: Kelewele African Dance Camp
DESCRIPTION:This is a free\, in-person African dance workshop for youth and
  adults.\n\n\n\nThe Community Connects series strengthens the links betwee
 n members of the diverse multi-disciplinary Brampton creative community wh
 ile fostering communal learning and knowledge sharing as well as developin
 g individual members' facilitation skills. We are empowering Brampton arti
 sts and creatives to craft programming specifically for our community.\n\n
 &nbsp\;\n\nIn collaboration with Doggpound and Kaizen Dance Initiative joi
 n Faith Sodipo\, Martin "Prempz" Prempeh and Kwasi Obeng-Adjei for a free 
 African Dance workshops for youth and adults.\n\nYou will learn from knowl
 edgeable and working professional instructors various African dance forms 
 including the style of Azonto\, Pantsula\, Naija Fusion\, Afrofusion\, and
  Traditional West African.\n\nThe purpose of this project is to push the A
 frican narrative in the Peel region\, creating opportunities for people wh
 ether young or old\, beginners and or experience to learn and grow in the 
 art form. Come and join Bramptons dance community!\n\nClass 1: Naija (Nige
 rian) Fusion\n\nClass 2: Azonto (dance and musical genre from Ghana)\n\n&n
 bsp\;\n\nAccessibility: If you need assistance or support to participate s
 uch as an ASL interpreter\, please get in touch with us at info@bramptonar
 tsorg.ca as soon as possible (minimum of three days in advance) so that we
  can make the necessary accommodations.\n\n&nbsp\;\n\nTransportation: We c
 an provide all-ages Brampton Transit Tickets free of charge to those who n
 eed them for all BAO in-person events. If you would like to pick up a tick
 et for yourself and others attending with you\, please email info@brampton
 artsorg.ca prior to the event and we will have them available for you onsi
 te. Tickets work for both Brampton Transit and Züm buses.\n\n&nbsp\;\n\n\
 n\nWORKSHOP PRESENTERS:\n\n\n\n\nFaith Sodipo aka @Yhemyzy_ is a Nigerian 
 born artist and has been active in the entertainment industry as a dancer\
 , performer and teacher for 7+ years. She has worked with A-list stars tha
 t include Seyi Shay\, Joeboy\, Cardi B and many more.Faith is Presently te
 aching at DanceklifeX in Toronto as an afro dance instructor\n\n&nbsp\;\n\
 n\n\n\n\nBorn in Kumasi\, Ghana\, Martin "Prempz" Prempeh is Toronto’s m
 ost notable dancer and choreographer. Dancing is something he lives\, brea
 thes and loves to do and has high hopes in becoming more successful. With 
 the ability to move his waist in different directions and his non-stop fli
 ps\, he never fails to grasp an audience's attention.\n\n\n\n\n\nKwasi Obe
 ng-Adjei is a Canadian multidisciplinary artist\, emerging choreographer a
 nd dance educator based in Brampton Ontario. Acceptance into the regional 
 arts program at St Roch Catholic Secondary School is where he began his jo
 urney and developed his foundation. Training with Leading Artistic directo
 rs and choreographers that include the likes of Esie Mensah\, and Lua Shay
 enne to name a few\, have led to opportunity that include Pan-American Gam
 es\, Kira\, The Path | La Voie\, The Raptors half-time show\, Zayo and mor
 e. Kwasi believes dance is a spiritual experience that involves connecting
  all that are among us.\n\n\n Community Connects: Kelewele African Dance C
 amp
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2024/06/28017_image.png
CATEGORIES:African,Azonto
LOCATION:DoggPound MMA\, 40 B Hansen Road South\, Brampton\, ON L6W 3H4\, B
 rampton\, ON\, L6W 3H4\, Canada
GEO:43.695591;-79.739356
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=40 B Hansen Road South\, Br
