SUMMARY:13th Annual Afro-Carib Fest
DESCRIPTION:A free 2-day annual festival that celebrates the diverse cultur
 es of African and Caribbean communities through music\, dance\, and food.\
 n\n\n\nAfro-Carib Fest is an award-winning FREE 2-day outdoor festival tha
 t celebrates diversity by showcasing the arts\, culture and heritage of th
 e Afro-Caribbean diaspora to over 30\,000 attendees. Audiences will be eng
 aged through 30 live performances from 80+ local artists\, over 80 vendors
 \, a cultural parade\, a kid’s zone\, dance competitions with cash prize
 s\, drum circles\, raffle draws with prizes\, and much more.\n\n&nbsp\;\n\
 nAfro-Carib Fest invites people of all backgrounds to share in cultural pr
 esentations\, artistic performances\, learning\, and networking opportunit
 ies. The event will take place on August 24th and August 25th\, 2023 from 
 12 pm to 9 pm at Thomson Memorial Park\, Scarborough.\n\n\n\n 13th Annual 
 Afro-Carib Fest
