URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/idpwd-therapeutic-dance-a-fusion-o
 f-cultures/
SUMMARY:IDPWD – Therapeutic Dance: A Fusion of Cultures
DESCRIPTION:Join Ishaa during the International Day of Disabilities to expl
 ore various dance styles\, such as Latin dance rhythms in a ‘Zumba’ st
 yle.\n\n\n\nThrough Cultural Dance Movement and Therapy (Indian and Latin 
 styles)\, dance therapy will be explored for the purpose and joy of pursui
 ng a hobby instead of merely replicating choreography. There will be an em
 phasis on using ‘somatic’ awareness\, where the movements are intrinsi
 cally motivated and come from a space of being present in the moment.\n\nJ
 oin Ishaa during the International Day of Disabilities to explore various 
 dance styles\, such as Latin dance rhythms in a ‘Zumba’ style\, and ex
 plore beats. Dance styles will include Salsa\, Bachata\, and Kizomba. Folk
  Dances of India\, such as the North Indian Bhangra (From the state of Pun
 jab)\, Ghoomar (Rajasthan)\, and Gujarati folk music\, will also be utiliz
 ed. We will be using a combination of Bollywood and Pop Music for the clas
 ses.\n\n&nbsp\;\nEvent Details\n\n 	Date: Tuesday\, December 3\, 2024\n 	T
 ime: 4 pm to 5 pm\n 	Location: Join Virtually Zoom\n 	In-Person Waterfront
  Campus (51 Dockside Drive)\n\nFor registration assistance or accessibilit
 y accommodation\, please contact Sarah Gillard sgillard@georgebrown.ca\n\n
 \n\n\nIshaa (she/her) holds a degree in Performing Arts in the North India
 n Classical Dance form of Kathak. She is also a trained Latin dancer and h
 as previously participated in national-level dance competitions. She has a
 lso performed in India\, Germany\, Spain\, and Canada. After moving to Tor
 onto\, her focus as an artist shifted from that of a Dancer to an Early Ch
 ildhood Educator/Mental Health Advocate and Author (Memoir titled #Finding
 OrderinDisorder).\n\nShe finds that utilizing her dance form served as a c
 atharsis in the form of Dance Movement and Therapy. It took her into a pea
 ceful state of mind\, and this is exactly what she desires to share with t
 he community.\n\n&nbsp\;\n\n\n IDPWD – Therapeutic Dance: A Fusion of Cu
 ltures
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2024/11/28447_image.jpg
CATEGORIES:Latin,Therapeutic,Zumba
LOCATION:George Brown College - Waterfront Campus\, 51 Dockside Drive\, Tor
 onto\, ON M5A 1B6\, Toronto\, ON\, M5A 1B6\, Canada
GEO:43.643977;-79.365466
