URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/english-country-dance-live-music-b
 eginner-lesson-2/
SUMMARY:English Country Dance - Live Music + Beginner Lesson
DESCRIPTION:Dance like a Bridgerton\, or the folks from Jane Austen movies:
  experience the joy of a dance form that has lasted the ages. This is what
  all the cool kids did in the 1600s-1800s - it's surprisingly fun!\n\nEngl
 ish Country Dance is an interactive\, social form of dance. The dance uses
  gender-free instructions\, and is very accessible: if you can walk\, you 
 can dance ECD.\n\nLive Music provided by Pat Mearns and Elena Spanu\, with
  calling and instruction by Toronto's own Cathy Campbell.\n\nFirst Time?\n
 We are delighted to offer your first dance for free (a $25 value.) Here’
 s what you need to do to take advantage of this:\n\n1. Arrive between 1:15
 -1:30\, so you are ready to dance.\n2. Add yourself to our email list.\n3.
  Attend our half hour beginner lesson\, from 1:30-2:00\, which will set yo
 u up for dancing success!\n\nIt is challenging for other dancers and our c
 aller to incorporate new dancers after the beginner session starts\, so we
  are unable to extend our first dance free offer after 1:30pm. Plan ahead\
 , arrive early!\n\nThen\, from 2-5pm\, we will be joined by the rest of th
 e TECDA dancers\, and dance a selection of accessible dances from across t
 he centuries\, from energetic and exuberant to gentle and heartwarming. We
 'll dance dances that were wildly popular in the 1700s all the way through
  to today’s beautiful creations.\n\nNo partner needed\, each dance is ty
 pically danced with someone different. If you are a beginner\, our more ex
 perienced dancers are always happy to partner with you to help you as you 
 learn. Bring clean indoor shoes and comfortable\, casual clothing (we only
  dress up in Regency clothing a couple times a year.)\n\nWe Dance Often!\n
 If you enjoy the dance form\, it's easy to make English Country Dance a vi
 brant part of your schedule!\n\nTECDA dances twice a week: Tuesdays in Nor
 th York at Willowdale Presbyterian\, and Fridays at the Ralph Thornton Cen
 tre\, near Queen &amp\; Broadview\, all by sliding scale/donation. We have
  live music twice a month\, including a special monthly dance\, usually he
 ld at St. Barnabas Hall.\n\nEnglish Country Dance is an accessible way to 
 get some exercise for both the body and the mind\, and it's a very warm an
 d welcoming group. Come join us for a dance! English Country Dance - Live 
 Music + Beginner Lesson
