URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/english-country-dance-live-music-b
 eginner-lesson/
SUMMARY:English Country Dance - Live Music + Beginner Lesson
DESCRIPTION:Dance like a Bridgerton\, or the folks from Jane Austen movies:
  experience the joy of a dance form that has lasted the ages. This is what
  all the cool kids did in the 1600s-1800s - it's surprisingly fun!\n\nEngl
 ish Country Dance is an interactive\, social form of dance. The dance uses
  gender-free instructions\, and is very accessible: if you can walk\, you 
 can dance ECD.\n\nOur February dance features live music provided by Susan
 ne Maziarz and Daev Clysdale\, with calling and instruction by Toronto's o
 wn Alan Rosenthal.\n\nFirst Time?\nWe are delighted to offer your first da
 nce for free (a $25 value.) Here’s what you need to do to take advantage
  of this:\n\n1. Arrive between 1:15-1:30\, so you are ready to dance.\n2. 
 Add yourself to our email list.\n3. Attend our half hour beginner lesson\,
  from 1:30-2:00\, which will set you up for dancing success!\n\nIt is chal
 lenging for other dancers and our caller to incorporate new dancers after 
 the beginner session starts\, so we are unable to extend our first dance f
 ree offer after 1:30pm. Plan ahead\, arrive early!\n\nThen\, from 2-5pm\, 
 we will be joined by the rest of the TECDA dancers\, and dance a selection
  of accessible dances from across the centuries\, from energetic and exube
 rant to gentle and heartwarming. We'll dance dances that were wildly popul
 ar in the 1700s all the way through to today’s beautiful creations.\n\nN
 o partner needed\, each dance is typically danced with someone different. 
 If you are a beginner\, our more experienced dancers are always happy to p
 artner with you to help you as you learn. Bring clean indoor shoes and com
 fortable\, casual clothing (we only dress up in Regency clothing a couple 
 times a year.)\n\nWe Dance Often!\nIf you enjoy the dance form\, it's easy
  to make English Country Dance a vibrant part of your schedule!\n\nTECDA d
 ances twice a week: Tuesdays in North York at Willowdale Presbyterian\, an
 d Fridays at the Ralph Thornton Centre\, near Queen &amp\; Broadview\, all
  by sliding scale/donation. We have live music twice a month\, including a
  special monthly dance\, usually held at St. Barnabas Hall.\n\nEnglish Cou
 ntry Dance is an accessible way to get some exercise for both the body and
  the mind\, and it's a very warm and welcoming group. Come join us for a d
 ance! English Country Dance - Live Music + Beginner Lesson
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2025/01/ECDbeige-1.jpg
CATEGORIES:English Country Dance
LOCATION:St. Barnabas Hall\, 175 Hampton Avenue\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M4K2Z
 3\, Greektown\, Canada
GEO:43.6770833;-79.35219259999997
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=175 Hampton Avenue\, Toront
