UID:4357@torontodance.com
DTSTART:20250211T183000Z
DTEND:20250211T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20250105T031439Z
URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/afrorhythms-african-dance-percussi
 on/
SUMMARY:AfroRhythms - African dance & percussion
DESCRIPTION:Danse et percussions avec le Griot &amp\; Master Drummer Amadou
  kienou / Dance and percussion with Griot &amp\; Master Drummer Amadou kie
 nou\n\n\n\nAMADOU KIENOU\n\nMaster drummer Amadou Kienou hails from Ouagad
 ougou\, Burkina Faso\, West Africa\, once part of the vast ancient Manding
 o Empire. A descendant of the Dafin people\, Amadou was initiated as a dje
 li or griot (an oral historian)\, one of a long line of griots whose role 
 is to preserve and transmit their people’s history\, culture\, and value
 s.Nowadays\, bringing the traditional to the contemporary\, Amadou delight
 s international audiences with his unique polyrhythmic expression of emoti
 ons and memories.The djembe is Amadou’s principal instrument. As he desc
 ribes it\, “the djembe is more than a musical instrument\; it is an exte
 nsion of the musician through which he expresses his life\, his emotions.
 ” Mastery of the djembe requires a lifetime of discipline and dedication
 \, and the guidance of a djembe master\, provided\, in Amadou’s case\, p
 rimarily by his father\, the late revered Baba Kienou. Amadou plays severa
 l other traditional African instruments – the dunduns\, the n’goni\, a
 nd the tama\, not to mention the Western guitar and drum set.\n\n\n\n\n Af
 roRhythms - African dance &amp\; percussion
