DTSTART:20250215T140000Z
DTEND:20250215T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20250123T204153Z
URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/kuumba-365-masterclass-syreeta-hec
 tor/
SUMMARY:KUUMBA 365 Masterclass: Syreeta Hector
DESCRIPTION:Join Syreeta Hector for a movement session that invites partici
 pants to explore the intersection of identity\, race\, and classical balle
 t.\n\n\n\nJoin Syreeta Hector for a movement session that invites particip
 ants of all levels to explore the intersection of identity\, race\, and cl
 assical ballet. Emphasizing comfort and openness\, this workshop offers an
  opportunity to connect through dance\, moving with intention and expressi
 on. Syreeta brings her expertise as a teacher and performer\, offering a s
 pace to engage with movement in a supportive and creative environment.\n\n
 As part of KUUMBA 365: Second Edition\, Syreeta Hector has created a dance
  piece in response to Charles Campbell’s How many colours has the sea at
  The Power Plant. Inspired by Campbell’s profound exploration of the Mid
 dle Passage\, colonial legacies\, and collective healing\, Syreeta’s mov
 ement language reflects the intricate layers of identity\, memory\, and re
 silience. Her work channels the emotional depth and spiritual weight of th
 e exhibition\, using dance to evoke a sense of connection\, loss\, and the
  ongoing journey towards reclamation. Syreeta's performance will be presen
 ted at the Harbourfront Centre Theatre on February 1\, 2025.\n\nArtist's b
 io: Syreeta Hector is a dance artist and educator in Toronto\, Ontario. As
  a highly accomplished performer\, Syreeta has worked for internationally 
 recognized companies like Adelheid Dance Projects\, Danny Grossman Dance C
 ompany\, Peggy Baker Dance Projects\, Political Movement\, and Toronto Dan
 ce Theatre. She is a proud graduate of The National Ballet School’s Teac
 her Training Program\, The School of Toronto Dance Theatre. She has achiev
 ed her Master of Arts in Dance Studies from York University.\n\nHer work\,
  “Black Ballerina\,” focuses on the dualities within one's identity\, 
 along with Syreeta’s blackness and indigeneity in relation to classical 
 ballet. This short work-in-progress solo gained recognition at the Summer 
 Works Festival in 2019 and won the Stratford Festival Lab Award for Resear
 ch and Creation. In 2019\, “Black Ballerina” was nominated for a Dora 
 Mavor Moore Award and is currently being performed internationally.\n\nShe
  is an Assistant Professor in the Theatre\, Dance\, and Performance Depart
 ment at York University.\n\n\n KUUMBA 365 Masterclass: Syreeta Hector
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2025/01/28606_image.jpg
CATEGORIES:Ballet
LOCATION:The Power Plant Contemporary Art Gallery\, 231 Queens Quay West\, 
 Toronto\, ON M5J 2G8\, Toronto\, ON\, M5J 2G8\, Canada
GEO:43.638679;-79.382161
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=231 Queens Quay West\, Toro
 nto\, ON M5J 2G8\, Toronto\, ON\, M5J 2G8\, Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TI
 TLE=The Power Plant Contemporary Art Gallery:geo:43.638679,-79.382161
END:VEVENT
