URL:https://www.torontodance.com/events/the-pool-by-aisha-sasha-john/
SUMMARY:The Pool by Aisha Sasha John
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Dance Theatre is proud to present The Pool\, a new proj
 ect led by choreographer and poet Aisha Sasha John\, with a premiere perfo
 rmance on March 1\, followed by three performances March 6-8\, 2025 at Win
 chester Street Theatre. The Pool is the culmination of Aisha's time with t
 he company as the inaugural TDT Affiliate Artist (2023-25)\, created in co
 llaboration with the current TDT ensemble.\n\nThe Pool\, fundamentally\, i
 s a work about the power\, patterns\, and poetry of being together. Althou
 gh being-together may be a common theme for group dance work\, The Pool ta
 kes very seriously what those terms of togetherness are and could be. The 
 Pool documents a commitment not to betray our hearts\, with the understand
 ing that the heart is both collective field and personal compass.\n\nChore
 ographed by Aisha Sasha John\, The Pool will feature the current TDT ensem
 ble Camil Bellefleur\, Brayden Cairns\, Millina Fletcher\, Megumi Kokuba\,
  Ryan Kostyniuk\, Roberto Soria\, and Elizabeth Yip. The Pool by Aisha Sas
 ha John
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.torontodance.com/wp-content/uploads/
 2025/02/Camil-Bellefleur-Roberto-Soria-for-The-Pool-by-Aisha-Sasha-John.-P
 hoto-by-Fran-Chudnoff.jpg
